	quest.000E9F2ECF5432D5.quest_desc: [
		"With the Crushing Wheel, you can turn cobblestone into gravel and sand in bulk."
		""
		"Washing gravel, red sand, and soul sand yields iron, gold, and quartz."
	]
	quest.000E9F2ECF5432D5.title: "Mass-Producing Minerals"
	quest.004EAF9EE2AEAA4E.quest_desc: [
		"Villagers sell Dripstone Blocks."
	]
	quest.004EAF9EE2AEAA4E.title: "Villager Trading"
	quest.00C23897B3EEAEFD.quest_desc: [
		"These special stones often generate in huge amounts underground; crushing them yields the corresponding ore."
		""
		"Use a Prospector Pickaxe to locate them quickly."
	]
	quest.00C23897B3EEAEFD.title: "Massive Ore Veins"
	quest.00CE1F4328EC11AB.quest_desc: [
		"Conveyor belts are a simple, easy-to-use way to transport items — and they can carry rotation too. You'll definitely want plenty of them later, so if you can, mass-produce their raw material: kelp."
		""
		"No kelp? No problem — there are other ways to get conveyor belts. Check JEI&7 (EMI)&r! &7(Hint: Mechanical Pressing)"
		""
		"&aTips&r: An Item Drain can double as a conveyor belt, and it doesn't even need stress!"
		""
		"You can also use containers &7(especially large chests and item safes)&r with funnels to move items short distances — very handy."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Of course, the Item Drain has its downsides compared to a conveyor belt: it's expensive, and you can't take items straight off it."
		""
		"Anyway, just make some conveyor belts oao."
		""
		"&aPS&r: I only added the extra recipe in case you can't find kelp — it probably won't work in other modpacks."
	]
	quest.00CE1F4328EC11AB.title: "3.2 Kelp Logistics"
	quest.0189212CF2483E93.quest_desc: [
		"These ingredients are a good example of drops you can only get by finishing off mobs with a &eKnife&r or &eKitchen Knife&r — these come from pigs and endermites."
		""
		"Kaleidoscope and Farmer's Delight knives are basically interchangeable, so pick whichever feels best."
		""
		"&7Actually, the drop only requires the killing blow to come from a knife — you can use a normal sword the rest of the time."
	]
	quest.0189212CF2483E93.title: "F4.3 Special Ingredients"
	quest.01A72753873DD8DE.quest_desc: [
		"Both dynamic structures require Deployers to replant saplings"
	]
	quest.01A72753873DD8DE.title: "H2.5 Necessary Deployer"
	quest.01AE879008D8F755.quest_desc: [
		"Exercise your logistics wiring skills."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Quick jump\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"175C11A7E58931AE\"}}"
	]
	quest.01AE879008D8F755.title: "H2.6.1 Mass-Producing Coal Fuel"
	quest.01C34E2A1F16EBF8.quest_desc: [
		"Press &eE&r to open the backpack. On the right is the item manager, and below it is the &esearch bar&7 (supports Chinese, English, Pinyin, and Pinyin initials)&r."
		""
		"Hover over any &eitem&7 (in your backpack or the item manager)&r you're curious about, then press &eU&r to see its uses or &eR&r to see how to get it."
	]
	quest.01C34E2A1F16EBF8.title: "Mom No Longer Has to Worry About Me Forgetting Recipes!"
	quest.01D2AFDC5E35C0B6.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have wood, it's time to go mining — bringing these along will help a lot."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Ladder &7(and scaffolding)&r climbing speed has been massively buffed, so stop hating on it."
	]
	quest.01D2AFDC5E35C0B6.title: "1.2 Stone Age"
	quest.0234D5EF778A3227.quest_desc: [
		"Use the Minecart Assembly Station to mount a Deployer on a minecart and move it around."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"This was already covered in S1.7\",\"underlined\":true,\"color\":\"blue\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"263229837952BEAC\"}}"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Remember to enable rotation lock."
	]
	quest.0234D5EF778A3227.title: "S2.5 Long-Distance Dynamic Structure"
	quest.02ABE04F668CD001.quest_desc: [
		"Using Display Links to gather the status of a physical structure onto a screen is definitely a good idea."
		""
		"Of course, don't push yourself too far."
	]
	quest.02ABE04F668CD001.title: "Information Summary"
	quest.02AC24E1D7921EB0.quest_desc: [
		"While playing, you may occasionally see &e&lghosted&r text — this is caused by the &eMCsans+&r resource pack."
		""
		"You have two &eoptions&r:"
		""
		"①Remove &eMCsans+&r under &eOptions…&r/&eResource Packs…&r"
		""
		"②Install the [&eModern UI&r] &eModernUI&r mod instead, at the cost of a few slightly misaligned text elements."
	]
	quest.02AC24E1D7921EB0.title: "Font"
	quest.02DB3C1ECE2179FD.quest_desc: [
		"Sophisticated Backpacks gain more features by installing upgrade modules. Here are some practical ones:"
	]
	quest.02DB3C1ECE2179FD.title: "O2.11 Upgrades"
	quest.03519B3E2CB89140.quest_desc: [
		"Brass Tunnels offer several ways to split item flows, covering almost all your needs."
	]
	quest.03519B3E2CB89140.title: "4.4 Smart Splitting"
	quest.03B2C386D1570502.quest_desc: [
		"Kelp is an important raw material. If you come across any, be sure to collect some — you'll need to farm it later."
		""
		"If you need conveyor belts urgently but can't find kelp, you can craft some from coal &7(this recipe doesn't exist in vanilla — I added it manually)."
	]
	quest.03B2C386D1570502.title: "Kelp Drive"
	quest.0436FFFC388310C8.quest_desc: [
		"Use a Chute to easily feed items into a vertically placed Crushing Wheel."
		""
		"&aTips&r: There's a picture on the next page"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Example:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/s2_9_2.png width:256 height:142 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0436FFFC388310C8.title: "S2.9.2 Vertical Crushing"
	quest.0490516D16B022FC.quest_desc: [
		"The Resonator can be used as a pickaxe, axe, shovel, or hoe all at once, letting you break blocks quickly."
		""
		"Hold &eLeft Alt&r to switch modes; each mode also has its own right-click ability — for example, using it as an axe to strip bark."
		""
		"When you craft either Resonator, it &ekeeps the enchantments of the materials used&r, so you can craft it directly from the tools you're already using."
	]
	quest.0490516D16B022FC.title: "AC1.21.9 Resonator"
	quest.04D3E49C9BD5DA98.quest_desc: [
		"You can pull stress out from above or below a Chain Drive and feed it into your machines."
	]
	quest.04D3E49C9BD5DA98.title: "Stress"
	quest.052EEC12A5F2DD36.quest_desc: [
		"Waystones can also generate naturally in the wild. They let you hop around the world easily — the only cost is some experience based on distance."
	]
	quest.052EEC12A5F2DD36.title: "S1.8.2 Waystone"
	quest.0550AC0D680BA949.quest_desc: [
		"Hold a Package Frogport, right-click a &eChain&r, then place the Frogport on top of a Packager. It will then automatically handle packages at that spot."
		""
		"After placing it, remember to \"&erename&r\" the Frogport — for example, if this is a warehouse, name it &eWarehouse&r."
	]
	quest.05554C4F04FC7D2E.quest_desc: [
		"At this point, you just need to collect the output and haul it back — then the automation is complete."
	]
	quest.05554C4F04FC7D2E.title: "Collect Products"
	quest.055EE1EB615A1D5E.quest_desc: [
		"This recipe isn't used much."
	]
	quest.055EE1EB615A1D5E.title: "S2.2.5 Mass-Producing Glowstone"
	quest.05B2A7C2114EDC8F.quest_desc: [
		"Sometimes a single Crushing Wheel isn't enough, and you'll need several. Brass Tunnels make it easy to distribute materials to all of them, boosting throughput."
	]
	quest.05B2A7C2114EDC8F.title: "S2.9.4 Stacked Crushing Wheels"
	quest.062FEDF3AB2B437B.quest_desc: [
		"Build a simple rope-pulley miner and dig out a huge area in one go, putting an end to resource shortages."
		""
		"Use the Minecart Assembly Station to pack the miner up and take it with you; you can grab the output directly with a storage panel from Tom's Simple Storage."
		""
		"&aTips&r: A Windmill is a convenient way to supply stress."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"▷Build an ore-processing line next to your miner."
		""
		"▷Combine dynamic structures so your miner can move on its own."
		""
		"▷Add automatic drainage &8(and lava)&r to your miner."
	]
	quest.062FEDF3AB2B437B.title: "Mining Machine"
	quest.06BD7C3624E3270E.quest_desc: [
		"Hand-crafting Precision Mechanisms forever isn't great — build a &9machine [①]&r to automate it, and make several at once."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Click here for logistics quests\",\"underlined\":true,\"color\":\"blue\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2E816548D1DE0868\"}}"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Check the Deployer's Ponder scene."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note&r:"
		""
		"&9① [Machine]&r \"Machine\" here doesn't mean one specific block or device — it refers to a production line of your &eown design&r, including &eitem transport&7 (conveyor belts)&r and &eprocessing machines&7 (Deployers)&r."
	]
	quest.06BD7C3624E3270E.title: "S2.5 Mass-Producing!"
	quest.06CA0ACF6DACA1B2.quest_desc: [
		"Engineer's Goggles show the running status of various Create machines."
		""
		"The Wrench lets you quickly rotate and dismantle Create devices."
		""
		"They'll stick with you through your whole Create journey."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Don't use chain-mining with the Wrench — it eats blocks."
	]
	quest.06CA0ACF6DACA1B2.title: "S1.6.4 Engineers Should Behave Like Engineers"
	quest.06CF1E92496C2D66.quest_desc: [
		"Place food on the table, sit on the chair, and right-click to eat what's on the table."
		""
		"You can get potion effects lasting up to 30 minutes!"
		""
		"Cooked food goes bad if it sits around — make it fresh as you go and don't cook too much at once, or it'll go to waste!"
		""
		"&8Boss, remember to eat your cat food before heading out on an adventure, meow!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Kaleidoscope's tag system isn't well written, so I'm too lazy to write quests for this."
		""
		"Just take this free table and chair set! ("
		""
		"Time to slack off!"
	]
	quest.06CF1E92496C2D66.quest_subtitle: "&cThis part is temporarily disabled"
	quest.06CF1E92496C2D66.title: "F3.7 Feast!"
	quest.06D4C3E526DAE55F.quest_desc: [
		"Scarecrows protect surrounding farmland from being trampled."
	]
	quest.06D4C3E526DAE55F.title: "F1.15 Scarecrow"
	quest.072DA9EF2D5B6D65.quest_desc: [
		"Head to the savanna and look for wild armadillos."
		""
		"Right-click an armadillo with a Brush to get armadillo scutes."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Everything You Ever Wanted to Know About Armadillos\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://zh.minecraft.wiki/w/%E7%8A%B0%E7%8B%B3\"}}"
		""
		"&aTips&r: &eHand of God&7 (Deployer)&r and &eSeats&r will come in handy next."
	]
	quest.072DA9EF2D5B6D65.title: "H5.3.2 How Many Scales Does It Have?"
	quest.079FDC6C3116B4B4.quest_desc: [
		"Besides Ponder scenes, this quest system is also part of the guidance — if you're ever stuck, just follow the quest lines."
		""
		"For example, you can switch to the \"&eAndesite Age&r\" chapter right now and officially start your Create journey."
	]
	quest.079FDC6C3116B4B4.title: "Quest Guidance"
	quest.08164D6F47C14EF3.quest_desc: [
		"You may have noticed: if the redstone signal stays on, the small warehouse packs a package as soon as it has any items, and the wheel gets stuffed to the brim —"
		""
		"When it's full, packages heading to other Frogports get jammed. What do we do?"
		""
		"Switch to a Stockpile Switch for the redstone signal instead:"
		""
		"Attach the Stockpile Switch to the small warehouse, then connect it to the Packager with redstone dust — done!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Stockpile Switch works out of the box, but you can also tweak it — for example, output a redstone signal when the small warehouse holds &e≥64 items&r&8 (by default it triggers at ≥128)&r."
		""
		"One package holds 9 stacks, so for high-output machines &7(like a cobblestone generator)&r, you can set the switch to trigger at &e≥9 stacks&r."
	]
	quest.08164D6F47C14EF3.title: "Smart Activation"
	quest.082C92E76122BACB.quest_desc: [
		"When the &ewind stream&7 (the wind blown out by an Encased Fan)&r passes through &ewater&7 (or a waterlogged block, like wet leaves)&r, it becomes a &ewashing wind stream&r."
		""
		"The processing speed of the wind stream is &eunrelated&r to rotation speed, but multiple washing streams &estack&r, so the more, the faster."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Don't wash too much gravel in one batch — it can lag."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Wind streams &ecan't pass through&r full blocks, but some partial blocks &7(like Metal Girders and empty Blaze Burners) just happen to have the right shape —"
		""
		"items dropped on top of them get stuck right between the two levels, so they can be processed by both wind streams at once, boosting efficiency even further."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Example:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/encased_fan_eg.png width:256 height:144 align:center}"
	]
	quest.082C92E76122BACB.quest_subtitle: "Cobblestone—[Crush]—>Gravel—&e[Wash]&r—>Iron Nuggets"
	quest.082C92E76122BACB.title: "2.13 Gravel"
	quest.083DA2FEC30E56A3.quest_desc: [
		"These materials are easy to gather and mass-produce, and you can also use them to make cakes for yourself."
	]
	quest.083DA2FEC30E56A3.title: "HS4.2.1 Raw Materials"
	quest.086003948C4C3044.quest_desc: [
		"&eCreate: Aeronautics&r is a new Create add-on that lets you freely build aircraft — so freely that you might not know where to start."
		""
		"I haven't written proper tutorials for it yet, but at least I can give you a head start on materials."
	]
	quest.086003948C4C3044.quest_subtitle: "Be sure to collect your prize near the warehouse"
	quest.086003948C4C3044.title: "O5.5 Aeronautics"
	quest.08751BF9AAAF13A1.quest_desc: [
		"After a &etime shift&r, a &eBlock of Resin&7 (not a Block of Amber)&r holding a mob has a small chance of becoming the matching &eResentful Block of Amber&7 (it usually becomes a Block of Amber)&r — this is the core material for crafting mob spawners."
		""
		"This requires advancing in &eAnvilCraft&r tech — though the spawner itself isn't strictly necessary."
	]
	quest.08751BF9AAAF13A1.quest_subtitle: "It's Practically Animal Husbandry"
	quest.08751BF9AAAF13A1.title: "F2.7 Artificial Monster Spawner"
	quest.0894A266F5654165.quest_desc: [
		"While building your iron production line, did you notice you have tons of identical items to store?"
		""
		"That's where Functional Storage drawers shine — they can hold huge amounts of a single item type, making them perfect for this."
	]
	quest.0894A266F5654165.title: "S2.12.1 Drawer Cult"
	quest.08BE372420D63E29.quest_desc: [
		"Finally, use the two-in-one forging template at the Ember Forging Table with both Resonators and the Heavy Halberd to craft the Transcendent Resonator and the Transcendent Heavy Halberd."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"How to obtain Transcendent templates\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5428A8E531D969A5\"}}"
	]
	quest.08BE372420D63E29.quest_subtitle: "And that's a wrap~"
	quest.08BE372420D63E29.title: "S2.17.8 Artifact Mastery"
	quest.08C6C0161A9864BE.quest_desc: [
		"This modpack &7(well, it barely counts as one, but let's call it that)&r doesn't have grand ambitions — it just wants you to actually understand Create by the end."
		""
		"That said, you should still have a rough idea of the general modded-MC tips &7(see the quests ahead)&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There will be a lot of guidance, which might feel like \"the game teaching you how to play\"; some parts may be under-guided, or even messy."
		""
		"My apologies in advance."
	]
	quest.08C6C0161A9864BE.title: "How to Play This Modpack?"
	quest.0955E2B800DC1C95.quest_desc: [
		"When it comes to &epower transmission&7 (moving stress)&r, the most basic option is of course the &eShaft&r!"
		""
		"The Shaft transmits stress along a straight line — simple and clear."
		""
		"Some machines &7(like the Mechanical Press)&r contain Shafts, so they can double as Shafts too."
		""
		"&aTips&r: These quests don't need to be done in order — do whichever catches your eye first."
	]
	quest.0955E2B800DC1C95.quest_subtitle: "This part is more like an instruction manual than a task, so there are no numbers :)"
	quest.0955E2B800DC1C95.title: "Transmission"
	quest.098F5ADD42F45F21.quest_desc: [
		"Often you'll need to split raw materials across several machines."
		""
		"When items pass through an Andesite Tunnel, it tries to push one out to the side — pair it with a Millstone &7(or any other open container)&r."
		""
		"Containers like chests and vaults are more than one block wide, so attaching several funnels is another way to split or merge flows."
		""
		"&aTips:&r Check the Ponder scene."
	]
	quest.098F5ADD42F45F21.title: "3.4 Splitting"
	quest.0994BCB8D5EFCA4E.quest_desc: [
		"These special stones often generate in huge amounts underground; crushing them yields the corresponding ore."
		""
		"Use a Prospector Pickaxe to locate them quickly."
	]
	quest.0994BCB8D5EFCA4E.title: "Massive Ore Veins"
	quest.09B330403F3C7545.quest_desc: [
		"Or stick it next to the warehouse — when the Packager &creceives a redstone signal&r, it will &ccontinuously&r pack the items in the container."
	]
	quest.09BC3C34B7A4D7B0.title: "AnvilCraft"
	quest.0A68D103B8BE5DB4.quest_desc: [
		"Drop an anvil onto a snow block placed on a cauldron and it turns into ice, leaving a layer of powder snow in the cauldron — that's how you can mass-produce Frost Metal..."
		""
		"There are many ways to get powder snow; pick whichever you like best."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Build a snow golem, then use a Mechanical Plough to break the snow that keeps spawning under its feet — endless snowballs!"
	]
	quest.0A68D103B8BE5DB4.title: "AC1.16.1 Frost Metal"
	quest.0AA19D11C352F234.quest_desc: [
		"Tools that help you control dynamic structures via redstone wiring — feel free to skip this if redstone isn't your thing."
	]
	quest.0AA19D11C352F234.title: "S1.7.13 Snuggle Up~"
	quest.0AC87DB1718993F2.quest_desc: [
		"Plenty of Farmer's Delight foods can't be placed down, but some can be served on plates — and they even have models!"
	]
	quest.0AC87DB1718993F2.title: "F3.4 Place Food"
	quest.0B3D66496B266276.quest_desc: [
		"Lead, Zinc, and Silver can be obtained by meshing &eCinerite&r."
	]
	quest.0B3D66496B266276.title: "Mesh"
	quest.0B4E423D0F00553B.quest_desc: [
		"Stores inserted items in multiple forms at once — blocks, ingots, nuggets, and more."
		""
		"It can even force-open some irreversible compression recipes &7(like clay and quartz)&r."
	]
	quest.0B4E423D0F00553B.title: "O3.2 Compacting Drawer"
	quest.0B6015A377AFF8C3.quest_desc: [
		"Use a Blaze to melt stone into lava, then turn it into Blaze Cakes to feed the Blaze."
		""
		"Feels a bit odd, but it works."
	]
	quest.0B6015A377AFF8C3.title: "S2.6.6 Cobblestone to Lava"
	quest.0B84B2F18C3DC8DC.quest_desc: [
		"The cheapest white dye is, of course, made from bone meal."
		""
		"You should have an automatic farm by now, right?"
		""
		"A Composter can consume excess seeds and turn them into bone meal."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Seeds have plenty of other uses — check JEI&7 (EMI)"
	]
	quest.0B84B2F18C3DC8DC.title: "HS5.4.3.4 Bleaching"
	quest.0BB11F4B6ECD25A8.quest_desc: [
		"Use connectors to hook a beacon up to your storage network, letting you access it remotely — even across dimensions."
		""
		"&aTips&r: The storage connector needs to be in the &eloaded&r state."
		""
		"In simple terms, there should be &eplayers&r/&echunk loaders&r nearby — or build the storage network near &eyour spawn point&r."
	]
	quest.0BB11F4B6ECD25A8.title: "O4.5 Remote Access"
	quest.0BFDF28D91E1F1A8.quest_desc: [
		"Smoke the dough in bulk to make bread."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Smoking and washing can share the same Encased Fan — just add a campfire behind the existing washing stream and you're done."
	]
	quest.0BFDF28D91E1F1A8.title: "H1.15 Bulk Smoking"
	quest.0C04B457C2D670B9.quest_desc: [
		"Once you've gathered enough liquid experience, you can use all that green goo to duplicate enchanted books."
		""
		"A full set of Protection IV, Unbreaking III, Mending armor is within reach."
		""
		"&7That said, you should still set up a villager trading hall — it comes in handy elsewhere."
	]
	quest.0C04B457C2D670B9.title: "E1.5 Enchanted Books in Bulk"
	quest.0C4EF4D4A37ADC06.quest_desc: [
		"Multiphase Materials are the raw materials used to craft Resonators and Heavy Halberds."
	]
	quest.0C4EF4D4A37ADC06.title: "AC1.21.7 Multiphase Materials"
	quest.0C768DA9019E22C9.quest_desc: [
		"It works like a Bundle — check out &eF3.5(1)&r for the usage guide."
		""
		"Unlike a lunch basket, the food stored in this bag \"mingles\": every time you eat from it, you get the potion effects of all the food stored inside."
	]
	quest.0C768DA9019E22C9.title: "F3.10 Transmutation Lunch Bag"
	quest.0CB3B9C9C4BFAF6A.quest_desc: [
		"Stores huge amounts of a single fluid, seriously squeezing Fluid Tanks' job prospects."
		""
		"About all Fluid Tanks are good for now is boiling water."
	]
	quest.0CB3B9C9C4BFAF6A.title: "O3.3 Fluid Drawer"
	quest.0CB71FF44BE3CEB1.quest_desc: [
		"Sharestones let you teleport straight to other Sharestones of the same color without activating them first — extra handy on multiplayer servers."
	]
	quest.0CB71FF44BE3CEB1.title: "S1.8.3 Sharestone"
	quest.0CE7AF686BE2EFE5.quest_desc: [
		"&cPlayers&r throwing Iron Ingots through a Hollow Magnet have a chance to turn them into Magnets."
		""
		"Aiming is way too fiddly — try wedging yourself inside the Hollow Magnet instead."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7A Chute won't work, though — it's sealed up tight&r"
	]
	quest.0CE7AF686BE2EFE5.title: "AC1.5.1 This Is a Feature!"
	quest.0CF88205796A3F1F.quest_desc: [
		"This is the cozy little home you've prepared for your hard-working Blazes &m&8(pending verification)&r. Right-click it on a &eBlaze&r or a &eBlaze Spawner&r to turn it into a Blaze Burner."
		""
		"The Nether is full of dangers — bring a &eWaystone&r so trips to and from fortresses &7(fortress)&r are much easier."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Fire Resistance potions work great against Blazes."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Can't find a fortress? Use the &eExplorer's Compass&r and search for &efortress&r."
	]
	quest.0CF88205796A3F1F.title: "1.9 \"A Cozy Home\""
	quest.0D309C1374621C8A.quest_desc: [
		"It's pricey, but worth every bit."
	]
	quest.0D309C1374621C8A.title: "AC1.21.6 Expensive Collisions"
	quest.0D79B24C56340C45.quest_desc: [
		"You can &ewash&r different sands to get the corresponding nuggets, and every ingredient needed is renewable."
		""
		"Use JEI&7 (EMI)&r to look up the exact methods."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Related information\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"44E4DB19E314EABB\" } }"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Copper Nuggets come from washing &eCinerite&r or &eControllable Sand&r — Cinerite is much easier."
		""
		"The next page has other methods."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"All five of these special stones can be crafted from Cobblestone, and there are plenty of different routes."
		""
		"Some routes are short, some are tedious — it's best to read them all and pick your favorite."
		""
		"You can design and build your own production lines to mass-produce them."
		""
		"How do you get Cobblestone? A cobblestone generator, of course — I shouldn't have to teach you that."
	]
	quest.0D79B24C56340C45.title: "Everything from Cobblestone"
	quest.0D82EA971359499B.quest_desc: [
		"The End doesn't really hold important resources for you — feel free to visit once you're not busy."
		""
		"&8Since you've been playing with Create this long, why not design some machines for the Ender Dragon and Endermen too?"
	]
	quest.0D82EA971359499B.title: "2.15 Heading Towards the End"
	quest.0DA337D6434410D6.quest_desc: [
		"Building an Enderman farm in the void beyond the End's main island is extremely efficient — pair it with Deployers for the finishing blow and your XP problems are solved for good."
		""
		"Once it's built, check out the Create: Enchantment Industry content."
	]
	quest.0DA337D6434410D6.title: "S2.17.1 Enderman Farm"
	quest.0DE0AD10085E2DB7.quest_desc: [
		"When a Factory Gauge is set to a crafting recipe, packages can be fed into the Mechanical Crafter to craft. Combined with the Unpackager, multiple packages can be merged and imported."
	]
	quest.0DE0AD10085E2DB7.title: "S4.10.1 Automated Crafting"
	quest.0E14CA0D1F334373.quest_desc: [
		"Use Gold Ingots at the Royal Grindstone to remove curses and obtain Cursed Gold Ingots."
		""
		"Where do all those curses come from?"
		""
		"When you copy items like keys at the &eJewelry Workbench&r, the copies come pre-cursed."
	]
	quest.0E14CA0D1F334373.title: "HS5.2.3.1 Remove Curse"
	quest.0E261EE5B5EA8F41.quest_desc: [
		"The trick is Resistance!"
		""
		"The impurities in the potion even boosted the yield — a double win."
	]
	quest.0E261EE5B5EA8F41.title: "S2.2.13 Grow up Quickly~"
	quest.0E2A14E3043A91C5.quest_desc: [
		"Stuff a Crafting Table into your backpack and you get 9 extra storage slots to boot — quite practical."
	]
	quest.0E2A14E3043A91C5.title: "O2.16 Portable Workbench"
	quest.0E75BB7A7E113575.quest_desc: [
		"The Storage Controller can handle a huge number of drawers without even needing to touch them."
	]
	quest.0E75BB7A7E113575.title: "S2.12.3 Storage Controller"
	quest.0E7C030F8D3D4F89.quest_desc: [
		"Don't throw away extra bread — feed it to villagers and trade supplies with them later."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"▷Build a villager trading hall."
		""
		"▷Use a Trading Depot to automate trades."
		""
		"▷Set up a villager trade discount machine."
	]
	quest.0E7C030F8D3D4F89.title: "Villager Breeding"
	quest.0EBEB923AE73671A.quest_desc: [
		"The Redstone Requester places an order with the storage network when it receives a redstone signal &7(needs to be configured manually first)&r."
	]
	quest.0EDF4C9A21F28291.quest_desc: [
		"You've got &eEncased Fans&r ready for bulk smelting, right? Just ship the wood over."
		""
		"Multiple processing streams stack, so if you're interested, you can build a multi-speed bulk processing center."
	]
	quest.0EDF4C9A21F28291.title: "H2.6 Logistics"
	quest.0EF1BC9EBF6AE1D3.quest_desc: [
		"Get uranium from collisions — stock up on plenty."
	]
	quest.0EF1BC9EBF6AE1D3.title: "AC1.21.3 Uranium"
	quest.0F281521E69C4A60.quest_desc: [
		"There are plenty more &7(really, a lot)&r machines you can build right now."
		""
		"If you're in a hurry to progress, feel free to skip them for now."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Remember to come back to these later."
	]
	quest.0F281521E69C4A60.title: "S1.7 Other Machines"
	quest.0F492741358DF5E0.quest_desc: [
		"Making Andesite Alloy this way uses only half the materials of hand-crafting it."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Besides throwing items straight into the Basin, you can also feed it with Funnels."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Power it with &eCogwheels&7 (not Shafts)&r!"
		""
		"&eRemember to watch the Ponder scene, meow! Please watch it, meow!"
		""
		"The Basin also automatically ejects finished items into nearby &eopen containers&r&7 (Basin, Depot, Conveyor Belt, Andesite Funnel, Brass Funnel, Item Drain, Millstone, Crushing Wheel... — Basins and Item Drains can also accept fluids)&f."
		""
		"That means you can easily separate out the output — just place an open container nearby."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Vanilla Funnels don't count as open containers."
	]
	quest.0F492741358DF5E0.quest_subtitle: "Industrial Frother (Not)"
	quest.0F492741358DF5E0.title: "1.7 Kitchen Utensils"
	quest.0FA4245F6B8D3912.quest_desc: [
		"This modpack changes the crafting recipes of quite a few items, which means some recipes probably won't work in other modpacks."
		""
		"My apologies — a teaching pack that changes recipes is a bit of a letdown—"
		""
		"But I promise this pack will properly teach you how to play Create, and how to play modpacks."
		""
		"Given that most modpacks tweak recipes anyway, maybe the modified recipes are actually this pack's selling point &7(laughs)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"On the recipe lookup page, hold &eCtrl&f and &eleft-click&r a recipe's output to get its recipe ID. For example:"
		""
		"&aminecraft&r:&6spruce_trapdoor&r"
		"&7[Definition]&r&aminecraft&7 (mod)&r adds &6spruce_trapdoor&7 (item)&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Any recipe whose ID contains &zkubejs&r or &zkjs&r is modpack-added content and won't work outside this modpack. For example:"
		""
		"jei:/create/&zkjs&r/raw_earth_core_shard"
	]
	quest.0FA4245F6B8D3912.title: "Recipe Changes"
	quest.0FB7A7F78D570407.quest_desc: [
		"A classic, easy method to quickly collect the cobblestone churned out by your cobblestone generator."
	]
	quest.0FB7A7F78D570407.title: "S2.11.1 Water Collection"
	quest.0FF38519C23079ED.quest_desc: [
		"It's a decoration too."
	]
	quest.0FF38519C23079ED.title: "O4.15 Can Also Be Dyed"
	quest.10275511180E910D.quest_desc: [
		"Build a compact workstation that covers everything you need early on: rolling, mixing, grinding, cutting, and Encased Fan bulk processing."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"▷Run your workstation at 256 rpm — i.e., every machine gets 256 rpm."
		""
		"▷Push your Encased Fan bulk processing to 2x speed or more."
		"&aTips:&r Encased Fan processing speed has nothing to do with rotation speed — only stacking multiple fans' wind streams makes processing faster."
		""
		"▷Add automatic feeding and output buffering to your machines."
	]
	quest.10275511180E910D.title: "Workstation"
	quest.102C4636E621290E.quest_desc: [
		"The big new thing in Create 6.0 is this logistics system: Packagers and Stock Links form your &elogistics network&r."
		""
		"I only bring it up in the Brass Age because you usually don't need it during the Andesite Age."
		""
		"&cNote&f: Packages can't travel by water!"
	]
	quest.102C4636E621290E.title: "S2.12.5 Create 6.0"
	quest.1053C23A8B5552FE.quest_desc: [
		"A boiler in the &epassive&r state can still produce &a2048su&r of stress — already pretty big!"
		""
		"Stacking passive boilers is actually quite convenient; the only downside is a slower rotation speed."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Stacked, it looks something like this:"
		"&7\"equivalent\" refers to the stress produced by a single boiler"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/s_1_6_5.png width:256 height:144 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1053C23A8B5552FE.quest_subtitle: "If someone interrogates you, don't rat me out!"
	quest.1053C23A8B5552FE.title: "S1.6.5 Shhh, Don’t Tell Others That I Taught You"
	quest.1065B8AFEBAC48AF.quest_desc: [
		"A one-time-use Warp Stone."
		""
		"Taking damage while using it will still interrupt the teleport."
	]
	quest.1065B8AFEBAC48AF.title: "OS1.3.2 Warp Scroll"
	quest.106C38491170F4B2.quest_desc: [
		"Yes — there's Farmer's Delight and Kaleidoscope. This is a food modpack; there's no saving us!"
		""
		"This content is here to enrich your Create journey — feel free to ignore it if it's not your thing."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"While wearing a Straw Hat, breaking short grass has a chance to drop Kaleidoscope crop seeds."
		""
		"Also, the knives from both mods are interchangeable now, so you don't need two sets."
		""
		"Lastly, Create: Food adds tons of food that looks plain but actually grants potion effects &8(the author was too lazy to put it in the item descriptions)&r."
		""
		"Check them out in JEI&8 (EMI)&r — just press \"U\"."
	]
	quest.106C38491170F4B2.title: "E1.7.3 Eat Something Good"
	quest.1085E91902D8E1AF.quest_desc: [
		"This is the final quest of the modpack."
		""
		"In this series, the quest line runs backwards — which is also the real, common way to explore any mod on your own: &eworking backwards&r."
		""
		"From now on, whenever you want to craft something, use JEI&7 (EMI)&r to trace the process and materials step by step from the final product."
		""
		"Of course, when actually crafting, you still go forward from the raw materials."
	]
	quest.1085E91902D8E1AF.quest_subtitle: "The Final Countdown"
	quest.1085E91902D8E1AF.title: "H5.1 Transcendent Alloy"
	quest.108A7293964E6860.quest_desc: [
		"Besides the basic materials, you'll also need one set each of Frost Metal and Ember Metal weapons and tools."
	]
	quest.108A7293964E6860.title: "S2.17.1 Smithing Template"
	quest.109BE3721445EE5E.title: "AC1.21 AnvilCraft Matryoshka Doll"
	quest.10D8C7654C651BEB.quest_desc: [
		"Attach a Packager to any face of a container, then power it with a redstone signal and it will &econtinuously&r pack the container's items into packages."
		""
		"One package holds 9 stacks, and packages can be moved quickly via Chain Conveyors, greatly boosting logistics efficiency."
	]
	quest.10D8C7654C651BEB.title: "3.7 Packaging"
	quest.10E3D0924F832EC6.quest_desc: [
		"Tridents can be crafted repeatedly using a &eHeart of the Sea&r&7 (it's renewable — check the recipe)&r."
		""
		"For the Heavy Hammer, bring the &eBad Omen&r effect into a Trial Chamber, use the Ominous Trial Key it drops to open an &eOminous Vault&r, and grab the Heavy Core &7(the drop rate is heartbreaking)&r."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Smash a Lead Block into the vault with an anvil and the vault will forget it's already been opened."
		""
		"Also, both keys and Heavy Cores can be duplicated at the Jewelry Workbench."
	]
	quest.10E3D0924F832EC6.title: "AC1.21.10 Heavy Halberd Core"
	quest.10EB5A662608C367.quest_desc: [
		"Hover over it and hold &eShift&r to see the description."
		""
		"&aTips&r: The Potato Cannon can fire more than just potatoes — its damage scales with the ammo type &7(Golden Carrots and Blaze Cakes recommended)&r."
		""
		"Both the cannon and the tank on your back can be enchanted."
	]
	quest.10EB5A662608C367.title: "S2.15.1 Alternatives to Bows and Arrows"
	quest.10F6FE7BC7406958.quest_desc: [
		"A dedicated filter for package destination addresses, aimed at veteran mechanics."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&e*&r is a wildcard that matches any text of any length and any amount — it also works in Create's logistics system."
		""
		"\"&e*&r machine\" can match \"&eiron&r machine\", \"&ewitch&r machine\", or \"&ePhantom&r machine\"."
		""
		"But \"&e*&r machine\" can't match \"&cThis is a&r &epig&r machine&c device&r\" &7(if you want, use \"*machine*\" to match this name)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Besides &e*&r, &e?&7 (English question mark)&r is also a wildcard that matches exactly one character."
		""
		"For example, \"&e?&r\" can match \"&eA&r\", but not \"&eB&cC&r\"."
		""
		"The two symbols can be combined for complex patterns — \"&e*&rtext&1?&2?&3?&4?&r\" matches \"&eRandom&rtext&1A&2B&3C&4D&r\"."
		""
		"This comes in handy for &epackage address encoding&8 (a feature you'll probably never use)&r."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Package Address Encoding (Part 4 of this video)\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1qqh6zME9n/\"}}"
	]
	quest.10F6FE7BC7406958.quest_subtitle: "A Niche Overkill Trick"
	quest.10F6FE7BC7406958.title: "4.7 Package Filters"
	quest.112A60B1E4DAD6AD.quest_desc: [
		"Use a simple physics trick: a &elarge Cogwheel&r driving a &esmall Cogwheel&r doubles the rotation speed!"
		""
		"One step isn't very noticeable, so &erepeat&r it a few times."
		""
		"Higher speeds mean &ehigher work efficiency&r — and higher stress consumption."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aTips&f:"
		""
		"Machine efficiency depends on rotation speed, not the total amount of stress."
		""
		"Stress can't be stored — unused stress just vanishes."
		""
		"Also, wearing &eEngineer's Goggles&7 (next quest)&r shows detailed speed and stress consumption."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Gear ratio reference:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/s1_6_3.png width:256 height:142 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The default speed cap is 256 rpm — beyond that, gears and Shafts will explode."
		""
		"Wear &eEngineer's Goggles&r to check a machine's stress consumption, and use a Speedometer to check the current speed."
		""
		"Andesite Casing can enclose gears, making your gearbox more compact."
		""
		"&aTips&r: The images are works by other novice mechanics — as you reference them, think about what could be improved :)"
	]
	quest.112A60B1E4DAD6AD.quest_subtitle: "Work efficiency is only linked to rotation speed"
	quest.112A60B1E4DAD6AD.title: "S1.6.3 Faster, Faster"
	quest.11B92BA6A58AD720.title: "Naturally Occurring"
	quest.11B9BB3FA707DA1D.quest_desc: [
		"The vanilla Crafter is quite efficient and is a solid choice."
		""
		"&aTips&r: If you want to use Grandpa Niu &8(the Crafter really does look like him www)&r, Brass Tunnels help a lot — check their Ponder scene."
	]
	quest.11B9BB3FA707DA1D.title: "HS3.5.2 Grandpa Niu"
	quest.11D2770974ED6ABB.quest_desc: [
		"The second step in mass-producing Frost Alloy."
		""
		"Other than that, titanium isn't much use."
		""
		"&8You could make a flying machine with it, but that thing needs electricity."
	]
	quest.11D2770974ED6ABB.title: "S2.2.7 Silver to Titanium"
	quest.11E5F573B98CA97B.quest_desc: [
		"Try using this logistics system to boost your efficiency—"
		""
		"Keep your warehouse stocked with ingredients so you don't have to run between machines, and keep your workbench table stocked with chocolate berries!"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Automation example\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"5329D3AD8C264AAE\"}}"
	]
	quest.11E5F573B98CA97B.title: "H2.12.1 Automation!"
	quest.11F5C25A065AA3EA.quest_desc: [
		"Farmer's Delight is a classic cooking mod — most of its food is quite nutritious and great for everyday eating."
		""
		"Place a Cooking Pot or Skillet on a &eheat source&7 (fire, campfire, magma block, stove, Blaze Burner...)&r, then just add ingredients according to the &erecipe&7 (check JEI)&r and it cooks automatically."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Basket is surprisingly practical — check its Ponder scene."
	]
	quest.11F5C25A065AA3EA.title: "F3.2 Farmer's Delight"
	quest.12011211264DC272.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click the air with a handheld magnet to pull nearby dropped items toward you."
		""
		"Right-clicking a block creates a magnetization node that attracts dropped items in a small radius. That way, tossing ingredients into a cauldron won't miss."
	]
	quest.12011211264DC272.title: "AC1.6.1 Drop Magnet"
	quest.12D50270D012C75B.quest_desc: [
		"Chocolate is a great food."
		""
		"Besides eating it, you can also use it in some forbidden rituals to draw in cursed power and turn Gold into Cursed Gold."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Oh right, there are many kinds of chocolate and they're all edible — that's normal."
		""
		"I mean, supermarkets sell plenty of chocolate brands too!"
		""
		"Only Create's &eChocolate&7 (the Chinese one)&r can make Cursed Gold — don't mix them up!"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/create_mixing_chocolate.png width:165 height:135 align:center}"
	]
	quest.12D50270D012C75B.title: "F3.8 Forbidden Power"
	quest.12F6325DFF5A2511.quest_desc: [
		"A giant cake marks your outstanding achievement in the culinary arts!"
		""
		"Such a big cake is beyond what ordinary kitchen tools can handle. You'll need to study &eAnvilCraft&r techniques — or find a player who's handy with industry?"
	]
	quest.12F6325DFF5A2511.title: "F3.9 Creating Wonders!"
	quest.12FCCFF67EB9D9B3.quest_desc: [
		"Tracks aren't better than wheels, but maybe more stable?"
		""
		"They work much like tires, except you can only steer using &espeed differences&r."
	]
	quest.12FCCFF67EB9D9B3.title: "Track"
	quest.133F45D674B072EA.quest_desc: [
		"A contraption built around Mechanical Bearings is great for tree farms too, though a large one like a spruce farm will take up quite a bit of space."
	]
	quest.133F45D674B072EA.title: "H2.3 Rotating Tree Farm"
	quest.13729347EEB874B9.quest_desc: [
		"Brass Funnels and Smart Chutes can have filters installed directly, letting you sort out exactly the items you need."
	]
	quest.13729347EEB874B9.title: "H1.12 Filter"
	quest.13B8ADC73C056AFB.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Crafter can also make some fun, practical tools."
		""
		"The &eSymmetry Wand&r boosts your building speed, the &ePotato Cannon&r is a powerful ranged weapon, and the &eExtendo Grip&r extends your interaction range."
		""
		"&7Best paired with a Gas Tank"
		""
		"There are plenty of other fun tools too — they'll be listed in the next quest."
	]
	quest.13B8ADC73C056AFB.title: "S2.8.1 Rare Stuff"
	quest.13CB6BB1680BF625.quest_desc: [
		"This part requires Andesite Alloy to craft."
	]
	quest.13CB6BB1680BF625.title: "Statement"
	quest.1456D6B04B4DA15A.quest_desc: [
		"Multiple Item Vaults can be linked into one big container that supports lots of Packagers or Funnels — perfect as a logistics hub."
	]
	quest.1456D6B04B4DA15A.title: "S3.7.1 Large Container~"
	quest.1480AE598B3F5363.quest_desc: [
		"Later recipes can't avoid needing a Beacon, so you'll have to slay a few Withers."
		""
		"If you're not confident in your combat skills, you can trap a Wither in the Nether's top bedrock — Bilibili has plenty of tutorials."
	]
	quest.1480AE598B3F5363.title: "AC1.15 Beacon"
	quest.152C662A5793BE8E.quest_desc: [
		"Use them to remotely control your logistics system, see its Ponder scene for details"
	]
	quest.152C662A5793BE8E.title: "S2.12.8 Managing a Logistics Network"
	quest.15347E77C3F75184.quest_desc: [
		"Here are some tools that can replace most complex redstone wiring and make building physical structures much easier."
		""
		"&aTips&r: See the item description for how to use them."
	]
	quest.15347E77C3F75184.title: "Simplify Wiring"
	quest.154416D3A6801D63.quest_desc: [
		"No doubt about it: farming is a key source of cooking ingredients."
		""
		"In this pack, some recipe ingredients also have to be farmed."
		""
		"So grab your hoe and get to work!"
	]
	quest.154416D3A6801D63.quest_subtitle: "\"Shennong is reincarnated, and when he arrives in another world, he must show his true skills!\""
	quest.154416D3A6801D63.title: "F1.1 Farming!"
	quest.156A3365E209D363.quest_desc: [
		"If you're short on a certain resource in later quests, you can get some on credit here for now."
		""
		"Yes, on credit — the kind you never have to pay back."
	]
	quest.156A3365E209D363.quest_subtitle: "&cAbuse of this feature may harm the gaming experience"
	quest.156A3365E209D363.title: "Credit"
	quest.1572E75B690DD564.quest_desc: [
		"Mix gems into Melt Gem, then Compact it to get the corresponding gem block."
	]
	quest.1572E75B690DD564.title: "Melt Gem"
	quest.15C05C2A9039B324.quest_desc: [
		"One of the ways to remove items from a dynamic structure"
	]
	quest.15C05C2A9039B324.title: "S1.7.13 Automated Retrieval"
	quest.16E1D2B2AF8645E7.quest_desc: [
		"Both Tungsten Ore and Ancient Debris can be obtained by &espout-filling&r them with different potions."
	]
	quest.16E1D2B2AF8645E7.title: "Alchemy"
	quest.175C11A7E58931AE.quest_desc: [
		"Mount a Mechanical Saw on a dynamic contraption to fell a whole tree at once and automatically collect the drops&7 (if there's a container)&r."
		""
		"A Deployer is used to replant saplings."
	]
	quest.175C11A7E58931AE.title: "H2.1 No Matter What, Let’s Mass-Produce Wood First."
	quest.17D89E90D4C73DFC.quest_desc: [
		"This is the pack's endgame material — Transcendent Alloy."
		""
		"Transcendent Alloy is a complex material: you process large amounts of Iron and Gold with Dragon's Breath, experience, and potions."
		""
		"It's tricky to make, but worth it — it's the ingredient for crafting all sorts of &zCreative items&r."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Click to jump to the guide quest\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"1085E91902D8E1AF\" } }"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aTips&r: You can also make Transcendent Alloy with &eAnvilCraft&f recipes — though it's not any easier."
		""
		"With luck&7 (i.e. under the Luck effect)&f, you can also find Transcendent Alloy Ingots in the End's vaults."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Random thoughts:"
		""
		"I've noticed a lot of packs like to have a complicated endgame item, so I went along with the trend..."
		""
		"But not all the way — no hundreds of craft cycles like some packs, and the process isn't that complex either."
	]
	quest.17D89E90D4C73DFC.quest_subtitle: "Countdown to the Final Save"
	quest.17D89E90D4C73DFC.title: "S2.17.6 Beyond the Limit"
	quest.17E1343A083C40E0.quest_desc: [
		"It is difficult to mass-produce gold ingots, but this is the final task after all."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Mass-Producing Gold Ingots\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"469208ED7DC7B90E\"}}"
	]
	quest.17E1343A083C40E0.title: "H5.2.3 Mass-Producing Cursed Gold"
	quest.17F191488FABC5C3.quest_desc: [
		"Create: Steam 'n' Rails adds a huge variety of decorative blocks. Search \"&e@rails&r\" to see them all!"
	]
	quest.17F191488FABC5C3.title: "T1.3.1 Decorative Trains"
	quest.180F4DF11E0D9B34.quest_desc: [
		"The Linker connects drawer blocks into / removes them from the drawer network&7 (right-click air; Shift+right-click to switch modes)&r."
		""
		"The Configurator can &elock&r a drawer so the controller won't push other items into it even when empty&7 (which simplifies wireless item transport in the drawer network)&r."
	]
	quest.180F4DF11E0D9B34.title: "O3.6 The Wrench in the Drawer World"
	quest.182A1B6AC2CC4A60.quest_desc: [
		"If you see this, it means that either I forgot to write it, or I didn't finish the follow-up content."
	]
	quest.182A1B6AC2CC4A60.title: "Explanation"
	quest.185B93334F9DA51C.quest_desc: [
		"&eThat's it — you've graduated!"
		""
		"Feels sudden? Along the way you've basically learned how to play Create, enough to handle most adventure packs that include it."
		""
		"Keep gaining experience as you play on, and expert packs or chill packs will be a breeze."
		""
		"&8Finished all the side quests yet?"
	]
	quest.185B93334F9DA51C.quest_subtitle: "It's over?"
	quest.185B93334F9DA51C.title: "2.17 Liberate the End"
	quest.186329A2A56FD210.quest_desc: [
		"Power the Heater, toss some ore into the cauldron above, give it a whack, and it becomes two ores."
	]
	quest.186329A2A56FD210.title: "AC1.8 Ore Doubling, So Fast!"
	quest.18820CFAE741DB8A.quest_desc: [
		"Since you need liquid experience, the quest only asks for the equivalent of 1000mb&7 (one bucket)&r."
		""
		"There are plenty of ways to get experience: furnace arrays, silverfish farms, enderman farms, Ultimate Lapis..."
		""
		"Silverfish farms are the pick of the bunch."
	]
	quest.18820CFAE741DB8A.title: "H5.2.4 Mass-Producing Experience"
	quest.18C1E22A9888E1B5.quest_desc: [
		"Mount a Mechanical Saw on a &edynamic contraption&7 (a Mechanical Bearing works great)&r, and you can easily build a tree farm."
		""
		"See the &eMechanical Bearing's&r Ponder scene for details."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Auto-replanting saplings needs a Deployer."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Rotating tree farm diagram:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/s1_7_3.png width:256 height:142 align:center}"
	]
	quest.18C1E22A9888E1B5.quest_subtitle: "Remember to view the Ponder scene!"
	quest.18C1E22A9888E1B5.title: "S1.11.4 Build a Tree Farm"
	quest.18EFCAA387654B1A.quest_desc: [
		"Create adds a powerful railway system, but it's not enough."
		""
		"So along came &eCreate: Steam 'n' Rails&r, a mod dedicated to expanding the rail system."
		""
		"In the quests ahead, I'll walk you through the rail system's features in roughly the order you'll need them."
		""
		"Before that, you'll need a few basic things — namely, train tracks."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"This pack uses an unofficial port of Steam 'n' Rails, since the official version never came out."
		""
		"If you'd like a preview of what this part has to offer, check out this video:"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"A Brief Introduction to the Rail System\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1gCNkeGEJR?p=12\" } }"
	]
	quest.18EFCAA387654B1A.quest_subtitle: "Unofficial Port"
	quest.18EFCAA387654B1A.title: "T1.1 Create: Steam 'n' Rails"
	quest.190F08AFB913637A.quest_desc: [
		"Craft these tasty snacks and let a Blaze perform Transcendent Enchantments — up to level 60!"
		""
		"Transcendent Enchanting draws down a thunderbolt, so use Lightning Rods to divert it and take fire precautions in advance."
	]
	quest.190F08AFB913637A.title: "E1.10 Beyond Enchantment"
	quest.192EF43BCEAC74B1.quest_desc: [
		"&eFunctional Storage&r offers a wide variety of drawers for storing large amounts of the same item."
		""
		"Just peek at the Life Tips section when you need it. No need to read through everything now — that'd be exhausting."
	]
	quest.192EF43BCEAC74B1.title: "Functional Storage"
	quest.1987C1711966FB61.quest_desc: [
		"Many modpacks add tons of items, and the vanilla inventory just isn't enough."
		""
		"The mod &eSophisticated Backpacks&r offers a huge backpack plus lots of handy upgrades to make your travels easier."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Press &eE&r to open your inventory. There's a small ring at the character's upper left — that's the &etrinket slot&r. You can put your backpack in the &eback slot&r so it won't take up your chestplate slot."
		""
		"Press &eB&r to quickly open the backpack. It can also be upgraded for more space — see the Sophisticated Backpacks chapter."
	]
	quest.1987C1711966FB61.title: "We Need Big Backpacks"
	quest.19BCE614B4AAEE0A.quest_desc: [
		"Take a look at JEI&7(EMI)&r, there is an extra recipe for green dye: you can extract green dye from leaves!"
		""
		"If you really don't want to figure it out, just claim it for free here."
	]
	quest.19BCE614B4AAEE0A.title: "S1.7.16 Can’t Find Cactus and Fern?"
	quest.19E7D0D5D4F06150.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click the seed packet to get random seeds&7 (yay, a mystery box!)&r, enriching your field's ecology."
		""
		"With more crop varieties, you can &eintercrop&7 (within 4 blocks of each crop, there can be at most 2 crops of the same kind)&r, which speeds up crop growth&7 (growing time is cut by about a quarter)&r"
		""
		"But... yield aside, more crop varieties clearly means &emore tasty food&r!"
		""
		"&8Yummy! Yummy! Yummy! Yummy! Yummy!"
	]
	quest.19E7D0D5D4F06150.title: "F1.2 A Richer Field Ecology"
	quest.1A37242E93FF0AF5.quest_desc: [
		"It's a very useful upgrade — not so much automatic feeding as automatic healing."
		"And while you're at it, enjoy a feast."
	]
	quest.1A37242E93FF0AF5.title: "O2.21 Map Exploration Artifact"
	quest.1A569E75FFA4641D.quest_desc: [
		"The Nether and the End have unique ingredients that cook up into unexpected delicacies."
		""
		"As MC's finest chefs, we've got to roam the world, gather rare ingredients, and taste every dish!"
		""
		"&8Tired? Whatever, take your time..."
	]
	quest.1A569E75FFA4641D.title: "3.11 Eat Everything in Minecraft"
	quest.1B033F4CB68051B3.quest_desc: [
		"Place some &eOrganic Compost&r on the ground; after a long while, it will turn into &eRich Soil&r."
		""
		"Crops planted on Rich Soil grow faster."
		""
		"You can also &egrow mushrooms&r on Rich Soil."
	]
	quest.1B033F4CB68051B3.title: "F1.7 Higher Yields"
	quest.1B135D79345CE60F.quest_desc: [
		"At this stage, Andesite Alloy is no longer enough for all your complex needs..."
		""
		"We need to find &eBlazes&r and use their heat to produce Brass."
	]
	quest.1B135D79345CE60F.title: "1.8 We Need to Go Deeper"
	quest.1B317264B3ABF709.quest_desc: [
		"Same as before: set up a Package Frogport."
		""
		"This Frogport just hangs packages on the chain — no need to take them down, so you don't have to name it."
	]
	quest.1BABACE4C71BED40.quest_desc: [
		"Just like its description."
		""
		"&8By the way, the filtering of the Sophisticated Backpacks also has this option."
	]
	quest.1BABACE4C71BED40.title: "O4.18 Whitelist"
	quest.1BB9BF9EFC596EDC.quest_desc: [
		"27 Blocks of Coal trade for one Diamond Block. You could already mass-produce diamonds by now, but this recipe is cheaper."
		""
		"Similarly, Giant Anvils can be produced this way."
		""
		"&aTips&r: See the tutorial book for details."
	]
	quest.1BB9BF9EFC596EDC.title: "AC1.21.1 Mass-Producing Diamonds"
	quest.1C04AB8617976CBD.quest_desc: [
		"The Encased Fan's bulk processing has tons of advantages and some exclusive recipes — I highly recommend building one."
		""
		"For example: it only needs stress&7 (no fuel)&r, processes extremely fast&7 (compared to vanilla)&r, and its throughput is limited only by your PC's performance."
	]
	quest.1C04AB8617976CBD.title: "S1.7.12 Bulk Processing"
	quest.1C3CAA1C27534E62.quest_desc: [
		"Create your first bogie with &eTrain Casing&r!"
		""
		"After that, keep building the train on top of the bogie. A train needs at least one bogie and one driver's cab."
		""
		"You can seat a driver on a chair, or let a Blaze Burner do the job instead. They can follow train schedules and drive automatically, and they're faster than you."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Don't forget the Super Glue!"
	]
	quest.1C3CAA1C27534E62.title: "T1.3 Assembling Trains"
	quest.1C571172EDD00AC2.quest_desc: [
		"Install a boring head on a car and it becomes a tunnel boring machine."
		""
		"Be careful not to let the boring head break blocks below wheel level, or it'll turn into a core-drilling rig."
	]
	quest.1C571172EDD00AC2.title: "Special Features"
	quest.1C5B599C278D3669.quest_desc: [
		"A dynamic contraption with containers can store and transport items too. Pair it with a Portable Storage Interface to interact with external logistics systems."
	]
	quest.1C5B599C278D3669.title: "3.6 Dynamic Structure Logistics"
	quest.1C7A6F53784CCDB3.quest_desc: [
		"When the Packager receives a package, it automatically opens it and stores the contents in a container."
		""
		"Mechanical Saws are usually placed between conveyor belts to unpack packages and queue the items back onto the belt."
		""
		"Packages also pop open when they touch water or when they take fatal damage, spilling their contents."
	]
	quest.1C7A6F53784CCDB3.title: "3.8 Unpacking"
	quest.1CA3056632D85267.quest_desc: [
		"Consume Blocks of Netherite and Earth Core Shards to obtain Ember Metal."
	]
	quest.1CA3056632D85267.title: "AC1.19 Ember Metal"
	quest.1CC282F6F0C22441.quest_desc: [
		"Yes, there are fish living in the Nether's lava. Besides being ingredients, they can also be used for brewing."
	]
	quest.1CC282F6F0C22441.quest_subtitle: "Lava lake is also a lake, so it is normal to have fish!"
	quest.1CC282F6F0C22441.title: "F4.6 I Wonder If There Are Fish Here"
	quest.1CCE66A323DCA9C1.quest_desc: [
		"Hmm...just make a brush first"
	]
	quest.1CCE66A323DCA9C1.quest_subtitle: "The forgettable update suddenly attacks me"
	quest.1CCE66A323DCA9C1.title: "H5.3.1 Archaeology"
	quest.1D073B7C4BD59CA6.quest_desc: [
		"If the end of a conveyor belt isn't blocked, items fly right off."
		""
		"Besides putting a block at the end, a Depot is a great choice too — a Depot holding items also blocks the belt."
	]
	quest.1D073B7C4BD59CA6.title: "S3.2.2 This Road Is Blocked"
	quest.1D3280A6441C9112.quest_desc: [
		"I mean it — you can't go any faster; it'll break!"
		""
		"&aTips&r: The default speed cap is 256. Above that, Cogwheels and Shafts explode."
	]
	quest.1D3280A6441C9112.title: "A1.6.1 Wuhu, Take Off!"
	quest.1D8C4BC9D5F96D9E.quest_desc: [
		"You can make a few more backpacks. Whether you wear them on your body or connect them to the logistics system, backpacks are very useful and you won’t have too many."
	]
	quest.1D8C4BC9D5F96D9E.title: "O2.4 More Backpacks"
	quest.1DA94D67F0B86E9B.quest_desc: [
		"You can hunt Shulkers in the End for Shulker Shells, or get them by finishing Wolf Armor."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Everything You Need to Know About Shulkers\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://zh.minecraft.wiki/w/%E6%BD%9C%E5%BD%B1%E8%B4%9D#%E4%BA%BA%E4%B8%BA%E7%94%9F%E6%88%90\" } }"
	]
	quest.1DA94D67F0B86E9B.title: "H5.3 Casing"
	quest.1DBF6994087931C6.quest_desc: [
		"Head to the Nether, capture a Blaze, and step into the Brass Age."
		""
		"The Brass Age unlocks many handier components, making machine design much easier."
	]
	quest.1DBF6994087931C6.quest_subtitle: "Prerequisites (but not mandatory)"
	quest.1DBF6994087931C6.title: "New Member"
	quest.1DF7559560D06CF3.quest_desc: [
		"The most important aspect of the modpack is the guidance &7 (personal opinion, please do not criticise) &r."
		""
		"In this modpack, guidance is mainly provided through the quest system, which is this page."
		""
		"If you are unsure what to do, follow the quest instructions to progress."
	]
	quest.1E178EEB88CDD228.quest_desc: [
		"Arriving in another world&7 (and how is MC not another world?)&r, the first priority is survival, and the second is figuring out whether you can grow crops&7 (obviously)&r."
		""
		"None of this is strictly required, but the honey here can significantly boost mineral output, and chocolate lets you mass-produce Cursed Gold."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If you like farming, you might also enjoy building."
		""
		"The blueprint system lets you easily build your designs in survival. See the Ponder scenes for Blueprints and the Blueprint Cannon."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Blueprint Cannon Quests\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"6B151160907137A0\" } }"
	]
	quest.1E178EEB88CDD228.quest_subtitle: "\"Retired Mechanic's Retirement Life in Another World\""
	quest.1E178EEB88CDD228.title: "Explanation"
	quest.1E50A5A4F80B9E92.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click both Chain Drives in sequence with a Chain to link them."
	]
	quest.1E68F4F5A372D83C.quest_desc: [
		"Amethyst and ender pearls can be mixed into teleport powder without grinding."
	]
	quest.1E68F4F5A372D83C.title: "O1.2 Rough Machining"
	quest.1EBE33170D6B21D8.quest_desc: [
		"This logistics system only moves packages."
		""
		"Package delivery has auto pathfinding — you just need to hook all the nodes together with frogports."
		""
		"&cNote&f: The frogport itself doesn't add destination info to packages. Place a &eSign&7 (or Clipboard)&r on the Packager to set the destination address."
	]
	quest.1EBE33170D6B21D8.title: "3.11 Iron Chain Logistics"
	quest.1F5D746E88B94694.quest_desc: [
		"The core working component — using the Crushing Wheel as an example."
	]
	quest.1F5D746E88B94694.title: "Work"
	quest.1F9AD531D28B402C.quest_desc: [
		"Overcoming hardship makes you grow, but I won't force you to do this..."
		""
		"But kids who skip the grind can forget about quest rewards."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Related Extra Info\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"44E4DB19E314EABB\" } }"
	]
	quest.1F9AD531D28B402C.title: "H3.6.1 Skipping the Grind"
	quest.1FB862502EE9B3D4.quest_desc: [
		"Trains can also carry machinery, such as drills and steamrollers."
		""
		"I highly recommend putting a steamroller on your train — although thanks to Aeronautics' wonderful bugs, it will occasionally skip some blocks."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Curved train tracks have no collision box, so you can slip through and fall down."
	]
	quest.1FB862502EE9B3D4.title: "T1.3.2 Work Trains"
	quest.1FB8F3E6B3CE1FB4.quest_desc: [
		"This Package Frogport sits by the Crushing Wheel, so let's call it &eCrushing&r."
	]
	quest.1FF0F589C7990D81.quest_desc: [
		"You'll need to build Beacons with Cursed Gold Blocks later, so go stock up."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Items duplicated with the Jewelry Workbench come with Curse of Vanishing — washing it off yields 16 Cursed Gold."
	]
	quest.1FF0F589C7990D81.title: "AC1.13.1 Curse Me, Hurry Up!"
	quest.201AABAACD988B7C.quest_desc: [
		"Do you want me to repeat?"
	]
	quest.201AABAACD988B7C.title: "O3.11 Upgrade 2"
	quest.203380ED9BC38B15.quest_desc: [
		"Frost Metal is a relatively cheap alloy that upgrades Royal Steel weapons and tools."
		""
		"It can also craft some stronger talismans, and is one of the ingredients for multiphase materials."
	]
	quest.203380ED9BC38B15.title: "S2.2.8 Frost Metal Ingot"
	quest.20478B1B35E6429D.quest_desc: [
		"These crops grow quite differently from ordinary ones."
		""
		"Pumpkins & watermelons: seeds grow into &estems&r, and the stem tries to grow a fruit on an adjacent &eopen block&r. Break them with a &eMechanical Saw&r or &eMechanical Drill&r."
		""
		"Cocoa: must be planted on the side of &eJungle Logs&r. Harvest with a &eMechanical Harvester&r."
		""
		"Bamboo: plant on top of dirt/sand-like blocks; shoots and bamboo grow upward. Harvest with a &eMechanical Saw&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Sugarcane: plant on dirt/sand-like blocks &enext to water&r; grows up to 3 blocks tall. Harvest with a &eMechanical Saw&r."
		""
		"Kelp: plant underwater; grows upward without breaching the surface. Harvest with a &eMechanical Saw&r or &eMechanical Harvester&r."
		""
		"Cactus: plant on sand; grows up to 3 blocks. If any of the 4 blocks touching a cactus is solid, the cactus &ebreaks automatically&r."
		""
		"Apples: breaking Oak Leaves&7 (including Dark Oak Leaves)&r has a chance to drop them."
	]
	quest.20478B1B35E6429D.title: "F1.4 Special Crops"
	quest.2056328E74370A67.quest_desc: [
		"Drawers with customizable textures are a good thing"
	]
	quest.2056328E74370A67.title: "O3.4 Decorate It"
	quest.2057A20E7F0C1E8F.quest_desc: [
		"The Cages from Handcrafted can scoop up small creatures and carry them off — super handy."
		""
		"Pigs, cows, and sheep can't be picked up directly, but their babies can, so bring some feed and go."
	]
	quest.2057A20E7F0C1E8F.title: "O2.3 Capture Small Animals"
	quest.20B7FB68F5EAB7B3.quest_desc: [
		"Control the speed so that the items leave the processing area &7 (such as falling from the edge of the block) &r when they are processed, thus eliminating the need for sorting operations"
		""
		"&aTips&r: The rotation speed does not affect the efficiency of batch processing"
	]
	quest.20B7FB68F5EAB7B3.title: "H1.16 Speed Is Also an Art"
	quest.20D88DF956E243B9.quest_desc: [
		"Struck by lightning, an Iron Block becomes a Hollow Magnet. Use a Topaz to right-click a Lightning Rod and summon lightning."
	]
	quest.20D88DF956E243B9.quest_subtitle: "What a rough-and-ready crafting method!"
	quest.20D88DF956E243B9.title: "AC1.5 Magnet...?"
	quest.20F464BA72DB0D4E.quest_desc: [
		"Drive mobs&7 (mules, villagers, and horses recommended)&r onto the Millstone, and they'll keep turning it."
		""
		"Right-click with an item in hand, or use a Funnel to insert items."
		""
		"Use JEI&7 (EMI)&r to see all the Millstone's recipes."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Most recipes can also be handled by Create's Millstones or Crushing Wheels, which is more convenient."
	]
	quest.20F464BA72DB0D4E.title: "F3.5 Practical Kitchenware (4)"
	quest.20F6DBC3D5425C0E.quest_desc: [
		"A Storage Terminal gives connected containers a management interface."
		""
		"Usually attached to a Storage Connector, it also works great on Item Vaults."
		""
		"&aTips&r: In this pack, Storage Terminals work on dynamic contraptions&7 (needs Super Glue)&r."
	]
	quest.20F6DBC3D5425C0E.title: "O4.2 Only Needs to Be Applied Lightly"
	quest.2126752394BE9DCD.quest_desc: [
		"Kaleidoscope tavern also provides some decorative blocks, you can search &e@Kaleidoscope tavern&r with &eJEI&7 (EMI) &r to view them."
	]
	quest.2126752394BE9DCD.title: "F3.3.3 Decoration"
	quest.212D60A9905FE097.quest_desc: [
		"Frogports can hang packages on chains and also take packages off them."
		""
		"&cNote:&f The frogport itself doesn't add destination info to packages. Place a &eSign&7 (or Clipboard)&r on the Packager to set the destination address."
	]
	quest.212D60A9905FE097.title: "S2.12.7 Short-Distance Transport"
	quest.214357CF42EF2C0D.quest_desc: [
		"Lead — a heavy metal."
		""
		"With some research, it can surely be used to regenerate Netherite."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Fermented Spider Eyes need mushrooms — plant mushrooms on &eRich Soil&r to grow more of them."
		""
		"Or you can give them a boost with fertilizer."
	]
	quest.214357CF42EF2C0D.title: "S2.2.10 That's Alchemy Too!"
	quest.219BE29A5A5CC9AB.quest_subtitle: "This one's tricky to click — see the one above"
	quest.219BE29A5A5CC9AB.title: "Stress"
	quest.220B58C7BF98AD45.quest_desc: [
		"Automatically destroy items/fluids that exceed the storage limit"
	]
	quest.220B58C7BF98AD45.title: "O3.17 Say Goodbye to Overflow"
	quest.220BD2647ED0E33F.quest_desc: [
		"When facing upward, the Mechanical Saw can process some items&a①&r, such as stripping logs or sawing an Andesite Alloy into 6 Shafts."
		""
		"Of course, its real job is breaking blocks in place of an axe. What's special is that it can fell an entire tree in one go&7 (see the Ponder scene)&r, and it's also great on &edynamic contraptions&r&a②&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aNote ①&r: Worth noting that when an item has multiple processing recipes, the Mechanical Saw will cycle through them in order."
		""
		"That not only wastes resources, but can also &ecause lag&r. Luckily it has a filter slot, so you can filter for the recipe you want and avoid these problems."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aNote ②&r: The dynamic contraption quests unlock once you craft Super Glue, but you can just make it yourself."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Prerequisite Quest Guide\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"4A218D10EEB4096E\" } }"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Rotating tree farm diagram:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/s1_7_3.png width:256 height:142 align:center}"
	]
	quest.220BD2647ED0E33F.title: "S1.7.3 Dangerous Machines in the Workshop"
	quest.221F781E3AA472E6.quest_desc: [
		"Same as before: stick the Packager next to the warehouse, then put down a Package Frogport."
	]
	quest.226935413D16F11F.quest_subtitle: "Euphemistically: Herbal Essence"
	quest.226935413D16F11F.title: "HS5.4.3.3 Nether Wart"
	quest.2281917373F10D54.quest_desc: [
		"After binding, use it to teleport to the bound Waystone."
		""
		"Taking damage during the teleport still interrupts it."
	]
	quest.2281917373F10D54.title: "OS1.3.3 Bound Scroll"
	quest.22847E52B5242373.quest_desc: [
		"You no longer need a Mechanical Crafter to make Granite — a Mixer can handle it."
		""
		"Still, a single Mixer isn't fast enough. For efficiency, you'll want a stacked design&8 — if you care about speed."
	]
	quest.22847E52B5242373.title: "H3.6 Granite"
	quest.2298ABEC00E545E7.title: "Tungsten, Titanium, Tin, Silver, Lead"
	quest.22DF702CDA6EC855.quest_desc: [
		"Small and nimble, Command Robots are a great help for operating redstone circuits by hand."
		""
		"They can't place or break blocks, but they can flip buttons and levers — which is already plenty useful!"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Use &eRobot Channels&r to give them dedicated fast lanes."
	]
	quest.22DF702CDA6EC855.title: "T1.2.2 Command Robots"
	quest.22F6493780CA5E18.quest_desc: [
		"Mesh Cinerite to get Lapis Lazuli."
	]
	quest.22F6493780CA5E18.title: "Mesh"
	quest.2311F440D9DD1D20.quest_desc: [
		"By controlling the angle of attack of &ehorizontally&r placed &eSymmetric Sails&r&7 (best kept under 30°)&r, you can generate lift in different directions, giving you &epitch control&r."
		""
		"Similarly, controlling &evertically&r placed Symmetric Sails adjusts your &edirection of travel&r."
		""
		"For large, slow physical structures, differential speed control works even better:"
		""
		"Place the power sources&7 (propellers)&r on both sides of the structure; running them at different speeds makes the structure turn toward the &eslower&r side."
	]
	quest.2311F440D9DD1D20.title: "Directional Control"
	quest.23636E72D5D35C87.quest_desc: [
		"Factory Gauges enable automated production and restocking."
		""
		"&7For automatic, high-volume material requests, you'll still want the Wireless Redstone + Redstone Requester combo."
	]
	quest.23636E72D5D35C87.title: "4.10 Smart Factory"
	quest.23D39D0E1647207D.quest_desc: [
		"Wild flax now spawns along rivers, and breaking it drops seeds that steadily supply you with thread."
	]
	quest.23D39D0E1647207D.title: "O2.1 Find Flax Seeds"
	quest.248EE09D0CD9A24D.quest_desc: [
		"Crush Blocks of Amethyst to recover Amethyst."
		""
		"A Cutting Board works too."
	]
	quest.248EE09D0CD9A24D.title: "Crushing Amethyst Blocks"
	quest.249AC0661E558EED.quest_desc: [
		"Crushing Wheels can crush raw ore, &eincreasing your mineral yield&r."
		""
		"Crushing Wheels can also perform &7most&r Millstone recipes in bulk."
		""
		"&aTips&f: Can't tell which way it's spinning? Try lowering the speed a bit."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"From here on, your machines will take up a lot more space, so it's time to build a factory."
		""
		"Building a factory requires the following steps:"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Flattening Land (Quest Series)\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"78627F8BDF656AC6\" } }"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Logistics & Stress (Diagram)\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"5329D3AD8C264AAE\" } }"
		""
		"[&aOptional&r] Casing: wrap up your machines&7 (or the whole factory)&r. If you can't see it, the render load drops noticeably&7 (in plain terms: no more lag)&r."
	]
	quest.249AC0661E558EED.title: "2.9 Which Way Is It Turning!"
	quest.252895B7179244B7.quest_desc: [
		"These two building tools need a &eMechanical Crafter&r to make, but both are great — I recommend getting one."
		""
		"How to use the &eBlock Placer&r:"
		""
		"&eLeft-click&r to select a block, &eRight-click&r to place it, &eShift+Right-click&r to open the config panel."
	]
	quest.252895B7179244B7.quest_subtitle: "Architectural Wonder"
	quest.252895B7179244B7.title: "S2.4.1 Handheld Block Placer"
	quest.25329C2F777F8256.quest_desc: [
		"Combined with the Void Energy Collector, it can produce a lot of electricity"
	]
	quest.25329C2F777F8256.title: "AC1.21.5 Void Matter"
	quest.255E0ED975E37262.quest_desc: [
		"The journey of Create also starts from collecting starting resources."
		""
		"Like most MC starts, let’s collect some wood first."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Originally, I planned to give a lantern that could be hung on the waist, but... due to various reasons, it was not possible to hang it on the waist and light up QAQ"
	]
	quest.255E0ED975E37262.title: "1.1 To Get Rich, Punch Trees First!"
	quest.2562BB5024D041D5.quest_desc: [
		"Use Table Cloths to set up your mechanically powered shop, and there are no refunds even if the goods are not delivered!"
		""
		"&8Ah, it seems... there aren't many customers..."
	]
	quest.2562BB5024D041D5.title: "S3.10.1 \"I Open a Store in MC\""
	quest.259C2614E8FE14AE.quest_desc: [
		"Boilers can produce enormous amounts of stress for you to use freely. For a long time, you won't need to worry about stress."
		""
		"That means you can afford a little luxury: generating electricity."
		""
		"This electricity can power &eAnvilCraft&r machines, such as the Heater."
		""
		"It processes an entire stack of ores instantly and doubles the output."
		""
		"Check its Ponder scene to learn how to use it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"AnvilCraft's machines are more fragmented than Create's, and most can't run on their own. This places &zextremely high demands&a①&r on your redstone skills."
		""
		"No need to go down the AnvilCraft rabbit hole though — this is a Create modpack, after all. Diving deep into multi-mod combos takes real effort. If you don't enjoy this part, feel free to skip AnvilCraft entirely — it has no impact on anything else."
		""
		"&a①&r Extremely high demands: relative to Create."
	]
	quest.259C2614E8FE14AE.quest_subtitle: "&cStudying cross-mod synergies takes real effort — please pace yourself"
	quest.259C2614E8FE14AE.title: "S2.1.1 Power Generation"
	quest.25C40E93F22FDAC6.quest_desc: [
		"It's listed here to tell you not to bother — Create already handles bulk processing anyway."
	]
	quest.25C40E93F22FDAC6.title: "O2.19 Don't Make It"
	quest.25F2421EDCDE70CE.quest_desc: [
		"When an anvil strikes a Piezoelectric Crystal, it generates electricity. The Current Collector gathers it, and power poles carry it to your appliances."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Click for the Pulse Generator manual\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://www.mcmod.cn/item/884568.html\" } }"
	]
	quest.25F2421EDCDE70CE.title: "AC1.7 Power Generation"
	quest.263229837952BEAC.quest_desc: [
		"The Minecart Assembler is seriously overpowered — you can use it to move tons of blocks quickly&7 (like a bunch of Item Vaults)&r."
		""
		"For now, putting Mechanical Drills on a minecart contraption may not be the best idea, since the track can't extend itself..."
		""
		"But the two &eDeployers&r I gave you are enough to auto-lay track and keep the minecart contraption going."
		""
		"And don't forget to use the &eMechanical Plough&r to pick up the rails!"
		""
		"&aTips:&r Feed a &eMinecart&r a piece of Coal and it'll run for ages — cheap, sturdy, and reliable."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Shuttling the minecart back and forth over a short stretch makes the machines on its contraption work at ridiculous speeds."
		""
		"This trick is called the &eShaking Minecart&f — catchy name, works great, but I'm not teaching it&7 (there's a reason, oao)&f."
		""
		"Go find a tutorial if you want to learn."
	]
	quest.263229837952BEAC.title: "S1.7.8 Thomas the Tank Engine Gets Rolling!"
	quest.26737A5660E83B28.quest_desc: [
		"Burn fuel to fly fast. Here's how to operate it:"
		""
		"&aSpacebar&r: Start the engine / increase engine power"
		""
		"&aLeft Shift&r: Shut down the engine / decrease engine power"
		""
		"&aW key&r: Push the control stick&7 (nose down)"
		""
		"&aS key&r: Pull the control stick&7 (nose up)"
		""
		"Take off once your ground speed is high enough."
		""
		"OK, you know how to fly a plane now. Go have fun!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{ \"text\": \"Biplane Flight Guide — By Vanilla\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://www.mcmod.cn/post/3942.html\" } }"
		""
		"&cBiplanes are tricky to take off and land; one mistake and it's crash-and-burn."
		""
		"&aRunway design:"
		""
		"Biplanes need a runway for takeoff and landing."
		""
		"Without upgrades, to reach the needed takeoff speed, the runway should be about &e60 meters&7 (1 meter = 1 block in-game, same below)&r long and about &e7 meters&r wide."
		""
		"It's recommended to place light sources along both sides and down the middle of the runway so it's visible at night."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aFlight — final preparations before takeoff"
		""
		"Before taking off, run through these checks:"
		""
		"Fuel: flying the biplane burns &ea lot of fuel&r, so estimate how much you need for the trip&7 (default fuels: coal, Blaze Powder, and anything a Furnace accepts)&r."
		""
		"Weapons: &eDon't&r load weapons into the weapon slot before takeoff, to avoid accidents."
		""
		"Food and other essentials."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aTakeoff"
		""
		"The plane needs no fuel while taxiing, and even with the engine running it won't taxi any faster. So &edon't start the engine until you're lined up with the runway centerline&r."
		""
		"Once lined up, crank the engine to full power, but &edon't pull the control stick&r yet — otherwise the tail will scrape the ground."
		""
		"When you're &eat least 5 meters&r off the ground, you can ease the stick back a little — but don't pitch up too far&7 (keep it within about 40°)&r, or the plane will stall."
		""
		"&aUpgrade modules that shorten the takeoff run:"
		""
		"Nether Engines, Steel Boilers, Reinforced Pipes, Improved Landing Gear"
		""
		"&aTips&r: You can also use an Encased Fan to blow the plane up to takeoff speed"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aCruising"
		""
		"Once you reach cruising altitude, nudge the stick forward to level the nose out closer to the horizon."
		""
		"While cruising, keep an eye on and adjust the nose angle. You can adjust the pitch to control flight speed&c (remember: don't adjust speed via engine power unless you really have to)&r."
		""
		"In flight, the plane will &edrift off course in the wind&r, so keep watching your heading or install the upgrade module&7 (gyroscope)&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aLanding"
		""
		"Before reaching your destination, descend early, adjust your attitude, and line up with the runway."
		""
		"When entering the runway, the nose-down angle shouldn't exceed 10°, or the plane may crash."
		""
		"Since this mod's planes have no brakes, cut the engine before entering the runway and let inertia carry you in, while fine-tuning the nose angle."
		""
		"If you're coming in too fast, pull the stick back immediately&7 (nose up, accelerating)&r, go around, and re-enter the runway."
		""
		"Once the plane has slowed down and rolled out on the runway, get off it right away."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aRemoval"
		""
		"Hitting the plane&7 (or other aircraft)&r with melee attacks will eventually turn it into an item drop. Items in the plane's inventory scatter across the world, while items in the fuel and upgrade slots are kept as data inside the dropped plane."
		""
		"&aRepair"
		""
		"If the plane's health&7 (the wrench-like icon)&r isn't full, you can repair it by holding right-click while not riding it. This takes priority over mounting, so you'll have to fully repair the vehicle before you can board it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aOther notes"
		""
		"Adjust your &erender distance&r"
		""
		"The biplane's top speed is fairly high, so crank the render distance as high as you can and make attitude adjustments early. If the server limits client render distance, use something like a minimap mod to gauge terrain and chunk loading ahead of time. If you fly into unloaded&7 (or unrendered)&r chunks at speed, wait a bit or relog."
		""
		"&aServer"
		""
		"On a server&7 (dedicated server)&r, if a player disconnects mid-flight, the plane's engine will be set to off when they rejoin. The plane won't fall out of the sky though — it keeps the attitude and state it had on exit."
	]
	quest.26737A5660E83B28.quest_subtitle: "Read the manual first"
	quest.26737A5660E83B28.title: "O5.2 Map-Exploring Marvel"
	quest.2674DC9309EDD25F.quest_desc: [
		"These special stones often generate in huge amounts underground; crushing them yields the corresponding ore."
		""
		"Use a Prospector Pickaxe to locate them quickly."
	]
	quest.2674DC9309EDD25F.title: "Massive Ore Veins"
	quest.26A47109D96AD5A7.title: "AC1.26 Beyond the Limit!"
	quest.26A7CB7354874119.quest_desc: [
		"These special stones often generate in huge amounts underground; crushing them yields the corresponding ore."
		""
		"Use a Prospector Pickaxe to locate them quickly."
	]
	quest.26A7CB7354874119.title: "Massive Ore Veins"
	quest.26BEAF09440ADDAF.quest_desc: [
		"Yes, it counts, bro. It counts."
		""
		"Any container can be linked into a whole with Storage Connectors — just attach a Funnel to the connector to export the cobblestone in time."
	]
	quest.26BEAF09440ADDAF.title: "S2.11.4 Does the Chute Count as a Container?"
	quest.2709CC4F17953FB8.quest_desc: [
		"The later stages of AnvilCraft demand a mountain of emeralds, so having a Trading Depot collect them automatically is a real time-saver."
		""
		"&aTips&r: When playing with AnvilCraft, don't forget Create's Ponder scenes!"
	]
	quest.2709CC4F17953FB8.title: "AC1.9.3 Automated Trading"
	quest.2779FF4D8283A9C8.quest_desc: [
		"&eRedstone signal output direction&r follows the way the hopper's redstone torch points"
		""
		"&eItem output direction&r is the thicker side"
	]
	quest.2779FF4D8283A9C8.title: "O4.16 Comparator and Funnel"
	quest.2790065D5F10ED8D.quest_desc: [
		"The magnet pulls any anvil within the 5 blocks below it up to its own position. It stops working when it receives a redstone signal, letting you raise anvils automatically."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Hollow magnets can't conduct redstone signals, but the other two kinds can."
	]
	quest.2790065D5F10ED8D.title: "AC1.6 Hey, Magnet"
	quest.27A36CE2AB72F808.quest_desc: [
		"&eAndesite&r can be obtained by &eCompacting&r Flint."
		""
		"[ \"You can also use a \", { \"text\": \"Melt Gem Cobblestone Generator\", \"color\":blue, \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"44E4DB19E314EABB\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.27A36CE2AB72F808.title: "Compacting"
	quest.27A7F173EAB82EF0.quest_desc: [
		"Conveyor belts can also transmit stress in a straight line — but along the plane perpendicular to the Shaft."
		""
		"Hold a conveyor belt&7 (the item)&r and &eright-click&r a conveyor belt&7 (the block)&r to extend it."
		""
		"Use a Wrench to &eright-click&r the belt&7 (block)&r to shorten it; &eShift&r + &eright-click&r removes it."
	]
	quest.27A7F173EAB82EF0.quest_subtitle: "Just a random subtitle, so no one says I'm bullying conveyor belts"
	quest.27C0C1D582764952.quest_desc: [
		"Postboxes hook Create 6.0's new logistics system into the rail network, making long-distance automated delivery a reality."
		""
		"&aTips&r: The destination address is decided by the Packager, not the postbox."
	]
	quest.27C0C1D582764952.title: "T1.3.4 Mailing You Later"
	quest.27DE7AD859F9FDCC.quest_desc: [
		"Many foods grant powerful potion effects, and sitting down to a full banquet can keep them going for up to 30 minutes."
		""
		"Once you're full, of course you should go out and stretch your legs, right?"
	]
	quest.27DE7AD859F9FDCC.title: "F4.2 Kung Fu Is No Match for a Cleaver"
	quest.27E288909A98C7B1.quest_desc: [
		"&eThe Deployer's power is absolute!&r You'll come to realize that sooner or later."
		""
		"For example, a Deployer can process rose quartz at a speed that would make Steve's head spin."
		""
		"You should already have worked with the Deployer in the earlier side chapters. When you hit a tricky problem later on, see if it can solve it for you too."
	]
	quest.27E288909A98C7B1.quest_subtitle: "This route is an important side branch"
	quest.27E288909A98C7B1.title: "2.4 Deployer"
	quest.27F40A9EF4C57BD7.quest_desc: [
		"Plutonium's main use is generating power, so whether to make it is up to you."
	]
	quest.27F40A9EF4C57BD7.quest_subtitle: "Perhaps a bit too green-skinned"
	quest.27F40A9EF4C57BD7.title: "AC1.23.1 I Reckon It'll Work"
	quest.285BF1D72C2DE4F8.quest_desc: [
		"&eAndesite Alloy&r changed the world. This magical, cheap material is perfect for power transmission — it's the cornerstone of Create."
		""
		"&aTips:&f Click an item in the task goals to see how to get it."
		""
		"Both Iron Nuggets and Zinc Nuggets work for making Andesite Alloy; using a &eMechanical Mixer&r makes it even cheaper."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"I highly recommend finding a flat area for your base."
		""
		"Also, press &eF4&r to leave your body and scout underground to see if you like what's down there —"
		""
		"The ideal spot has &eflat ground&r on top and &emagma&r underneath."
		""
		"&7With the current world-gen settings, these two conditions shouldn't be too hard to meet&r"
	]
	quest.285BF1D72C2DE4F8.quest_subtitle: "Worth celebrating!"
	quest.285BF1D72C2DE4F8.title: "1.4 Start Create!"
	quest.289A567623689A49.quest_desc: [
		"The toolbox has 8 slots, each holding up to 4 stacks, and the contents stay inside when the block is broken."
		""
		"But that's not why it's here —"
		""
		"After you take everything out of a slot, the slot still shows 0 of that item and &ewon't accept anything else&r. Pair it with a funnel to sort out exactly what you need."
	]
	quest.289A567623689A49.title: "H1.10 Sorting"
	quest.28FCAC7113DE7F60.quest_desc: [
		"You may have noticed a drawback of the Threshold Switch:"
		""
		"When processing small batches, if you end up with fewer than 64 items, they won't be sent back to the warehouse automatically — they just pile up in the small buffer storage."
		""
		"There are plenty of workarounds, like setting up a pulse signal that fires once a minute."
		""
		"There are many ways to make a pulse signal: you can use Create's, AnvilCraft's&8, or a vanilla one."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"AnvilCraft has no Ponder scenes, so you'll need to consult the MCMOD wiki a lot, or go stalk xekr's Bilibili account"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/pulse_generator.png width:185 height:75 align:center}"
	]
	quest.28FCAC7113DE7F60.title: "Convenient Loop Activation"
	quest.293526A9C14D5E7B.quest_desc: [
		"Take the cobblestone you've collected to the Crushing Wheel!"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"For high-volume transport, see the Logistics topic\", \"underlined\": true,\"color\":\"blue\",\"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"10D8C7654C651BEB\" } }"
	]
	quest.293526A9C14D5E7B.quest_subtitle: "Cobblestone?&e[Crush]&r?>Gravel?[Wash]?>Iron Nuggets"
	quest.293526A9C14D5E7B.title: "2.12 Cobblestone"
	quest.2939B3D6F6D626F5.quest_desc: [
		"Functional Storage adds many drawers. Their shared traits:"
		""
		"Hold &ehuge stacks of a single item type&r"
		""
		"Keep their &estored items when broken&r"
	]
	quest.2939B3D6F6D626F5.title: "O3.1 Join the Drawer Cult"
	quest.295B5425E0E67AAA.quest_desc: [
		"Facing ever more complex material demands, you might want to start building a logistics center — make it impressive, so nobody looks down on us."
		""
		"Create 6.0 adds a whole new logistics system. Place a &ePackager&r next to the barrel holding charcoal over by the boiler, then attach a &eFactory Gauge&r and a &eStock Link&r to the Packager."
		""
		"Right-click the gauge with charcoal to set how much charcoal you want to keep here."
		""
		"When the stock drops below that amount, the gauge automatically requests charcoal from the storage network through the Stock Link. All you need to do is set up the logistics route that carries charcoal to the boiler."
	]
	quest.295B5425E0E67AAA.title: "H2.9 Logistics Center"
	quest.2970DBA86BE9E560.quest_desc: [
		"When a Hose Pulley draws water or lava, the source counts as infinite if the connected fluid exceeds &e10,000 blocks&7 (lava lakes usually qualify)&r."
		""
		"&eThe Nether&7 (Hell)&r is a great lava source, and there are plenty of ways to move items across dimensions — by &etrain&r, or by shipping &edropped items&7 (lava buckets, fluid drawers)&r."
		""
		"You could also dig a very deep pool and pour 10,000 buckets of lava into it for infinite lava."
		""
		"&aTips&f: If you drain water or lava into a pool that's already connected to more than 10,000 blocks of water or lava, the excess beyond 10,000 blocks will be destroyed."
	]
	quest.2970DBA86BE9E560.title: "S2.6.3 My Magma Is Endless"
	quest.2991185EF14A4AC6.quest_desc: [
		"As you can see, the Void Energy Collector produces ice, which turns into water when broken..."
		""
		"...and water seriously hurts the Collector's efficiency!"
		""
		"Regular sponges are way too much trouble — try a Menger Sponge, which can absorb water indefinitely."
	]
	quest.2991185EF14A4AC6.quest_subtitle: "Sponge Pro Plus Super Max Ultra"
	quest.2991185EF14A4AC6.title: "AC1.10.3 Menger Sponge"
	quest.299541DBC10244DF.quest_desc: [
		"The Canner lets you plug fluids into your Chain Conveyor logistics network, so you can feed water and lava to plenty of recipes. Nice."
		""
		"&8This mod is full of bugs, and all sorts of weird things can happen while using it. If you hit a bug, don't doubt yourself — it's definitely the mod's fault."
	]
	quest.299541DBC10244DF.quest_subtitle: "&m[WIP]&r [R.I.P.]"
	quest.299541DBC10244DF.title: "S3.11.1 Transport Fluids"
	quest.29CD73BC72280746.quest_desc: [
		"As long as it's covered in wool or sails, it can spin — no matter what the sails look like, whether there's wind or not, and it can even go through walls. Wow!"
		""
		"&aTips:&f Every 8 wool blocks or sails raises the windmill's level by one, producing more stress and increasing the speed."
	]
	quest.29CD73BC72280746.title: "S1.6.2 How Does It Spin?"
	quest.29CED57CCD52EBA9.quest_desc: [
		"Create's built-in fluid system is honestly pretty clunky to use, which is why the add-on &eCreate: Fluid&r exists to enhance it."
		""
		"This is optional content. It's genuinely very convenient, but later quests will mostly avoid referencing it — this is a tutorial pack, after all."
		""
		"Think of it as a shortcut for you self-learners :)"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Search \"&e@fluid&r\" to see everything this mod adds."
	]
	quest.29CED57CCD52EBA9.title: "S2.2.3 Fluid Expansion"
	quest.2A16BAB2FA4BDCDA.quest_desc: [
		"Hold &ethe mouse's side button&r to zoom in on distant scenes; use &ethe scroll wheel&r to zoom even further."
		""
		"You can also press &eF4&r to use the \"&eout-of-body&r\" mode and fly around freely to look at your surroundings. Your body stays where it is, though, so keep it safe!"
		""
		"&aTips:&r You can rebind these keys under \"&eMenu/Options/Controls/Key Binds&r\". Search for \"&ecategory:zoom&r\" and \"&ecategory:free&r\" to find them."
	]
	quest.2A16BAB2FA4BDCDA.title: "Zoom and Out-of-Body Experiences"
	quest.2A1B1E298D4199F0.quest_desc: [
		"A Display Link can be connected to a sign to automatically update the Packager's package info."
		""
		"It's fairly complex and can't be explained in a few words, so it isn't required — just mentioned in passing."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"See the video attached at the end of page 3 of this quest\", \"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"10F6FE7BC7406958\" } }"
	]
	quest.2A1B1E298D4199F0.title: "Sequenced Assembly"
	quest.2A5739CB5A0810FC.quest_desc: [
		"The Weighted Ejector can have a launch condition set. Set it to exactly 64 and wheat flour will be launched as full stacks, improving efficiency."
	]
	quest.2A5739CB5A0810FC.title: "H1.14 Washing in Groups"
	quest.2A7D0A1068318A17.quest_desc: [
		"Your energy is limited, so if you have any left over while designing, set up some auxiliary equipment, such as:"
		""
		"&eGyroscopes&7 (machine parts that automatically keep the physical structure's attitude balanced)&r, &eauto-cruise&r, and &eauto-docking&r."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Feeling lost, or even totally stuck, is completely normal."
		""
		"I can't really explain the specifics in words, so I recommend looking up some tutorials on Bilibili."
	]
	quest.2A7D0A1068318A17.title: "Automatic Control"
	quest.2A888276660446A8.quest_desc: [
		"This precious alloy is refined from Netherite and has even more outrageous performance."
		""
		"It's crafted by &emixing&r."
	]
	quest.2A888276660446A8.title: "H5.4 Ember Metal"
	quest.2AAE35B64CECB620.quest_desc: [
		"Suitable for large-scale collection and easy to carry on your body."
		"But absolutely! Absolutely! Never bring a magnet into a production line with falling items!"
	]
	quest.2AAE35B64CECB620.title: "O2.24 Handy, but Mind the Range"
	quest.2B0869C99B04EB5A.quest_desc: [
		"Give the Packager a redstone signal, and once the Crushing Wheels finish and the products enter the small buffer storage, they'll be packaged right away and sent back to your main warehouse by Package Frogports and Chain Conveyors."
	]
	quest.2B0869C99B04EB5A.title: "Activation"
	quest.2B1328EF1C25F8D4.quest_desc: [
		"Pushing the magnet back and forth builds up charges on the copper blocks on either side, which are then gathered by a Charge Collector."
		""
		"Copper blocks can't be waxed, so you'll need to de-rust them by hand every so often... or with a Deployer?"
	]
	quest.2B1328EF1C25F8D4.quest_subtitle: "What is this...cutting magnetic field lines?"
	quest.2B1328EF1C25F8D4.title: "AC1.7.2 Another Way to Generate Power"
	quest.2B76BD6A425C92B7.quest_desc: [
		"Mix gems into Melt Gem, then Time Warp it to get the corresponding gem block."
	]
	quest.2B76BD6A425C92B7.title: "Time Warp"
	quest.2B97BCEBEDDF02E1.quest_desc: [
		"Some recipes need huge quantities — use hoppers to feed and collect materials so the machine can stockpile them ahead of time, saving you the boring wait."
	]
	quest.2B97BCEBEDDF02E1.title: "Batch Processing"
	quest.2BA5FD303D178FA5.quest_desc: [
		"You can use various interfaces to exchange items between the train and its stations."
		""
		"Cover the interfaces with camouflaged trapdoors to keep the train looking clean."
		""
		"&aTips&r: When a train has fuel, it will burn some of it to accelerate."
	]
	quest.2BA5FD303D178FA5.title: "T1.3.3 Transport Cars"
	quest.2C1301A9907AB057.quest_desc: [
		"Trial rooms spawn scattered around &ethe outer End islands&r. Clear one to earn a key that opens a Vault."
		""
		"Gear up before you go — they're no pushover. Probably."
		""
		"&aTips&r:"
		"Once you've got your first key, you can use a &eJewel Crafting Table&r to duplicate&7 (forge)&r more keys."
		""
		"Vaults can be opened again and again: place a &eBlock of Lead&r on the Vault and drop an &eanvil&r onto it to open it once more."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"How to make lead\", \"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"214357CF42EF2C0D\" } }"
		""
		"&7Due to some odd performance issues, small structures are used for now instead of full Trial Chambers"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"With &eBad Omen&r, the challenge becomes &charder&7 (seriously)&r, but unlocks higher-tier Vaults."
		""
		"Opening the Vault with &eLuck&r yields more and better loot."
		""
		"&7All the good stuff is in the Ominous Vaults — don't forget the rum!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Because of performance issues, dungeon generation is set to mostly create dead ends."
		""
		"Under extreme conditions, there's still a tiny chance of generating a bigger dungeon — I'd written the code and couldn't bear to delete it, so I just set the probability very low."
		""
		"If you find one, treat it as an easter egg. Surely spawning a slightly bigger dungeon now and then won't seriously hurt performance... right?"
		""
		"I'm still a beginner at terrain generation, so feedback is welcome. Please bear with me if anything's off — orz"
	]
	quest.2C1301A9907AB057.title: "S2.17.4 Trial"
	quest.2C6BE589450E6334.quest_desc: [
		"Charge an Iron Ingot to get a Magnet Ingot."
	]
	quest.2CE821475BC7BFE8.quest_desc: [
		"Hold the tilde key \"&e~&r\"&7 (barring remaps, it's at the top-left of your keyboard, the first key below Esc)&r to activate Vein Mining. Once active, its status indicator shows in the &etop-left corner&r of your screen."
		""
		"While holding \"&e~&r\", also hold \"&eShift&r\" and scroll the &emouse wheel&r to switch mining modes."
		""
		"Mined the wrong thing? Press &eCtrl&f+&eZ&r to undo&7 (remembers only the last action)&r."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Vein Mining drains hunger and tool durability fast."
	]
	quest.2CE821475BC7BFE8.title: "Vein Mining"
	quest.2D2B3FC617173A73.quest_desc: [
		"These colorful stones generate in huge patches — massive reserves that are easy to mine at scale."
		""
		"Crush them and you can extract minerals from them. That's thousands of mineral ingots!"
		""
		"For now, though, we lack the right tools to crush them. Still, they're worth marking on your map for later."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Prospector's Pick is a diamond pick with extras: right-click to prospect for underground minerals. It pairs great with the &evertical mining machine&r&7 (taught later)&r."
		""
		"The Prospector's Pick has no crafting recipe — but you can repair it with diamonds."
		""
		"It can also be enchanted, just not at an enchanting table. Use an anvil and enchanted books if needed."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Use the Royal Grindstone to clear enchantment repair costs."
	]
	quest.2D2B3FC617173A73.quest_subtitle: "These are side quests — no rush!"
	quest.2D2B3FC617173A73.title: "S1.3.1 Beautiful Stones"
	quest.2D902F1562969306.quest_desc: [
		"Sharestones don't need to be activated — just place one down and you can teleport to other Sharestones of the same color, which is super handy on multiplayer servers."
		""
		"Unfortunately, &eWarp Stones&r and &eWarp Scrolls&r can't select Sharestones as their destination."
	]
	quest.2D902F1562969306.title: "O1.5 Sharestone"
	quest.2DB0E7C25A47D08B.quest_desc: [
		"Bake the dough and it turns into delicious bread!"
		""
		"Dough is sticky — maybe it can replace slime balls?"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Making bread with an Encased Fan needs &ebulk smoking&r — don't use bulk smelting, or you won't even get any ash back."
	]
	quest.2DB0E7C25A47D08B.title: "S1.7.15 Born From the Basin"
	quest.2DF84A43EDC96F48.quest_desc: [
		"The warped forest in the Nether is crawling with Endermen, so pass by and borrow some pearls from them :P"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Pearls now have a renewable recycling recipe, so once you've got one batch you can head back."
	]
	quest.2DF84A43EDC96F48.title: "S1.8.1 Visiting the Endermen"
	quest.2E0C0A656AA1908A.quest_desc: [
		"Create demands a lot of mineral resources, so it's recommended to take every ore you mine."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Sophisticated Backpacks can be upgraded for more storage space and more upgrade slots."
	]
	quest.2E0C0A656AA1908A.quest_subtitle: "Cheer! Best Miner!"
	quest.2E0C0A656AA1908A.title: "1.3 Important Supplies"
	quest.2E1A5D104F1CDD40.quest_desc: [
		"Washing soul sand can also yield gold nuggets — but the chance is way too low."
		""
		"What we mainly need here is quartz."
	]
	quest.2E1A5D104F1CDD40.title: "H3.4 Washing Soul Sand"
	quest.2E4F470968849D44.quest_desc: [
		"What's underneath the bedrock? In AnvilCraft, there are endless minerals down there!"
		""
		"Place an Impact Pile on bedrock and smash it with an anvil that &efell 20 blocks&r to make minerals gush forth."
		""
		"Lasers of level 4 and above can mine remotely&7 (128 blocks)&r and automatically drop the minerals into a container behind them."
		""
		"&aTips&r: The tutorial book has the specific instructions."
	]
	quest.2E4F470968849D44.title: "AC1.10.1 Infinite Ore"
	quest.2E6C68D190D2979E.quest_desc: [
		"If your vehicle is light enough, you can use a dispersion net to push it off the ground and hover."
		""
		"In practice, the Encased Fan's thrust isn't that strong, so hovercrafts aren't very practical."
		""
		"But they look awesome!"
	]
	quest.2E6C68D190D2979E.title: "Levitating Near the Earth"
	quest.2E6EB86ED33799FF.quest_desc: [
		"Sorting in the Andesite Age is a hassle, but you're not out of options:"
		""
		"The Toolbox is a great example —"
		""
		"A slot stays occupied even when its item count is 0, until you clear it manually."
	]
	quest.2E6EB86ED33799FF.title: "S1.7.18 Toolbox Filter"
	quest.2E7B2277B916B1B9.quest_desc: [
		"Crush cobblestone twice to get sand."
		""
		"You can route the intermediate product&8 (gravel)&r back into the Crushing Wheels, or arrange the Crushing Wheels in an &eL shape&r so that three wheels form two crushing stages in a row."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Diagram:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/h3_2.png width:256 height:142 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2E7B2277B916B1B9.title: "H3.2 Twice Crushed"
	quest.2E816548D1DE0868.quest_desc: [
		"The two new components Create adds for interacting with containers are the cornerstone of early logistics."
		""
		"&aTips&r: You can attach multiple funnels to one container to gather&7 (or split evenly)&r items."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If you don't have kelp, craft a few &eSeeds Packs&r and use seed oil mixed with coal dust to make dried kelp."
		""
		"You can also cut conveyor belts on a &eCutting Board&r to recover some of the dried kelp."
	]
	quest.2E816548D1DE0868.title: "3.1 Interacting with Containers"
	quest.2EA20C058E731DB4.quest_desc: [
		"This marvellous template is commonly found in Nether chests. It lets your Blaze take up the mantle of enchanting power ()"
	]
	quest.2EA20C058E731DB4.title: "E1.6 Blaze Class Change"
	quest.2ECF3D88C2366928.quest_desc: [
		"Do you know how to build a Creeper farm?"
	]
	quest.2ECF3D88C2366928.title: "Creeper Drops"
	quest.2EF4CFFEACC11C2C.quest_desc: [
		"Resurrection Soil is the Nether version of Rich Soil, obtained by \"forgetting\" Soul-Forgetting Compost placed in the Nether."
		""
		"\"Forgetting\" is sped up when there are &eopen flames&7 (working furnaces, lit candles, etc.)&r, &elava&r, or &eactivators&7 (Twisting Vines, Weeping Vines, mushrooms and fungi of all kinds, Nether Wart, Soul Sand, Bone Blocks, Wither Roses, Resurrection Rich Soil, Soul-Forgetting Compost)&r nearby."
		""
		"Nether Wart grows faster on Resurrection Rich Soil."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Resurrection Soil farmland is the Nether version of Rich Soil farmland, and grows crops just like Rich Soil."
		""
		"It must be &emoistened&7 (even visually, the \"moistening\" here is really \"ignition\")&r by &eopen flames&7 (fire, lava, torches, lanterns, campfires, stoves, bomb peppers, etc.)&r instead of water."
		""
		"Each open flame moistens the Resurrection Rich Soil farmland in a &e17×9×17&r area centered on itself."
		""
		"Moist Resurrection Rich Soil farmland has a light level of 10, bright enough for most crops to grow."
	]
	quest.2EF4CFFEACC11C2C.title: "F1.9 Fertile Soil Plus"
	quest.2EF9EAC427C522C0.quest_desc: [
		"Using these two Dripping Upgrades can replace the pointed dripstone cauldron setup, letting you shrink the boiler."
		""
		"&8Think about what else they can be used for?"
	]
	quest.2EF9EAC427C522C0.title: "S2.6.5 Integrated Renewable Water & Magma"
	quest.2F48103BD793ACB9.quest_desc: [
		"These ores are added by AnvilCraft and can be obtained by &espout-filling&r them with different potions."
	]
	quest.2F48103BD793ACB9.title: "Alchemy"
	quest.2F616531E63466F0.quest_desc: [
		"Chain Conveyors can be connected to each other quite freely — they transmit stress while also delivering items, which is super handy."
		""
		"It's recommended to build them up high&7 (and keep the area around the line clear)&r, like a cable car, which makes transporting players easier."
	]
	quest.2F616531E63466F0.quest_subtitle: "Flying Wire Expert"
	quest.2F616531E63466F0.title: "Chain Conveyor"
	quest.2FA08CE65CF0CC0F.quest_desc: [
		"Tungsten withstands heat just as well as Netherite."
		""
		"We're getting close to mass-producing Netherite."
	]
	quest.2FA08CE65CF0CC0F.title: "S2.2.11 Lead to Tungsten"
	quest.2FCA2FED5704B877.quest_desc: [
		"The Configuration Tool can lock a drawer, working like the Toolbox's slot lock."
	]
	quest.2FCA2FED5704B877.title: "S3.5.1 Locked Drawer"
	quest.3020A3A992C5700D.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrade at the Royal Smithing Table without consuming smithing templates."
	]
	quest.3020A3A992C5700D.title: "AC1.12 Royal Smithing Table"
	quest.3045392392527427.quest_desc: [
		"The Rotisserie Tower works like a campfire — it cooks food, but can grill a huge amount at once."
		""
		"The Steamer must be placed on a heat source. Add ingredients and &eseal the top&7 (empty-hand Shift+right-click, or stack another steamer on top)&r to start steaming."
		""
		"Once the food is done, it keeps puffing white steam. Break the Steamer to take the food out."
	]
	quest.3045392392527427.title: "F3.5 Practical Kitchenware (3)"
	quest.308A1563055A715B.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Grindstone comes from the Create addon \"Create: Enchantment Industry\". Its bonus feature is quickly polishing Rose Quartz — see the Ponder scene for details."
		""
		"You can hold Rose Quartz and right-click the Mechanical Grindstone directly, but using a funnel to automate it is recommended."
	]
	quest.308A1563055A715B.title: "S2.3 Sandpaper Is Fine, but So Is a Grindstone"
	quest.30BE06340C85D4A6.quest_desc: [
		"Prepare an Ionocraft ahead of time — it makes fighting the dragon and exploring the End much easier."
		""
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"How do you get titanium without going to the End?\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"66CD35919907E5AF\" } }"
	]
	quest.30BE06340C85D4A6.title: "AC1.20.1 Takes Off~fly~"
	quest.30DA2989D5BB1C21.quest_desc: [
		"\"Create: Enchantment Industry\" adds some new mechanics — now you can store experience, duplicate enchanted books, and break past the enchantment level cap!"
		""
		"But before you get started, there's some prep work to do..."
		""
		"Good news: there's plenty of free experience lying around here to &8&msquander&r while you get to know this mod."
	]
	quest.30DA2989D5BB1C21.title: "E1.1 Don’t Be in a Hurry to Enchant!"
	quest.30ED3DE9089FB3F2.quest_desc: [
		"There are tons of foods here that aren't exactly convenient — not great for taking on the go."
		""
		"But they all have different recipes, which makes them perfect for sharpening your Create production line design and layout skills. Pick a few that interest you and give them a try."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"▷ Build a stuffed potato production line"
		""
		"▷ Build a simple pizza production line"
		""
		"▷ Use Factory Gauges to build a fully automatic food line&7 (you can pick your own mass-production target)"
	]
	quest.30ED3DE9089FB3F2.title: "Eat Something Good"
	quest.31357BFEE09B328E.quest_desc: [
		"Crushing diamond items recovers some Diamonds."
		""
		"Buy diamond items from villagers."
	]
	quest.31357BFEE09B328E.title: "Crushing Old Gear"
	quest.3154F3DFC46A4654.quest_desc: [
		"If you haven't decided what to do next, try building a train, or an automated factory&7 (or play another modpack)&r."
		""
		"Workpieces with lots of rendering will noticeably cut your frame rate, so it's recommended to tuck your machines away."
	]
	quest.3154F3DFC46A4654.title: "S2.17.5.2 What Else Can It Do?"
	quest.315D37C37DF6F713.quest_desc: [
		"Use Pointed Dripstone and a Cauldron&7 (see the MC Wiki)&r to farm renewable lava."
		""
		"Lava burns for a very long time, so a little Dripstone goes a long way toward fueling your boiler."
	]
	quest.315D37C37DF6F713.title: "S2.6.2 Dripstone Dripping Magma? Makes Sense"
	quest.319DC9DFCB29F3E3.quest_desc: [
		"Next, stick a &ePackager&7 (not the Re-Packager — they look very similar)&r next to the warehouse."
	]
	quest.319DC9DFCB29F3E3.title: "Interface"
	quest.31AF2FB206146F3C.quest_desc: [
		"A very handy upgrade — compared to the auto-refill, the middle-click area select feature actually gets used more often."
	]
	quest.31AF2FB206146F3C.title: "O2.22 Pick"
	quest.32442854ACBD3319.quest_desc: [
		"Building on the Shaft, the Encased Chain Drive can carry stress horizontally&7 (like a Gearbox)."
		""
		"A single Encased Chain Drive can only connect to others horizontally &eor&r vertically, though you can connect it at a 90? &erotation&r."
	]
	quest.32442854ACBD3319.quest_subtitle: "Signature Skill Master"
	quest.32442854ACBD3319.title: "Encased Chain Drive"
	quest.32477C9F45EFC9CB.quest_desc: [
		"It can interact with the outside world in place of the container the arrow points to."
		""
		"It effectively enlarges the surface area, making it easy to attach more funnels to your container."
	]
	quest.32477C9F45EFC9CB.title: "O4.7 Expand Container Surface Area"
	quest.32AAEA2FFE571B7B.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Mixer can brew potions — not only faster, it also produces one extra potion per batch compared to the Brewing Stand."
		""
		"And a Blaze Burner's heat is enough to replace Blaze Powder, saving plenty of materials too."
	]
	quest.32AAEA2FFE571B7B.title: "H5.5.1 Automated Brewing"
	quest.32E2743E39A77F17.quest_desc: [
		"Besides producing mineral nuggets, I've also added ore production recipes — purely to tell you that you can use a &eMechanical Pump&r to draw &ehoney out of &ebee nests&r and &ebeehives&r."
		""
		"&8That's a whole plate of dumplings for one dip of vinegar, honestly."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Bees also speed up crop growth, so you can keep them in your fields."
	]
	quest.32E2743E39A77F17.title: "Mass-Producing Minerals 2.0"
	quest.32FC797C231A1B15.quest_desc: [
		"Ghasts can be used to make a Chunk Loader — since you're passing by anyway, why not catch one and take it home to play with?"
		""
		"As for how to catch one..."
		""
		"&8...ehehe?"
	]
	quest.32FC797C231A1B15.title: "S1.8.6 The Wondrous Use of Ghasts"
	quest.333E59BBBB468024.quest_desc: [
		"Why does a wooden Water Wheel keep working just fine in lava?"
	]
	quest.333E59BBBB468024.quest_subtitle: "Steve's technology is stunning"
	quest.333E59BBBB468024.title: "A2.6.1 Wow, Hot Wheels"
	quest.3371F80C22E76985.quest_desc: [
		"Point an Item Detector at the work block&7 (or one block above it)&r, and it emits a redstone signal whenever there are items waiting to be processed."
		""
		"Pair it with a Pulse Generator so the anvil keeps slamming down automatically while items sit beneath it."
	]
	quest.3371F80C22E76985.title: "AC1.6.3 Semi-Automated"
	quest.338B0B918205A36D.quest_desc: [
		"Many structures spawn randomly out in the wild and underground, packed with Create items — if you come across one, feel free to tear it apart and take everything home."
		""
		"Some structures are absurdly rich, like the sky villages up above or the Create bases underground. Finding just one early on can set you up nicely."
		""
		"So wandering around outside is a fairly profitable option."
	]
	quest.338B0B918205A36D.quest_subtitle: "Adventure!"
	quest.338B0B918205A36D.title: "Wild Supplies"
	quest.339B64DBFF03C75F.quest_desc: [
		"The Magnetic Chute is like a normal Chute."
		""
		"But! It can! Transport items upward!"
	]
	quest.339B64DBFF03C75F.title: "AC1.6.2 Chute Plus"
	quest.342B46BE38EDF880.title: "Work"
	quest.3434D3273D121F31.quest_desc: [
		"Through the Giant Anvil's multi-block transformation, you can turn Resentful Blocks of Amber into a spawner. Hoglins can be made into Resentful Amber — their drops include meat, which can be turned into oil, so it's worth setting one up."
		""
		"&aTips&r: The next page covers how to get Resentful Amber blocks; the tutorial book has it too."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"① Use a &eBlock of Resin&r in the Nether's &ecrimson forest&r to scoop up a bunch of Hoglins"
		""
		"② Throw the Block of Resin holding Hoglins into a time warp for a chance to get a Resentful Block of Amber with Hoglins inside"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Jeweler villagers will buy amber blocks that contain mobs, though only in small amounts."
	]
	quest.3434D3273D121F31.title: "AC1.18.2 Artificial Monster Spawner"
	quest.3467046051051E76.quest_desc: [
		"Create has unexpected interactions with plenty of mods — I'll introduce them as you run into them."
		""
		"Of course, using your head and exploring on your own will also lead to plenty of fun discoveries."
	]
	quest.3467046051051E76.title: "Multi-Mod Integration"
	quest.3481DC3DE442EB68.quest_desc: [
		"Animals will automatically eat from the Fodder and breed on their own."
		""
		"This is super handy for free-range raising, but you won't need it for large-scale mechanical farms."
	]
	quest.3481DC3DE442EB68.title: "F2.4 Free-Range Farming Marvel"
	quest.34CB3F726EEE85B5.quest_desc: [
		"It copies and applies an already-configured filter, like Create's clipboard."
		""
		"Also, to hook a multi-block container into the storage network, use it to &eremove the extra blocks&r&7 (usually keeping just one)&r — otherwise the network's inventory counts will go wrong and cause a ton of lag."
	]
	quest.34CB3F726EEE85B5.title: "O4.20 Copy and Paste"
	quest.3547FA56F0388380.quest_desc: [
		"The Inventory Connector automatically groups every &econtainer&7 (blocks that hold items — chests, barrels, drawers, backpacks, hoppers, etc.)&r it's connected to, plus containers linked through other containers or cables, into a single &estorage network&f, and can interact with the outside world on behalf of the whole network at once."
		""
		"Two Inventory Connectors can't join the same network, but one container can be part of several networks at once."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aTips&r:"
		""
		"1. Too many chests cause lag — use barrels&7 (an Item Vault is even better)"
		""
		"2. If you're connecting an Item Vault to the network, be sure to &ekeep only one vault&r&7 (see the related quest)"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Look here, look here\", \"underlined\": true,\"color\":\"blue\", \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"34CB3F726EEE85B5\" } }"
	]
	quest.3547FA56F0388380.title: "O4.1 Core Build"
	quest.355F3C687746614C.quest_desc: [
		"Here, besides summoning lightning, you can also use Dragon's Breath to transform it into Super Experience."
	]
	quest.355F3C687746614C.title: "E1.12 Bulk Termination"
	quest.35ACDC55ED20BAEB.quest_desc: [
		"It's terribly inefficient, but at least it's convenient."
	]
	quest.35ACDC55ED20BAEB.title: "O3.19 Integrated Obsidian Machine"
	quest.35BE83CC6ACDBC05.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a Waystone to spend experience and quickly travel to any other activated Waystone — very convenient."
		""
		"Besides crafted ones, Waystones also generate naturally in the world, like in villages."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Short-distance teleports cost no experience"
		""
		"Teleporting to a target 1000–2000 blocks away costs 1 level"
		""
		"2000–3000 blocks away costs 2 levels"
		""
		"Cross-world teleports, or targets over 3000 blocks away, cost 3 levels"
		""
		"Once you activate one, your minimap marks it with a beam of light; you can turn this off in the settings."
	]
	quest.35BE83CC6ACDBC05.title: "O1.4 Waystone"
	quest.35DCD1A9FEE91CB8.quest_desc: [
		"Flax crafts into String at a 1:1 ratio."
	]
	quest.35DCD1A9FEE91CB8.title: "O2.2 Linen Thread"
	quest.36998F46F141A4D7.quest_desc: [
		"All three of these dusts can be obtained by spout-filling &eCinder Flour&r with different potions."
	]
	quest.36998F46F141A4D7.title: "Alchemy"
	quest.36BF32980D7F2389.quest_desc: [
		"Create can brew potions in bulk, and the Sprinkler can spray fluids downward at 100 mb per use."
		""
		"Combine the two and you can automatically spray potions over every mob to heal them..."
		""
		"&eAnd then smash them hard with an anvil"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&e*&r is a wildcard — it matches any text of any length or amount, and also works in Create's logistics systems."
		""
		"For example, the &e*&r machine here can match an &eiron&r farm, a &ewitcher&r farm, or a &ePhantom&r farm"
		""
		"[ \"This will be useful when using \", { \"text\": \"Package Frogport\",\"color\":blue, \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"1EBE33170D6B21D8\" } }, \".\" ]"
	]
	quest.36BF32980D7F2389.quest_subtitle: "Respect all living things equally"
	quest.36BF32980D7F2389.title: "AC1.6.6 Mob* Farm"
	quest.36F5C01A7406A0BF.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Arm can move items &ein groups&r with few restrictions, and shines in tricky spots."
		""
		"For now, though, its job is to &eautomatically feed the Blaze Burner&r..."
		""
		"Of course, it can do much more — future hauling needs can all be handed to it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Example: a Mechanical Arm automatically feeding magma to a Blaze Burner:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/s2_6.png width:256 height:142 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"How it works:"
		""
		"First, this is a boiler fueled by &emagma&r. Compared to a solid-fuel boiler, it has one extra step — injecting liquid."
		""
		"In the picture, the &eInjector&r injects magma into the iron bucket on the Depot at the upper right; the Brass Funnel&7 (filtering magma buckets)&r then drops the magma bucket onto the Depot below."
		""
		"After that, the Mechanical Arm takes the magma bucket from the lower Depot, feeds it to the Blaze Burner, and puts the empty bucket into the Brass Funnel&7 (filtering empty buckets)&r at the upper right."
		""
		"You can also use a &eMechanical Pipette&r to skip liquid injection and feed magma straight to the burner."
	]
	quest.36F5C01A7406A0BF.title: "2.6 Servitor"
	quest.36F5E3EECFB6D761.quest_desc: [
		"It'll probably be your backpack's long-term companion."
	]
	quest.36F5E3EECFB6D761.title: "O2.8 Cheap Luxury Goods"
	quest.37260C62D6417351.quest_desc: [
		"Now you can ditch gear shifting and move up to high tech — the Rotation Speed Controller!"
		""
		"&aTips&r: The Rotation Speed Controller's &egear end&r and its &eshaft interface&7 (Shaft)&r are bidirectionally connected. Feed power into either end, and it comes out the other at the speed you've set."
	]
	quest.37260C62D6417351.title: "2.7 Essential for Engineers"
	quest.373702FA6AEFC5C5.quest_desc: [
		"Feed the Sprinkler with liquid fertilizer to speed up crop growth in the area starting &e2 blocks&r below it, &e5*5*7&7 (length*width*height)&r."
	]
	quest.373702FA6AEFC5C5.title: "F1.10 Liquid Fertilizer"
	quest.375E9A144E057AFC.quest_desc: [
		"Stick it on and you can access the &estorage network&r through a &eStock Ticker&8 (i.e., the stock keeper you've got sitting beside it)&r, and take extra manual control over item transport."
	]
	quest.375E9A144E057AFC.quest_subtitle: "It is recommended that you complete all other quest lines before reading here."
	quest.375E9A144E057AFC.title: "Storage Network"
	quest.376B0226F9435FAD.quest_desc: [
		"This nifty gadget from Tom's Simple Storage lets you access containers&7 (Depot, Funnel, Item Vault, etc.)&r"
		""
		"You can also glue it onto a &edynamic contraption&r&7 (needs Super Glue)&r to grab items straight from the contraption."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Once you reach the Brass Age, you can set up a storage network so your production lines automatically pull raw materials from the warehouse."
		""
		"Before that, you can use quest rewards to build a rough prototype and access the warehouse the Create way&7 (instead of borrowing other mods)&r."
	]
	quest.376B0226F9435FAD.title: "E1.7.1 Let Me See!"
	quest.37ABD5801057FBE9.quest_desc: [
		"Likewise, you'll need the matching smithing template to craft Frost Metal weapons and tools."
	]
	quest.37ABD5801057FBE9.title: "S2.2.9 Frost Metal Smithing Template"
	quest.3804A26316AC0091.quest_desc: [
		"It's also a good idea to put a small buffer storage here to hold products temporarily — the Crushing Wheels produce a lot when running in bulk."
	]
	quest.3804A26316AC0091.title: "Cache"
	quest.385E701E2A01ECC8.quest_desc: [
		"In AnvilCraft, an anvil knocking 20% off a mob's health grants one drop. Iron golems drop iron, and the iron can be used to heal them..."
		""
		"The iron farm loop is complete!"
		""
		"&aTips&r: The tutorial book has a detailed guide."
	]
	quest.385E701E2A01ECC8.quest_subtitle: "The mod that respects Iron Golems the most on the entire internet"
	quest.385E701E2A01ECC8.title: "AC1.6.5 Iron Farm"
	quest.3906FBFE6DF806E4.quest_desc: [
		"The contraption here needs a buffer and an interface, otherwise the Mechanical Harvester can't automatically collect the wheat and seeds."
	]
	quest.3906FBFE6DF806E4.title: "H1.2 Wildcard"
	quest.390C138909D71BED.quest_desc: [
		"Pulls items in from or pushes items out toward a chosen direction, and also works with fluid drawers — very handy."
		""
		"&aTips&f: Right-click these two upgrades inside your inventory to change the direction. Press &eF3&r to check which way you're facing."
	]
	quest.390C138909D71BED.title: "O3.15 Built-in Omnidirectional Funnel"
	quest.393AD5FF6F557EF0.quest_desc: [
		"Crushing Blaze Rods yields &7more Blaze Powder&r than crafting."
	]
	quest.397A15088D9D7C59.quest_desc: [
		"Grow mushrooms on Rich Soil and, after a while, there's a chance they turn into a &eMushroom Colony&r. Harvest with &eShears&r."
		""
		"Once the colony is fully grown&7 (when it has five caps)&r, left-click with Shears to harvest the whole colony&7 (without Shears you get 5 mushrooms)&r. Right-click harvests a single mushroom and removes one layer of caps&7 (leaving at least two caps)&r."
		""
		"Colonies can be ripened with Bone Meal. But be careful — only bone-meal them after they've become a &eMushroom Colony&r; bone-mealing a plain mushroom spawns a giant mushroom."
		""
		"Mushroom Colonies speed up the conversion of Organic Compost into Rich Soil."
	]
	quest.397A15088D9D7C59.quest_subtitle: "Steve picking mushrooms, carrying a big basket"
	quest.397A15088D9D7C59.title: "F1.8 Growing Mushrooms"
	quest.399182578F0DA809.quest_desc: [
		"Steam 'n' Rails also adds a variety of tracks to meet more complex needs."
		""
		"That said, I don't recommend turning back the clock — standard gauge is still the way to go."
	]
	quest.399182578F0DA809.title: "T1.8 More Tracks"
	quest.39D1FAC09600EFD3.quest_desc: [
		"Cardboard isn't just for the Packager — it can also make armor and weapons."
		""
		"Wearing a full set of Cardboard armor and sneaking&7 (crouching)&r gives a special effect!"
	]
	quest.39D1FAC09600EFD3.title: "S2.16.6 Cardboard"
	quest.39E11B52BE65F6B5.quest_desc: [
		"Once a villager claims a Jewel Crafting Table as their workstation, they become a Jeweler. You'll want to buy the Royal Steel smithing template from them."
	]
	quest.39E11B52BE65F6B5.title: "AC1.11 Jeweler"
	quest.3A2AF3E7B6EFE074.quest_desc: [
		"Who said you have to inject chocolate into dumplings?"
		""
		"Then they're not traditional dumplings anymore — what's wrong with a little innovation &7(said very loudly)&r!"
		""
		"Besides, you can desecrate pizza instead."
	]
	quest.3A2AF3E7B6EFE074.title: "HS5.2.3.2 Desecration"
	quest.3A434C665E7F627A.quest_desc: [
		"Same as before — not recommended."
	]
	quest.3A434C665E7F627A.title: "O2.20 Don’t Make It Either"
	quest.3A4783866AF0E954.quest_desc: [
		"Tired of cranking the handle like a slave? Give the Water Wheel a try — 100% clean, infinite energy."
	]
	quest.3A4783866AF0E954.title: "S1.6.1 Hydraulic…stress"
	quest.3AC7DED6E715F8EC.quest_desc: [
		"Hover your cursor over the Mechanical Press and hold &e[W]&r to open its Ponder — after watching it, you'll know how to use it."
		""
		"&aTips&r: This quest has multiple pages."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If you run into trouble transmitting stress, check out this chapter:"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Transmission and Logistics\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"0955E2B800DC1C95\" } }"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"At the very top of the JEI&7 (EMI)&r recipe page you can switch the acquisition method&7 (the arrow buttons also flip pages)&r."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/1_6.png width:135 height:47 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3AC7DED6E715F8EC.title: "1.6 Young People’s First Industrial Equipment"
	quest.3B0BCCECEE8775BF.quest_desc: [
		"&eRight-click a villager with a Block of Resin&r to pack them inside it; right-click again to let them out."
	]
	quest.3B0BCCECEE8775BF.title: "AC1.9.1 Catch... Recruit Villagers"
	quest.3B19E316E545E2C0.quest_desc: [
		"Crushing raw ore with Crushing Wheels gives you 2 crushed ores. Each crushed ore can be smelted into one ingot, or washed into 9 nuggets plus a bonus product."
		""
		"Crushing Wheels can be stacked — try building a large crusher to handle the massive crushing demand coming up."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"▷ Automatically separate the crushed ores, and set up washing and compacting lines"
		""
		"▷ Use Package Frogports to hook the Crushing Wheels into your logistics system"
		""
		"▷ Like the Crushing Wheels, build large-scale pressing and mixing centers and hook them into the logistics system"
	]
	quest.3B19E316E545E2C0.title: "Mineral Processing"
	quest.3B6D08C930787F82.quest_desc: [
		"Royal Steel — its defining feature is being very expensive."
		""
		"It's another upgrade path for weapons and tools besides Netherite, but sadly it can't upgrade armor..."
		""
		"You can still use it for amulets and other little trinkets, though."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Diamonds and emeralds can be obtained from villagers indefinitely — a &eBlock of Resin&r makes moving villagers around easy."
		""
		"Also, crushing spruce wood won't give you any resin."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If you're unhappy with a villager's trades, hit them with an &eanvil&r to reset the trades — at the risk of them turning into a &eGreen Robe Elder&7 (nitwit)&r."
		""
		"You can also craft an &eEmerald Amulet&r — while it's in your &einventory&r, villagers give you discounts."
		""
		"Finally, you can use a &eTrading Depot&r for automated trading — a great way to mass-produce emeralds."
		""
		"&aTips&r: The &eJewel Crafting Table&r recipe is a &ecopy&7 (forge)&r recipe&7 (meaning you need the first Emerald Amulet before you can make a second one)&r — for your first one, sequenced processing is recommended."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You can also use Royal Steel to build laser mining rigs, which need electricity — very un-Create."
		""
		"That's why I've set up other ways to mass-produce these assorted ores with Create, so you can skip laser mining."
	]
	quest.3B6D08C930787F82.quest_subtitle: "This is not about Create, but it might interest you"
	quest.3B6D08C930787F82.title: "S1.11.1 Where Does It Come From?"
	quest.3B7A4A7D237641F9.quest_desc: [
		"Train signals divide the track into \"sections\", effectively preventing collisions."
		""
		"Combined with redstone they can do advanced tricks, and they're also great for feeding redstone signals to decorations."
	]
	quest.3B7A4A7D237641F9.title: "T1.6 Traffic Control"
	quest.3BC40A2C1C254A3A.quest_desc: [
		"The Amethyst Sword comes with the &eBeheading&r enchantment&7 (up to level III)&r, which should make collecting Wither Skeleton Skulls easier."
		""
		"There's also a new structure in the Nether packed with Wither Skeleton spawners and decorative Wither Skeleton Skulls — great for grabbing."
	]
	quest.3BC40A2C1C254A3A.title: "AC1.14 Horror Thriller Skull"
	quest.3C1026EF37C893CF.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Crafter is just too slow. Vanilla happens to have a Crafter too — can we hook that into Create's logistics system?"
		""
		"&cNote:&f Although the vanilla one is faster, it's quite fiddly to use, and you need solid experience to integrate it into your logistics efficiently."
	]
	quest.3C1026EF37C893CF.title: "S4.10.2 Speed It Up!"
	quest.3C2CEBF878AB2A20.quest_desc: [
		"Cars are without a doubt the friendliest physical structure for beginners — just feed stress to the wheels and they go."
		""
		"Cars also touch the ground directly, so you don't need strict center-of-mass control — which lowers the difficulty considerably."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Besides wheels, you can also mount round things like Crushing Wheels or Flywheels on the suspension."
		""
		"&7This guide doesn't cover aerodynamics."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"On turning:"
		""
		"&a[Recommended]&r Method ①: send a redstone signal to the suspension to change the wheels' direction."
		""
		"&a[Optional]&r Method ②: control the speed difference between the left and right wheels to turn toward the slower side."
		""
		"&7There are other ways, of course, but since I don't recommend them, I'm obviously not going to write them."
	]
	quest.3C2CEBF878AB2A20.title: "Cars"
	quest.3C537D53825E8207.quest_desc: [
		"{ \"text\": \"Related supplementary info\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"0E261EE5B5EA8F41\" } }"
	]
	quest.3C537D53825E8207.title: "H5.4.2 Mass-Producing... Netherite?!"
	quest.3C5909F78FA7CFB7.quest_desc: [
		"A single track can connect to several tracks at different positions, creating some overlapping curves."
		""
		"While driving, use \"A\", \"W\" and \"D\" to switch between the branches."
		""
		"This is very handy, especially when building large stations."
		""
		"Switch points aren't strictly necessary."
	]
	quest.3C5909F78FA7CFB7.title: "T1.5 Junctions"
	quest.3D17451FBC81AF36.quest_desc: [
		"Unpack Dripstone Blocks to get Pointed Dripstone."
	]
	quest.3D17451FBC81AF36.title: "Unpack"
	quest.3D641E50217E411F.quest_desc: [
		"Usually only used early on to craft the Iron Backpack."
	]
	quest.3D641E50217E411F.title: "O2.6 Cheap Backpack"
	quest.3D7032A4AB2988DE.quest_desc: [
		"The drawer system can transport items wirelessly and in real time over a fairly large range — sometimes more useful than a Mechanical Arm."
		""
		"&aTips:&f You can use upgrade modules to expand the controller's working range."
	]
	quest.3D7032A4AB2988DE.title: "S4.3.1 Wireless Drawer Transmission"
	quest.3D7B77FC4DA4A48F.quest_desc: [
		"Sophisticated Backpacks is a modpack staple — simple yet powerful."
		""
		"The backpack can be carried with you or worn in the chestplate/back slot; press &eB&r to quickly open it."
	]
	quest.3D7B77FC4DA4A48F.title: "O2.5 Sophisticated Backpacks"
	quest.3D7E4FAEF34F3AA1.quest_desc: [
		"Whether smelted into ingots or washed into nuggets, processed minerals take up tons of storage space."
		""
		"Packing them into mineral blocks eases the storage pressure a lot — a Mechanical Press with a Basin can handle it."
	]
	quest.3D7E4FAEF34F3AA1.title: "S2.10.1 Compressed Block Storage"
	quest.3D7E9E4911A60BF0.quest_desc: [
		"The Blaze Forger can merge multiple smithing templates together, and apply templates to items."
	]
	quest.3D7E9E4911A60BF0.title: "E1.9 Living Anvil"
	quest.3E1685A174D77849.quest_desc: [
		"The two kinds of rice are planted differently, and sadly they don't work together.&7 (I'm considering whether to make them compatible, or just disable one?)"
		""
		"&eFarmer's Delight&r's rice must be planted in dirt&7 (or farmland, rich soil, rich farmland)&r under &eone block of water&r, using &erice seeds&r."
		""
		"You can harvest it by right-clicking or with a Mechanical Harvester."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eKaleidoscope's&r rice must be planted in farmland&7 (or rich farmland)&r under &eone block of water&r, using &eWild Rice Seeds&r&7 (or rice seeds — Kaleidoscope's rice has been unified with Farmer's Delight's)&r."
		""
		"Right-click harvesting &ewon't&r produce drops properly, and harvesting with a Mechanical Harvester can easily cause &elag or crashes&r."
		""
		"As compensation, Kaleidoscope's rice has a much bigger yield, and harvesting can occasionally drop a &eCaterpillar&r — feeding one to a chick makes it grow up instantly."
		""
		"With &efish&r in the water, Kaleidoscope's rice &egrows faster&r."
		""
		"Kaleidoscope rice paddies even make frog croaking sounds."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The subtitle's \"24 kinds of tomato in one pack\" refers to how some shoddy modpacks&7&m (like the one you're playing right now)&r don't add compatibility between same-named items from different mods."
		""
		"&7That's been fixed now — barring surprises, you'll see two identical rice in the quest requirements."
		""
		"In fact, many good mods already anticipated name collisions and implemented partial compatibility through tag systems &7(AnvilCraft and Create are partly compatible, for example)&r."
		""
		"Sadly, Kaleidoscope's tag system and recipes aren't written very well, and I can't be bothered to fix them one by one."
		""
		"So I'm just leaving it!"
	]
	quest.3E1685A174D77849.quest_subtitle: "Isn't it normal to have 24 kinds of tomatoes in one modpack? (looks away)"
	quest.3E1685A174D77849.title: "F1.5 Rice"
	quest.3E539ED236EC7635.quest_desc: [
		"The Boiler provides a massive amount of stress, freeing you from stress limits and letting you design large machines and production lines freely."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"▷ Set up fuel supply for your Boiler&7 (recommended fuel: charcoal, lava, Blaze Cakes)"
		""
		"▷ Upgrade the Boiler to max level&7 (18 levels)"
		""
		"▷ Design a boiler bank&7 (multiple Boilers connected together)"
	]
	quest.3E539ED236EC7635.title: "Boiler"
	quest.3EB2626D59177BE3.title: "Combat Components"
	quest.3EDB9250DFFFDC8A.quest_desc: [
		"Smash a &echarged&r Neutronium Ingot into an &eBlock of Ember Metal&r while it's in the &coverheated&r state to obtain it."
		""
		"&aTips&r: The Overheated Block of Ember Metal only lasts 10 seconds, and after that it has a chance to degrade into a Block of Netherite — so you need to be quick."
	]
	quest.3EDB9250DFFFDC8A.quest_subtitle: "Steve's power!"
	quest.3EDB9250DFFFDC8A.title: "AC1.24 Ultimate Material"
	quest.3F198015065022AD.quest_desc: [
		"Once the Steam Boiler starts up, it empties the water in its tank every so often, so you need to keep feeding it water."
		""
		"Just use a &eMechanical Pump&r with copper pipes to draw water straight from rivers, lakes, and seas&7 (even puddles)&r — no need for a Hose Pulley."
	]
	quest.3F198015065022AD.title: "2.2 Supply Water to the Boiler"
	quest.3F1D55B3D10C15A8.quest_desc: [
		"Tired of sorting items and rummaging through boxes to find things? Give &eTom's Simple Storage&r a try!"
		""
		"Just check the &eLife Tips&r section when you need it — no need to read it all now, that would be exhausting."
	]
	quest.3F1D55B3D10C15A8.title: "Simple Warehouse Management"
	quest.3F4C4C22D05DE8A4.quest_desc: [
		"Crab Traps can catch fish, because MC has no crabs ("
		""
		"Fishing Nets are more efficient, but you need quite a few of them."
	]
	quest.3F4C4C22D05DE8A4.quest_subtitle: "Did the Crab win its comeback match? Kind of!"
	quest.3F4C4C22D05DE8A4.title: "F4.5 Automated Fishing"
	quest.3F5CFDE873518004.quest_desc: [
		"In Aeronautics physical structures, &eweight&r is a crucial concept, especially for ships and aircraft."
		""
		"In many cases, you'll use &eplanks&r, &eballoons&r, or even &elevitation stones&r to lighten the structure."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Next up is &esize&r — for beginners, &ebigger is better&r."
		""
		"Miniaturization is far harder than you'd think."
		""
		"So I strongly recommend making your first build big&7 (unless you're dead set on starting with an aircraft)&r."
	]
	quest.3F5CFDE873518004.title: "Volume and Weight"
	quest.3FFD00A21D5D5669.quest_desc: [
		"Moving a Mechanical Drill with a Rope Pulley is a handy way to dig a mine shaft — a great early-game way to get minerals."
		""
		"See the &eRope Pulley&r Ponder for details."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Horizontal Miner\", \"underlined\": true,\"color\":\"blue\",\"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"263229837952BEAC\" } }"
	]
	quest.3FFD00A21D5D5669.quest_subtitle: "Remember to view the Ponder scene!"
	quest.3FFD00A21D5D5669.title: "S1.11.5 Simple Vertical Mining Machine"
	quest.3FFE5F7A41C3E51B.quest_desc: [
		"Many ingredients and materials come from mobs."
		""
		"Some ingredients can only be obtained by defeating mobs with a &eKnife&r / &eCleaver&r."
		""
		"&8A perfect excuse for a god of cuisine to grace the mortal world www"
	]
	quest.3FFE5F7A41C3E51B.quest_subtitle: "\"The Stove Lord's Pioneer in a Different World\""
	quest.3FFE5F7A41C3E51B.title: "F4.1 Butchering and Hunting"
	quest.40B5D2A4D81DDEC9.quest_desc: [
		"If you really can't be bothered to open Vaults, that works too..."
	]
	quest.40B5D2A4D81DDEC9.title: "Trade In for the Heavy Core"
	quest.40BD2A20316B98CC.quest_desc: [
		"&eCages&r are a bit pricey and &ecan only capture small creatures&r&7 (chickens and bees can be caught directly; anything bigger only as babies)&r, but they're &ereusable&r."
		""
		"&eBlocks of Resin&r are &eone-use&r, have a &ebigger capture range&r&7 (still size-limited)&r, and can even catch hostile mobs that are &eweakened&r. More useful overall, but you'll need &eCrushing Wheels&r or a &eMillstone&r to make them."
	]
	quest.40BD2A20316B98CC.quest_subtitle: "\"Food: I Have a Ranch in Another World\""
	quest.40BD2A20316B98CC.title: "F2.1 Develop Animal Husbandry"
	quest.40EF2F8772FB09DF.quest_desc: [
		"Can store multiple variants of a single item, like enchanted books."
		""
		"Not that great, honestly."
	]
	quest.40EF2F8772FB09DF.title: "O4.10 Storage of Similar Items"
	quest.40F1C2E17AFC1657.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Plough can till soil, but doing it by hand is clearly more convenient&7 (tilling also works with vein mining)&r."
		""
		"However, when you need lots of dirt, it comes in handy:"
		""
		"Dirt mixed with gravel makes Coarse Dirt, and tilling Coarse Dirt with a hoe turns it back into Dirt."
	]
	quest.40F1C2E17AFC1657.title: "F1.12 Automated Tilling"
	quest.4100506A28411BB5.quest_desc: [
		"Works just like Create's Filter."
	]
	quest.4100506A28411BB5.title: "O4.17 This Is the List Filter"
	quest.41207AC7A7FD17B3.quest_desc: [
		"First, you'll need to prepare a warehouse."
		""
		"Any container works for it, but I highly recommend an Item Vault."
	]
	quest.41207AC7A7FD17B3.title: "Warehouse"
	quest.413600B59E0C332D.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a train driver&7 (such as a Blaze Burner)&r with a train schedule, and the driver will follow it automatically."
		""
		"You can also place it above a &eTrain Station&r, and it will automatically apply to the drivers of trains stopping there."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Regex Matching of Station Names\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"10F6FE7BC7406958\" } }"
	]
	quest.413600B59E0C332D.title: "T1.7 Automated Operations"
	quest.4147FD563F5B8437.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Drill can break blocks in front of it — even Obsidian."
		""
		"It's great on a &edynamic contraption&r — see the Ponder."
	]
	quest.4147FD563F5B8437.title: "S1.7.2 A Drill Bit That Breaks Through the Sky!"
	quest.417DDED017FF632B.quest_desc: [
		"Warp Plates&7 (let's call this one A)&r are mainly for transporting creatures over long distances. Placing one generates an &eAttuned Shard&7 (also numbered A)&r with the same name — just stick &eAttuned Shard-A&r into another Warp Plate&7 (call it B)&r."
		""
		"&7If you lose the Attuned Shard, insert a &eDormant Shard&7 into the plate, and a new shard with the same name as the plate will be generated."
		""
		"When an entity&7 (like a villager)&r stands on &eWarp Plate-B&r, after a brief delay it gets teleported to the &eWarp Plate-A&r linked to &eAttuned Shard-A&r."
		""
		"&aTips&r: You can pair this with a Cart Assembler to move a spawner home."
	]
	quest.417DDED017FF632B.title: "OS1.3.1 Warp Plate"
	quest.41839730D89C3FA1.quest_desc: [
		"Putting a Block of Uranium through a time warp turns it into raw uranium while releasing tons of heat — you can use that to generate power."
		""
		"Mineral springs can also supply uranium in bulk, so you don't have to keep the collider busy."
		""
		"&aTips&r: See the tutorial book."
	]
	quest.41839730D89C3FA1.title: "AC1.21.4 Mass-Producing Uranium"
	quest.418B4F343AD328EA.quest_desc: [
		"As everyone knows, Ancient Debris is super rare — but since it's fireproof..."
		""
		"Why not just dig out all the lava lakes? XD"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Ancient Debris has a duplication recipe&7 (using tungsten)&r, though it's best to mass-produce it once you reach the Brass Age."
	]
	quest.418B4F343AD328EA.title: "S1.8.5 Rare? Dig It All Up!"
	quest.41CCD0F9241BE346.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Mixer is truly all-round — it can even brew potions!"
		""
		"Compared to the Brewing Stand, it's faster and much easier to automate."
		""
		"&7Many of Create's resource-renewal recipes need potions, but you don't necessarily need them right now."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Just fill the Basin with water, feed the Blaze Burner, then add the ingredients one by one, and you'll get potions."
		""
		"The tricky part is getting the potions out —"
		""
		"You can still use an &eopen container&7 (introduced earlier — hope you haven't forgotten)&f to export the brewed potions."
		""
		"But starting from Awkward Potion, every step's product is exported automatically, which actually makes open containers more complicated."
		""
		"You could of course build a super-long staircase like the vanilla redstone potion machine, but I'd recommend Smart Fluid Pipes instead."
	]
	quest.41CCD0F9241BE346.quest_subtitle: "Please do not use cement work basins to fill potions!"
	quest.41CCD0F9241BE346.title: "S2.2.1 Bulk Brewing"
	quest.41D3A1AE0002B54B.quest_desc: [
		"Farming can be automated too, though your needs probably only extend to auto-producing dirt and liquid fertilizer."
		""
		"If you're interested, check the Ponder scenes and the Automation chapter."
	]
	quest.41D3A1AE0002B54B.title: "F1.13 Automation"
	quest.41DA43B09C21ABDD.quest_desc: [
		"On your laid track, use Train Stations to create stations, where you can assemble your first train."
		""
		"After that, you can lay track and add or remove stations as you please."
		""
		"When naming a station, it's best to pick something neat and orderly."
	]
	quest.41DA43B09C21ABDD.title: "T1.2 Rail Network & Stations"
	quest.4202A7B822717C80.quest_desc: [
		"Earth Core Shards and their related ores don't generate naturally — they need to be actively stimulated."
		""
		"Synthesizing them might be the better choice."
	]
	quest.4202A7B822717C80.title: "H5.4.3 Things That Do Not Exist in Nature"
	quest.4255BE43A79443AC.quest_desc: [
		"AnvilCraft's superheated smelting turns one Ancient Debris into two Netherite Scraps, and one Netherite Scrap can be crafted back into one Ancient Debris."
		""
		"And just like that, you have infinite Netherite."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Remember to keep one Netherite Crystal Nucleus aside — don't use them all up."
	]
	quest.4255BE43A79443AC.title: "AC1.19.1 Infinite Netherite"
	quest.4274FBFC68ACEB87.quest_desc: [
		"Smithing upgrades at the Royal Smithing Table don't consume templates."
		""
		"You can also craft a &eRoyal Anvil&r and a &eRoyal Grindstone&r to further enhance your weapons and gear."
	]
	quest.4274FBFC68ACEB87.title: "S1.11.3 Saving Forging Templates"
	quest.429A59AB51756FCC.quest_desc: [
		"You might as well give me your spare diamonds — why would you make this?"
	]
	quest.429A59AB51756FCC.title: "O2.14 No Need"
	quest.42EA77856F0001DD.quest_desc: [
		"This chapter only lists methods that are hard to look up in JEI&7 (EMI)&r."
		""
		"\"&eCtrl + F&r\" can search the quests."
		""
		"&eJEI&7 (EMI)&r is a great helper too."
	]
	quest.42EA77856F0001DD.title: "How to Get\\What to Get"
	quest.438D5290BE258CBC.quest_desc: [
		"Can you imagine a world without meat, eggs, and milk?"
		""
		"Fence off a patch of land, raise some little critters, and enjoy delicious ingredients — what's not to like."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"By exploiting the size difference between baby and adult mobs&7 (F3+B shows hitboxes)&r, you can use an &eEncased Fan&r with blocks that have special collision volumes&7 (like cauldron bottoms, wool carpets, slabs, trapdoors, etc.)&r to separate the babies and set up automatic slaughter."
		""
		"&7Yeah... not very humane, but that's your call."
	]
	quest.438D5290BE258CBC.quest_subtitle: "Meat! Egg! Milk!"
	quest.438D5290BE258CBC.title: "F2.2 Ranch Prototype"
	quest.439FB931D388BDFB.quest_desc: [
		"The portal is right in front of you..."
		""
		"Can't find it? Don't forget F4 for out-of-body mode."
	]
	quest.439FB931D388BDFB.title: "2.16 Open Up, Steve's Delivering Warmth!"
	quest.43A0F994F8722DF4.quest_desc: [
		"Just a transitional tool."
	]
	quest.43A0F994F8722DF4.title: "O4.4 Beautiful Little Junk"
	quest.441B30BAB78F4D3E.quest_desc: [
		"Kaleidoscope: Tavern adds a brewing system, filling the gap left by the lack of table wine."
		""
		"Before you start, though, you'll need to hunt down some brewing ingredients: wheat, apples, berries, and most importantly — grapes."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Grapevines have a Ponder scene!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Grapevines planted on:"
		"Dirt → Grape"
		"Magma Blocks → Gold Grape"
		"Ice → Ice Grape"
	]
	quest.441B30BAB78F4D3E.title: "F3.3.1 Brewing Ingredients"
	quest.448BA2E592AE59B4.quest_desc: [
		"A Mechanical Arm can be bound to multiple Blaze Burners, making it easier to feed them."
	]
	quest.448BA2E592AE59B4.title: "H2.7 Feed the Blaze"
	quest.44989E6F78FFB9E5.quest_desc: [
		"Like iron, Create also has a way to mass-produce gold — though it's a bit trickier than iron."
		""
		"Of course, following the questline step by step will definitely get you there."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"The questline is here\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"469208ED7DC7B90E\" } }"
	]
	quest.44989E6F78FFB9E5.title: "S2.14.1 Unlimited Gold"
	quest.44E4DB19E314EABB.quest_desc: [
		"As everyone knows: &9water&r meeting &4lava&r creates &ecobblestone&8 (or stone)."
		""
		"Similarly:"
		""
		"&9Chocolate&r meeting &4lava&r creates &eslag&7 (produces charcoal and coal)"
		""
		"&9Honey&r meeting &4lava&r creates &elimestone&7 (produces lava, or can be turned into Cinerite)"
		""
		"&9Water&r meeting &4Melt Gem&r randomly creates &eandesite&r&7 (for Andesite Alloy)&r, &ediorite&r&7 (produces zinc)&r, or &egranite&r&7 (produces gold)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You might be wondering: why didn't I mention earlier that Melt Gem produces granite?"
		""
		"Mainly so you'd appreciate the vanilla crafting recipe — truly delicious&8 (not)"
	]
	quest.44E4DB19E314EABB.title: "Cobblestone Generator 2.0"
	quest.457937D43D028BF6.quest_desc: [
		"Mixing a Block of Frost Metal with a Block of Ember Metal in Dragon's Breath yields Multiphase Matter — though the loss is fairly high..."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Resonator Core\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"7DF4BEFADBEB9ADF\" } }"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Heavy Halberd Core\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"10E3D0924F832EC6\" } }"
	]
	quest.457937D43D028BF6.title: "S2.17.6 Multi-Purpose Tool"
	quest.45A166BD8DAE84F9.quest_desc: [
		"&eCrush&r diamond items to recover Diamonds based on their durability."
		""
		"A &eGiant Anvil&r can turn a 3×3×3 cube of Blocks of Coal into 1 Block of Diamond."
	]
	quest.45A166BD8DAE84F9.title: "Crushing & Crafting"
	quest.4691BD12327CDEB7.quest_desc: [
		"Wolf Armor is a seriously OP piece of gear — too bad humans can't wear it."
	]
	quest.4691BD12327CDEB7.title: "H5.3.3 Shulker Farm Replacement"
	quest.469208ED7DC7B90E.quest_desc: [
		"At this point your gold line is ready — next up is optimizing the logistics."
		""
		"For example: splitting cobblestone between the soul sand and red sand lines, using Factory Gauges to automate the line, and so on."
	]
	quest.469208ED7DC7B90E.title: "H3.8 You Did It!"
	quest.46B354A9BBAA036A.quest_desc: [
		"A Faucet from Handcrafted, when stuck onto a &ewater source&r&7 (such as waterlogged leaves)&r, provides water endlessly with zero cost."
		""
		"Use it for water and you can skip the tedious manual pumping after your boiler shuts down."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Stuck onto a container, it can also draw water out and pour it into the container below."
		""
		"Need a steam boiler in the Nether? A Faucet can help there too."
	]
	quest.46B354A9BBAA036A.title: "S2.2 Toothpick to Pry the Elephant"
	quest.46CCE67ABF227416.quest_desc: [
		"In the Brass Age, the Steam Boiler becomes the best source of stress."
		""
		"In most cases a level 9 Boiler is enough to power you for the rest of your life — the only cost is a bit of fuel, so why not?"
		""
		"&aTips:&f See the Steam Engine Ponder for how to build it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Also, Boilers are huge and need maintenance, so I recommend newbie mechanics&7 (yes, you)&r place theirs somewhere open."
		""
		"Then use &eChain Conveyors&r to connect the stress to your Andesite-Age stress network — that makes maintenance much easier."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"How Boiler level is calculated:"
		""
		"Size: 1 level per 4 Fluid Tanks"
		""
		"Water: 1 level per 10 mb/s of supply&7 (every 20 RPM of Mechanical Pump speed)&r"
		""
		"Heat: 1 level per burning Blaze Burner&7 (superheated Blaze Burners give 2 levels)&r"
		""
		"Each Boiler level needs one Steam Engine, exporting 16384 su of stress."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Related Wiki\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://www.mcmod.cn/item/696090.html\" } }"
	]
	quest.46CCE67ABF227416.title: "2.1 Steam Boiler"
	quest.4716E23A66F62EE2.quest_desc: [
		"If you think Netherite isn't enough..."
		""
		"Under superheating, with Earth Core Shards, Netherite, lava, and Blaze Powder can react further to produce Ember Metal."
	]
	quest.4716E23A66F62EE2.title: "S2.6.7 Another Upgrade"
	quest.4792C0C9F0D5DF5E.quest_desc: [
		"The first step toward mass-producing Frost Metal."
		""
		"Other than that, silver isn't of much use anymore."
	]
	quest.4792C0C9F0D5DF5E.title: "S2.2.6 Alchemy!"
	quest.4816843BD5B2FE89.quest_desc: [
		"Water streams and vanilla hoppers still have their uses in Create — don't forget about them completely."
	]
	quest.4816843BD5B2FE89.title: "S3.2.1 Old Skills Cannot Be Lost"
	quest.48B46D0ECFAD13D0.quest_desc: [
		"Gantry contraptions have a low performance cost and plenty of special features, but compared to other contraptions, they're far more complex."
		""
		"You can use the drive-by-wire mod to make the wiring easier."
	]
	quest.48B46D0ECFAD13D0.title: "S1.7.9 The Most Difficult Dynamic Structure to Use"
	quest.498D6CAE7F0D43ED.quest_desc: [
		"The Space Overcompressor needs quite a few Shulker Boxes, so bring back plenty of shells."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Brushing an &earmadillo&r with a brush quickly gets you Armadillo Scutes."
	]
	quest.498D6CAE7F0D43ED.title: "AC1.20 Exploring the End"
	quest.49A957BCE55402AB.quest_desc: [
		"Trains can pass through Nether portals."
		""
		"And as everyone knows, 1 block in the Nether = 8 blocks in the Overworld."
		""
		"So you can build express trains down in the Nether."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Building above the Nether bedrock ceiling is a great idea"
	]
	quest.49A957BCE55402AB.title: "T1.4 Nether Transit"
	quest.49AA6727342CA7EB.quest_desc: [
		"Washing quartz sand yields zinc, and washing Cinerite yields three minerals at once — copper, zinc, and iron."
		""
		"Also, mixing Cinerite and quartz sand with &ehoney&r and &edye of the matching color&r directly crafts &eVeridium&r and &eAsurine&r..."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Related supplementary info\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"44E4DB19E314EABB\" } }"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You may have noticed that iron and gold can also be boosted with honey —"
		""
		"Maybe it's time to upgrade your old lines?"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&mOriginally, crushing tuff yielded all four minerals — copper, zinc, iron, and gold — but I've changed the recipe."
		""
		"&7&mAfter all, tuff used to be non-renewable and now it is, so a small adjustment was only natural"
		""
		"Changed it back."
	]
	quest.49AA6727342CA7EB.quest_subtitle: "I reckon it'll work"
	quest.49AA6727342CA7EB.title: "S2.14.2 Mass-Producing Copper and Zinc"
	quest.49BEAE6B58A06418.quest_desc: [
		"You usually won't craft this — elite mobs with backpacks occasionally spawn in the wild, and their backpacks can contain the Jukebox Upgrade."
	]
	quest.49BEAE6B58A06418.title: "O2.17 Random Spawns in the Wild"
	quest.49E985AF8A08783D.quest_desc: [
		"111"
	]
	quest.49E985AF8A08783D.title: "O3.12 Upgrade 3"
	quest.49F0BD005AF49BA8.quest_desc: [
		"Crops obviously take time to grow, so instead of having the gantry shuttle back and forth constantly, starting it on a timer is the better choice."
		""
		"&aTips&r: This component requires Brass, so you can come back and upgrade your farm later."
	]
	quest.49F0BD005AF49BA8.title: "H1.7 Scheduled Round Trip"
	quest.49F272968741D3DD.quest_desc: [
		"The Weighted Ejector can transport items in full stacks, and the wiring is fairly flexible."
		""
		"It can also be placed between belts so scattered items accumulate into a stack&7 (configurable)&r before being fed onto the belt."
		""
		"&8Try standing on it yourself?"
	]
	quest.49F272968741D3DD.title: "3.3 \"Air Freight\""
	quest.4A218D10EEB4096E.quest_desc: [
		"The &edynamic contraption&r we're about to cover is one of Create's signature features, letting you build all sorts of imaginative things."
		""
		"&eSuper Glue&r can forcibly stick multiple blocks together to form a huge contraption — you'll need to craft it first."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Remember to turn the page."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If Super Glue is hard to come by right now, you can make do with blocks that stick together without it, like the ones the task asks for."
		""
		"Either way, you'll need Super Glue eventually, so you might as well make it."
		""
		"&7I've hyped it this much, just make one, make one, make one"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"No luck finding slime? No problem."
		""
		"Create added a recipe for Slime Balls — check JEI&7 (EMI)&r to see it."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Or follow this quest instead\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"70B69557EC69A476\" } }"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Contraption Components Overview\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1gCNkeGEJR?p=5\" } }"
	]
	quest.4A218D10EEB4096E.quest_subtitle: "Do this task first!"
	quest.4A218D10EEB4096E.title: "S1.7.1 That's Really Powerful"
	quest.4A371F65307F46FA.quest_desc: [
		"Rose Quartz, made by mixing quartz with redstone, is great for crafting Electron Tubes and building smarter machines."
		""
		"But Rose Quartz can't be used directly — you'll need to polish it with sandpaper first."
	]
	quest.4A371F65307F46FA.title: "2.3 Strawberry-Flavored Lollipop"
	quest.4A4217E0399BAFB4.quest_desc: [
		"It no longer passes through blocks, so it can be processed now."
	]
	quest.4A4217E0399BAFB4.title: "AC1.22.1 Stable Neutronium Ingot"
	quest.4A42C3CC52E9DD9B.quest_desc: [
		"Gantries are also great at managing farms — long strips of farmland, or even 3D farms (which are more complex, so I won't elaborate)."
		"Note that the gantry contraption can't pass through blocks, so keep its work area clear."
	]
	quest.4A42C3CC52E9DD9B.title: "H1.4 Crane Farm"
	quest.4A4B02E72782E04B.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrade all your weapons and tools — Resonators, Heavy Halberds, and the rest — to the Transcendence tier."
	]
	quest.4A4B02E72782E04B.title: "AC1.26.1 Multiphase Transcendent Alloy"
	quest.4A5694303D4111D3.quest_desc: [
		"Logistics options in the Andesite Age are limited, but combined with various containers&7 (like double chests and hoppers)&r, you can put together plenty of handy setups that pull off fairly complex functions."
	]
	quest.4A5694303D4111D3.title: "S3.4.1 Clever Contraptions"
	quest.4A5F6F14E790FA8E.quest_desc: [
		"Here are some handy little tools to make building physical structures easier."
	]
	quest.4A5F6F14E790FA8E.title: "Utility Tools"
	quest.4A6C41CA1B64E670.quest_desc: [
		"Same function as the Inventory Proxy, except it has no direction limit."
	]
	quest.4A6C41CA1B64E670.title: "O4.8 Inventory Interface"
	quest.4ABD50F701E7028B.quest_desc: [
		"AnvilCraft's Chute is more like a vanilla hopper, but it moves a full stack at a time and comes with a built-in 9-slot filter."
		""
		"&8Too bad the filter only supports whitelisting&r"
	]
	quest.4ABD50F701E7028B.title: "AC1.4.1 Yet Another Chute"
	quest.4B579F26CD36BE18.quest_desc: [
		"Production lines often end up with multiple items mixed together, and vanilla hoppers are clunky for sorting — the Toolbox makes it much easier."
		""
		"A single slot of the Toolbox stays occupied even when its item&7 (call it Item A)&r count is 0&7 (it only accepts Item A, storing nothing else)&r, until you clear it manually."
		""
		"Pair it with Andesite Funnels for sorting — whatever fits gets taken out, whatever doesn't stays."
		""
		"It has 8 slots, so one Toolbox can sort 1–8 kinds of items."
	]
	quest.4B579F26CD36BE18.title: "3.5 Sorting"
	quest.4B739F8C258BD0C4.quest_desc: [
		"In AnvilCraft, many templates need to be bought from villagers for your first copy, so a villager trading hall becomes a must."
	]
	quest.4B739F8C258BD0C4.title: "AC1.9 Villager Exchange"
	quest.4BD59307EB5C3634.quest_desc: [
		"Crude oil can also generate power — see the tutorial book."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Even if you keep topping it up, a batch of crude oil only burns for 10 minutes — but you can toss hot tungsten into a cauldron of crude oil to relight it."
	]
	quest.4BD59307EB5C3634.title: "AC1.18.1 Oil and Electricity"
	quest.4BD7ABC1477AF18C.quest_desc: [
		"One capacitor refills an Ionocraft's power by 50%."
	]
	quest.4BD7ABC1477AF18C.title: "AC1.20.2 Battery Life"
	quest.4BF63C881904FBC1.quest_desc: [
		"Mobs defeated by a Warden's Sonic Boom drop an extra Echo Shard."
	]
	quest.4BF63C881904FBC1.title: "Sonic Boom"
	quest.4C140FE7AA365101.quest_desc: [
		"Any ore that has a \"&eRaw Ore Block&r\" form can be mass-produced via Laser Mining."
		""
		"See the \"Laser Mining\" and \"Mineral Fountain\" sections of the &eAnvilCraft guide&r."
		""
		"&aTips&r: You can use an &eAndesite Generator&r to generate power."
		""
		"The &eMineral Fountain&7 (a multiblock structure)&r also produces Cinerite."
	]
	quest.4C140FE7AA365101.title: "Laser Mining"
	quest.4CE6FD6210F20209.quest_desc: [
		"Drop! Why the heck won't it drop! Drop for me!"
		""
		"&aTips&r: The Amethyst Sword comes with Beheading — click the Amethyst Sword in the rewards to see the recipe."
	]
	quest.4CE6FD6210F20209.title: "S1.10.1 Decapitation Operation"
	quest.4D2314DA32426B80.quest_desc: [
		"Most crops can be harvested automatically with a &eMechanical Harvester&r."
		""
		"Just pick a &econtraption&r you like, stick the Harvester onto it with &eSuper Glue&r, then drive the contraption through the crops."
	]
	quest.4D2314DA32426B80.title: "F1.11 Automated Harvesting"
	quest.4D26957E0D0435EC.quest_desc: [
		"Copper gear is here too!"
		""
		"This diving set consumes air from the &eBacktank&r to let you breathe underwater."
		""
		"Copper boots also stop &ebelts&r from carrying you away."
		""
		"&aTips&r: 'Optional' subtasks mean you can claim the reward even without the Backtank."
		""
		"The first few quests are just handing out freebies, after all."
	]
	quest.4D26957E0D0435EC.title: "S1.3.4 Copper Diving Suit"
	quest.4D5DDEFA6A3A6697.quest_desc: [
		"A beefed-up version of the Shaft — basically identical when transmitting."
		""
		"Strangely enough, a powered Gantry Shaft paired with the Gantry is indeed a way to transmit stress — surprisingly handy when deploying &eCrushing Wheels&r."
	]
	quest.4D5DDEFA6A3A6697.quest_subtitle: "A weird niche idea"
	quest.4D9D414F0BEFE6C5.quest_desc: [
		"Planting mushrooms on &erich soil&r grows fungal colonies you can harvest with a Mechanical Harvester."
		""
		"Also, if you're in a hurry, you can spout liquid fertilizer to get mushrooms quickly, and it's cheap too."
	]
	quest.4D9D414F0BEFE6C5.quest_subtitle: "I'm not the god of medicine"
	quest.4D9D414F0BEFE6C5.title: "HS5.4.3.5 Infusing Souls"
	quest.4DCED2C3B2C8D63A.quest_desc: [
		"This little crystal nucleus has the potential to grow into a full piece of Ancient Debris — but how do you make it grow?"
	]
	quest.4DCED2C3B2C8D63A.title: "S2.2.12 Mass-Producing Netherite"
	quest.4DE6D8746807963A.quest_desc: [
		"Hiss..."
		""
		"Have you been playing AnvilCraft instead?"
	]
	quest.4DE6D8746807963A.title: "O2.15 Ultimate Dedication"
	quest.4DEE2D8CF9D0C8EA.quest_desc: [
		"Sophisticated Backpacks' Magnet Upgrade collects specified items over a large area — great for this spot too."
	]
	quest.4DEE2D8CF9D0C8EA.title: "S2.11.3 Yes, This Is a Backpack"
	quest.4E02F938DE948035.quest_desc: [
		"&ePowdery Cane&r grows &ePowdery Cannons&r — harvest them with a &eKnife&r, or use a &eMechanical Arm&r to pick them automatically."
		""
		"Both Powdery Cane and Chorus Flowers can be harvested with a &eMechanical Saw&r."
		""
		"&7Too lazy to write a detailed explanation — go look it up yourself oao"
	]
	quest.4E02F938DE948035.title: "F1.6 Give It a Whack Anyway"
	quest.4E20BD5FFEB221D0.quest_desc: [
		"Same as before — you probably won't need it."
		""
		"Again, it's here just for symmetry."
	]
	quest.4E20BD5FFEB221D0.quest_subtitle: "What are you for...?"
	quest.4E20BD5FFEB221D0.title: "S2.2.15 Alchemy's Unexpected Byproducts"
	quest.4E369AF79E286E91.quest_desc: [
		"Liquid Experience can be stored in Fluid Tanks; right-click an Experience Hatch to drain the experience you're carrying."
	]
	quest.4E369AF79E286E91.title: "E1.3 Storing Experience"
	quest.4E3CFC1C3EDC6E56.quest_desc: [
		"If you're bored, you can also try making some powerful weapons and tools."
		""
		"They come from AnvilCraft, but I've written some recipes so you can make them the Create way."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Use JEI&7 (EMI)&r to look up the recipes."
		""
		"These were actually all mentioned in earlier side chapters:"
		"{ \"text\": \"Royal Steel\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"3B6D08C930787F82\" } }"
		"{ \"text\": \"Frost Metal Ingot\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"203380ED9BC38B15\" } }"
		"{ \"text\": \"Ember Metal Ingot\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"4716E23A66F62EE2\" } }"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Looks like a hassle to craft? Endgame content is bound to be a bit more complex..."
		""
		"Besides, AnvilCraft's own recipes aren't exactly simple either."
		""
		"Of course, you can just climb AnvilCraft's tech tree and make it without Create."
	]
	quest.4E3CFC1C3EDC6E56.title: "S2.17.5 First Step to a God-Tier Tool"
	quest.4E479B2AC0165C0E.quest_desc: [
		"Trading with villagers gets you Emeralds."
		""
		"Use a &eTrading Depot&r to farm Emeralds automatically in bulk."
	]
	quest.4E479B2AC0165C0E.title: "Villager Trading"
	quest.4E53611D08E4513D.quest_desc: [
		"Holding&7 (or wearing)&r an Emerald Amulet makes villagers give you discounts — as for getting one..."
		""
		"Dying while holding an Amulet Box with a Totem of Undying inside has a chance to drop the matching amulet :P"
		""
		"I've also added some other ways to get them — you should be able to see them in JEI&7 (EMI)&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Now, holding a &eweapon enchanted with Looting&r, &8&mkill&r... pet the villagers, and there's a chance they'll drop an Emerald Amulet."
		""
		"&8&mI wrote the amulet's description myself — it might be wrong, so tell me if you spot an error."
		""
		"&8&mThe tutorial book used to have a dedicated page introducing amulets, but it's locked by default, so I went ahead and deleted the amulet description."
		""
		"&8&mWait, why did I patch up the old description while not covering the new one...? I'll just leave it."
		""
		"&8It's all complete now, so I'll just delete it all."
	]
	quest.4E53611D08E4513D.title: "AC1.9.2 Old Pal, Cut Me a Deal"
	quest.4E5F7465E4545CC9.quest_desc: [
		"Fluid Drawers can store large amounts of fluid, and keep the liquid inside when mined — very convenient."
		""
		"Conservatives can skip drawers and just use a Cart Assembler to move Fluid Tanks around."
		""
		"&8They can't replace Fluid Tanks for building a Steam Boiler, though."
	]
	quest.4E5F7465E4545CC9.title: "S2.6.4 Handier Fluid Tanks"
	quest.4E9D7D15638B9AF3.title: "Mob Farming"
	quest.4EFB4B43B0977EA5.quest_desc: [
		"The controller and its extensions can have custom textures too."
	]
	quest.4EFB4B43B0977EA5.title: "O3.8 Decorate It Too"
	quest.4F0981C6A7D6C9D5.quest_desc: [
		"A Mechanical Bearing spins attached structures when powered, making it great for small tree farms and farms."
		""
		"The farther from the axle, the faster the linear speed and the higher the workpieces' efficiency... wow!"
		""
		"Mechanical Bearing structures can pass through walls and crush any overlapping blocks when they solidify — so you can also use it to break blocks cheaply and quickly."
	]
	quest.4F0981C6A7D6C9D5.title: "S1.7.10 It's Spinning!"
	quest.4F6BF99936ED5ACB.quest_desc: [
		"You use a lot of redstone, so this recipe is surprisingly useful."
	]
	quest.4F6BF99936ED5ACB.title: "S2.2.4 Mass-Producing Redstone"
	quest.4F79E772A0B73E7A.quest_desc: [
		"The biggest difference is that it moves a full stack at a time and supports filtering — awesome."
	]
	quest.4F79E772A0B73E7A.title: "4.1 Get an Upgrade!"
	quest.4F849B5CCEA84C30.quest_desc: [
		"Like the iron line, the gold line also starts from cobblestone."
		""
		"You can build a new cobblestone generator, or have the gold line pull automatically from the warehouse&7 (the iron line's generator)&r."
	]
	quest.4F849B5CCEA84C30.title: "H3.1 Mass-Producing Cobblestone"
	quest.50815C1D74E30C19.quest_desc: [
		"The only aircraft that needs no fuel."
		""
		"Immersive Aircraft also adds airships and all sorts of upgrades — check them out if you're interested."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Search \"&e@aircraft&r\" in JEI&7 (EMI)&r to see related content."
	]
	quest.50815C1D74E30C19.title: "O5.4 Budget Aircraft"
	quest.5094D6E28313B8AD.quest_desc: [
		"With the Deployer, you can cram a pile of gears into one tiny component, building smarter machines."
		""
		"Don't ask how it fits — &ethe Deployer's power is absolute!"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Check the Deployer's Ponder&7 (mainly part 3)&r"
		""
		"&eSequenced Assembly&r just means processing from left to right, one step at a time."
		""
		"Try linking the stages together with &ebelts&r or similar."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"'Hand of God' is just a nickname for the &eDeployer&r — since its actions mimic a player's, it often produces baffling&8 (or hilarious?)&r results."
		""
		"The process of making Precision Mechanisms is called &eSequenced Assembly&r — a signature Create mechanic."
		""
		"This pack adds some fun Sequenced Assembly recipes on top of Create's own — give them a try when you find them."
	]
	quest.5094D6E28313B8AD.quest_subtitle: "The power of Deployer is absolute!"
	quest.5094D6E28313B8AD.title: "2.5 Subspace Compression Technology"
	quest.50DBE9905738208D.quest_desc: [
		"Brass Funnels, Smart Chutes, and Brass Tunnels can all be filtered — let's send the Toolbox into retirement."
	]
	quest.50DBE9905738208D.title: "4.5 Smart Filtering"
	quest.51305FC5A0A7542E.quest_desc: [
		"Items without a crushing recipe will be ground to bits in the Crushing Wheel — if you can, definitely set up a filter at the input!"
		""
		"Just put an &eAttribute Filter&r in the filter slot of a &eBrass Funnel&r or &eSmart Chute&r."
	]
	quest.51305FC5A0A7542E.title: "! Notice !"
	quest.518764631D4ECC3E.quest_desc: [
		"The Sophisticated Backpacks' Compacting Upgrade quickly compacts lots of items of many kinds, and the backpack itself holds a ton. It looks out of place at the end of a production line, but it's convenient."
		""
		"&8- Are you really a backpack?"
		""
		"&8- I think I am."
	]
	quest.518764631D4ECC3E.title: "S2.10.3 Even Better?!"
	quest.51D5A7E5C6A4D2E8.quest_desc: [
		"Besides feeding Blaze Burners directly, lava can also be made into Blaze Cakes."
		""
		"A Blaze Burner fed Blaze Cakes enters the &esuperheated&r state, which can push a Steam Boiler to level 18&7 (though you'll rarely use that much stress)&r."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"It's really simple\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"5A05710292F49280\" } }"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Mass-producing Netherrack is a hassle, so a 24/7 Blaze Cake line may not be the best idea — try the new Create 6.0 logistics components to produce them automatically on demand!"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Factory Gauge\", \"underlined\": true,\"color\":\"blue\", \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"23636E72D5D35C87\" } }"
	]
	quest.51D5A7E5C6A4D2E8.quest_subtitle: "Very simple"
	quest.51D5A7E5C6A4D2E8.title: "H2.6.2 Delicious Little Cakes"
	quest.5235B0EC83F33C50.quest_desc: [
		"By crushing minerals or defeating mobs with a Deployer, you can get Nuggets of Experience — a handy medium for storing experience. Create: Enchantment Industry expands the experience mechanics quite a bit — dig in if you're interested."
	]
	quest.5235B0EC83F33C50.title: "S2.4.2 Nuggets of Experience"
	quest.5248106EB435E7D0.quest_desc: [
		"End Cities have been revamped — bigger, better, and packed with more loot!"
		""
		"End Ships also spawn more often now, making Dragon Heads and Elytra easier to get."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Firework Rockets can also be mass-produced automatically."
		""
		"Why not design a line for them and hook it into your logistics?"
	]
	quest.5248106EB435E7D0.title: "S2.17.3 Mom, I Can Fly!"
	quest.525AD6D3FC562C55.quest_desc: [
		"Some advanced resources require collision crafting, which needs an accelerator setup and an explosion-proof collision chamber."
		""
		"&aTips&r: See the tutorial book for how to set up the collision rig."
		""
		"Also, transmission poles shut down when powered by redstone, so you can turn off the accelerator and free up power."
	]
	quest.525AD6D3FC562C55.title: "AC1.21.2 Art Is an Explosion"
	quest.5288F7E78271279C.quest_desc: [
		"Netherrack is everywhere, and it also has a crafting recipe&7 (a bit of a hassle, though)&f."
		""
		"Better to collect a big batch at once and not worry about it for a long time."
	]
	quest.5288F7E78271279C.quest_subtitle: "EZ!"
	quest.5288F7E78271279C.title: "H4.1 It's Everywhere"
	quest.529A777813CAC6FF.quest_desc: [
		"Create provides plenty of extra redstone components to help you wire things up better."
		""
		"Redstone isn't strictly necessary. But if you have complex needs later, or want cross-mod automation, don't forget they exist."
	]
	quest.529A777813CAC6FF.quest_subtitle: "Hey, it's me, Redstone System!"
	quest.529A777813CAC6FF.title: "S1.11.4 Nifty Gadget"
	quest.52B60DBE76B4794B.quest_desc: [
		"Like Netherite, use the Smithing Table to upgrade items to their Royal Steel versions."
	]
	quest.52B60DBE76B4794B.title: "AC1.10 Get an Upgrade!"
	quest.52D1638587ADF907.quest_desc: [
		"A Mechanical Bearing with a Harvester can automatically manage a circular farm — very handy."
		"The bearing can't hold water, but a Shaft can."
		"You can also stack Mechanical Bearings to build a wheat tower if you like."
	]
	quest.52D1638587ADF907.title: "H1.3 Mechanical Bearing"
	quest.52F16F3FED5488ED.quest_desc: [
		"Since AnvilCraft is installed, give it a try — its built-in tutorial book is quite detailed."
		""
		"Like Create, hold the book and press &eCtrl&r to 'Ponder' AnvilCraft items."
		""
		"To keep you from getting overwhelmed, I'll walk you through the main line here — explore the side quests at your own pace."
		""
		"&aTips&r: AnvilCraft's content can simplify many Create machines."
		""
		"Likewise, Create can simplify AnvilCraft's machines."
		""
		"Great for practicing cross-mod machine design."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&7&mDid you know: AnvilCraft was making Ponder scenes for its items!"
		""
		"They're done, but the dev keeps updating AnvilCraft without updating the Ponder addon, so it's full of bugs now."
		""
		"What can you do? Just go along with it."
	]
	quest.52F16F3FED5488ED.title: "AC1.1 Since You're Here"
	quest.5329D3AD8C264AAE.quest_desc: [
		"Here's an example — automatic crushing — to help you understand."
		""
		"You don't need to complete these quests; the arrows between them only show how the blocks connect."
	]
	quest.5329D3AD8C264AAE.title: "Automation Example"
	quest.540E288CA40A579F.quest_desc: [
		"It treats the block of air in front of it as a container, so item drops in that space get pulled into the storage network&7 (drops left unpicked for too long are auto-cleaned by the game)&r."
		""
		"Correspondingly, it also tosses received items out the front."
	]
	quest.540E288CA40A579F.title: "O4.9 Open Box"
	quest.5428A8E531D969A5.quest_desc: [
		"When an &eenchanted&r Eight to One Smithing Template is destroyed&7 (TNT recommended)&r, it randomly picks 4 of its enchantments and produces the matching smithing templates."
		""
		"If the 4 templates are all different, you get an extra &eTranscendium Smithing Template&r."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Use an Ember Anvil to put unrelated enchantments on items."
		""
		"Also, it's recommended to put &e15+&r enchantments on the Eight to One template before rolling for the Transcendium one."
	]
	quest.5428A8E531D969A5.title: "AC1.25 Eight to One Smithing Template"
	quest.544B8D112E834FEA.quest_desc: [
		"Hover over the item icon to see the description."
	]
	quest.544B8D112E834FEA.title: "O3.10 Upgrade 1"
	quest.54953E46874B97F4.quest_desc: [
		"Kaleidoscope's foods each have their own character, and many have models you can place."
		""
		"Like Farmer's Delight's pots, Kaleidoscope's pots need to sit on a &eheat source&r to work."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"With the &eCutting Board&r, hold &eingredients in your offhand&r and keep &eright-clicking&r with a &eKitchen Knife&r in your main hand to chop quickly."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Using a &eStockpot&r, first pour in the &ebroth&7 (like water)&r, then follow the recipe&7 (check JEI)&r, right-click&r to add the right amount of ingredients, &ecover it&r, and &ewait&r for it to cook."
		""
		"&eOnce cooked&r, lift the lid and right-click with a bowl to scoop out the food."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Using a &eWok&r, first add &eoil&r, then follow the recipe&7 (check JEI)&r, right-click&r to add the right amount of ingredients, then right-click with a &espatula&r to stir-fry."
		""
		"&eOnce cooked&r, quickly scoop it out with a bowl or rice&7 (or it'll burn)&r."
	]
	quest.54953E46874B97F4.title: "F3.3 Kaleidoscope"
	quest.54B68217423D0972.quest_desc: [
		"With Enchanting Templates, you no longer need to craft a pile of diamond pickaxes, enchant them separately, and hammer them together on an anvil."
	]
	quest.54B68217423D0972.title: "E1.8 Template"
	quest.54FBCC6AA2A3DA2A.quest_desc: [
		"Once connected to the Storage Controller, it acts as a proxy for it, expanding the drawer system's effective range."
	]
	quest.54FBCC6AA2A3DA2A.title: "S2.12.4 Storage Expander"
	quest.5536784AB66FDC28.quest_desc: [
		"A regular crafting table can't handle big builds like the Crushing Wheel — you'll need the bigger, clunkier Mechanical Crafter."
		""
		"&aTips&r: 21 Mechanical Crafters draw a hefty amount of stress."
		""
		"If stress is tight, try running the Crafters at &7extremely&r low speeds."
	]
	quest.5536784AB66FDC28.quest_subtitle: "This route is the main questline"
	quest.5536784AB66FDC28.title: "2.8 The Mysterious Mechanical Crafter"
	quest.553B73C3A38CC394.quest_desc: [
		"Quests fall into three categories: Main, Side, and Extension."
		""
		"&eMain quests&r:"
		""
		"Your primary goals — I recommend finishing these first."
		""
		"Main quests span two chapters: &eAndesite Age&r and &eBrass Age&r. Their titles clearly start with numbers, so you can easily look up the &nwalkthrough&r&7 (not done yet)&r or ask for help when stuck."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eSide quests&r:"
		""
		"Your secondary goals. They aren't required, but I recommend trying them in your spare time."
		""
		"These branch off from the main quests and start with &eS&r&7ide (side)&r + a number. Usually they supplement the main line."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eExtension quests&r:"
		""
		"A mixed bag of tasks you can work on when bored."
		""
		"These start with fairly arbitrary letter+number codes, making them easy to index and tell apart from the others. They're shown in their own chapters with no fixed theme."
		""
		"Of course, nobody's forcing you to do quests — play the pack however you like."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Can't turn in a quest? You probably haven't finished its prerequisites. You can:"
		""
		"①Check the &etop&r of the quest's &edetail page&r and click the left/right ▶ triangles to quickly jump to its prerequisites or follow-ups."
		""
		"②Look at the &ebottom-right corner&r of the whole FTB Quests &einterface&r, click the ✏ pencil to enter edit mode. This reveals all hidden quests, and right-clicking lets you force-complete or reset quests."
	]
	quest.553B73C3A38CC394.title: "Priorities"
	quest.5548825817C0DF6C.quest_desc: [
		"A machine that can hover — great for building."
		""
		"Though most of the time you'd build with a Schematicannon anyway."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Schematicannon\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"6B151160907137A0\" } }"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Ionocraft\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"30BE06340C85D4A6\" } }"
	]
	quest.5548825817C0DF6C.title: "O5.3 Construction Helper"
	quest.55DEC8C92162AD0E.quest_desc: [
		"Smelting a Gem Block&7 (usually a Block of Emerald)&r turns it into Melt Gem."
		""
		"Throw a gem into the Melt Gem and &etime warp&r it to get a matching gem block."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Getting emeralds in bulk\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"2709CC4F17953FB8\" } }"
	]
	quest.55DEC8C92162AD0E.title: "AC1.16.2 Gem Transformation"
	quest.5616A7673F58B988.quest_desc: [
		"Use some method — like a Chute — to feed items from the small buffer storage into the Crushing Wheel."
	]
	quest.5616A7673F58B988.title: "Feed"
	quest.56173986CFBAFCBC.quest_desc: [
		"Dripstone Blocks and Pointed Dripstone generate naturally underground."
		""
		"Use a &eProspector Pickaxe&r to locate them quickly."
	]
	quest.56357E854A76AA08.quest_desc: [
		"A very convenient fluid source — the Water Generator Upgrade even works in the Nether."
	]
	quest.56357E854A76AA08.title: "O3.18 Goodbye, Pointed Dripstone Cauldron"
	quest.565FC8E39E2DAD09.quest_desc: [
		"A crafting table built into the storage terminal."
		""
		"Works together with JEI&7 (EMI)&r."
	]
	quest.565FC8E39E2DAD09.title: "O4.3 Crafting Terminal"
	quest.56BBF2993021E622.quest_desc: [
		"This pack includes two main cooking mods — &eFarmer's Delight&7 (and some of its addons)&r and &eKaleidoscope&r — each with its own style:"
		""
		"Farmer's Delight has a rich menu that's relatively simple to make and easy to mass-produce. It mainly provides nourishment, and some dishes are even crafting ingredients."
		""
		"Kaleidoscope's dishes are more complex to make but more refined. Many grant powerful potion effects, making them great to eat before heading out to explore."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Don't forget you can use JEI&7 (EMI)&r to look up any dish's recipe."
	]
	quest.56BBF2993021E622.quest_subtitle: "\"Retired Mechanic's Restaurant in Another World\""
	quest.56BBF2993021E622.title: "F3.1 Delicious Food, at Your Fingertips"
	quest.5728E5DDFEC65C1B.quest_desc: [
		"Placing a large Item Vault under a chute so everything funnels into one container is also a way to collect."
	]
	quest.5728E5DDFEC65C1B.title: "S2.11.2 Large Size Containers"
	quest.5738B98A06AA37B3.quest_desc: [
		"It can suck up nearby players' experience and collect spilled Nuggets of Experience."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Mobs killed by a Deployer always drop Nuggets of Experience, so you don't need this for a mob farm."
	]
	quest.5738B98A06AA37B3.title: "E1.4 A Gadget"
	quest.57702AFB888B4828.quest_desc: [
		"AnvilCraft adds some Sliding Rails, similar to water streams, that can transport items in bulk — without the lag."
	]
	quest.57702AFB888B4828.title: "S3.2.3 Ice Road"
	quest.57CC8596A6F452F1.quest_desc: [
		"Lava buckets are also a fuel, and they burn for a long time — great for Blaze Burners. As for mass-producing them..."
	]
	quest.57CC8596A6F452F1.title: "S2.6.1 Mass-Producing Fuel: Lava"
	quest.57CE0B284AFB79CA.quest_desc: [
		"Compared to propellers, thrusters are a cruder power source — they're powerful, but they consume propellant."
		""
		"Vector Thrusters are a more advanced power source — mainly because they're easier to control."
		""
		"Generating power is a hassle, so a &eLiquid Vector Thruster&r is more recommended."
		""
		"Finally, the &eCreative Vector Thruster&r does have a crafting recipe."
	]
	quest.57DD30E6D5A0F3F0.quest_desc: [
		"This part requires Brass to craft."
	]
	quest.57DD30E6D5A0F3F0.title: "Statement"
	quest.57E4FB9B8140169F.quest_desc: [
		"Ghasts are most common in &eSoul Sand Valleys&r — it's recommended to bring a &eJetpack&r or a &ePotato Cannon&r."
		""
		"You can also build a ghast farm in the air above a Soul Sand Valley — all you need is an &eEncased Fan&r and a &eScattering Net&r."
	]
	quest.57E4FB9B8140169F.title: "H5.5 Bulk Brewing"
	quest.581B7F6328943A77.quest_desc: [
		"The Crushing Wheel is an upgraded Millstone — it can grind 64 wheat at once."
		""
		"You probably can't craft it yet — come back and upgrade once you have Brass."
	]
	quest.581B7F6328943A77.title: "H1.9 Crushing Wheel"
	quest.585E803B363CB5BB.quest_desc: [
		"The &eHand of God&r&7 (Deployer)&r can milk cows with a bucket, and using a milk bucket on an &eItem Drain&r empties it automatically."
		""
		"Mobs&7 (cows)&r that touch a &eSeat&r will sit on it, and you can even force mobs onto a Seat with a lead."
		""
		"Just a small automatic milking line built with Deployers is enough to fill your tanks to bursting."
	]
	quest.585E803B363CB5BB.title: "F2.3 Endless Milk Source"
	quest.58DC2571CADB5D6B.quest_desc: [
		"The Basin automatically pushes products into any open container in the 4 adjacent blocks, 1 block below."
		""
		"So which ones count as open containers?"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Written here\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"0F492741358DF5E0\" } }"
	]
	quest.58DC2571CADB5D6B.title: "S3.1.1 Auto-Export Products"
	quest.59AFEFB4D426325F.quest_desc: [
		"Not bad — bring it along if you have spare slots."
	]
	quest.59AFEFB4D426325F.title: "O2.23 You Probably Won't Get Used to It"
	quest.59DB538B35233DE2.quest_desc: [
		"These are milestone quests — aim for them when you're not sure what to do."
		""
		"Besides the basic objectives, milestone quests also have bonus objectives starting with \"▷\" on the &enext page&r of the description, like..."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"▷ This is a bonus objective — try completing it"
		""
		"▷ This is also a bonus objective — usually they get harder further down"
		""
		"▷ Try completing the bonus objectives — it might level up your Create skills"
	]
	quest.59DB538B35233DE2.quest_subtitle: "[WIP] means unfinished"
	quest.59DB538B35233DE2.title: "The Beginning of Everything"
	quest.59EE3CF0ABCE9FEE.quest_desc: [
		"Despite the name, the Potato Cannon can fire more than potatoes."
		""
		"Different vegetables have different effects."
		""
		"&7You can also fire fish, golden apples, even Blaze Cakes..."
	]
	quest.59EE3CF0ABCE9FEE.title: "F1.14 The Age of Firearms!"
	quest.5A0138E038698FF4.quest_desc: [
		"Clutch:"
		""
		"Cuts off stress when it receives a redstone signal — used to &esplit your stress network&r."
		""
		"Use it to isolate fragile machines&7 (like a Boiler)&r or rarely-used-but-necessary machines&7 (like the Mechanical Crafter)&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Gearshift:"
		""
		"Reverses the rotation direction when it receives a redstone signal — usually paired with &econtraptions&r."
		""
		"If you just want a fixed direction change, use a &eGearbox&r directly."
		""
		"&7Don't worry, there's a reverse!# Feed it a redstone signal"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Adjustable Chain Gearshift:"
		""
		"Lets a redstone signal control the speed — usually paired with &econtraptions&r."
	]
	quest.5A0138E038698FF4.quest_subtitle: "Simple and basic functions are the cornerstone of complex functions"
	quest.5A0138E038698FF4.title: "Redstone Control"
	quest.5A05710292F49280.quest_desc: [
		"Finally, inject lava into the cake base, and the little cake for your Blaze Burners is done!"
		""
		"Consider hooking it into your logistics system?"
	]
	quest.5A05710292F49280.title: "H4.4 Delicious Little Cakes"
	quest.5A620F05AAD3F8A5.quest_desc: [
		"Right-clicking while holding a package throws it — so can we develop some fun activities with that?"
	]
	quest.5A620F05AAD3F8A5.title: "A2.12.1 Slam Dunk"
	quest.5A83C7FC4C384938.quest_desc: [
		"Stick a sign on the &cPackager&r with an address written on it, and the package will be automatically carried by Chain Conveyors to the matching Frogport."
		"For example, write 'Warehouse' on the sign here — once a Frogport hangs the package on the chain, it'll be delivered to the Frogport named 'Warehouse'."
	]
	quest.5A83C7FC4C384938.title: "Guide the Way"
	quest.5A9DDD662F61550D.quest_desc: [
		"The Royal Anvil never breaks from falls and won't refuse to work for being 'too expensive'&8 (though you'll probably still not afford the XP)&r."
		""
		"The Royal Grindstone removes curses and enchantment penalties, giving &eCursed Gold&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"[ \"Anvils clearly need lots of experience, so you might want to check out \", { \"text\": \"Create: Enchantment Industry\",\"color\":blue, \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"30DA2989D5BB1C21\" } }, \" content.\" ]"
		""
		"Or you can convert spare lapis lazuli into &eNuggets of Experience&r — the yield is decent too."
	]
	quest.5A9DDD662F61550D.title: "AC1.13 Royal Anvil and Royal Grindstone"
	quest.5ABB862DDC32F580.quest_desc: [
		"Put the second one in the work area, like near the Crushing Wheels."
	]
	quest.5AC2947140295B05.quest_desc: [
		"The Sprinkler and Spout can extract liquids with high efficiency."
		""
		"Similarly, you can use an Item Drain to pour liquids back."
	]
	quest.5AC2947140295B05.quest_subtitle: "Pour the liquid in..."
	quest.5AC2947140295B05.title: "S2.2.16 Take Out the Potion..."
	quest.5AF27B54E33991CF.quest_desc: [
		"Put &ezinc&r and &ecopper&r into the Mechanical Mixer, feed the Blaze Burner &efuel&7 (like coal)&r, and you'll get Brass."
		""
		"Time to start a new chapter!"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Quest descriptions will get shorter from here on — don't forget you can use &eJEI&7 (EMI)&r to look up recipes."
	]
	quest.5AF27B54E33991CF.title: "1.11 Brass!"
	quest.5B26BC7019FB483C.quest_desc: [
		"The &ePortable Engine&r is a very convenient stress source from &eCreate: Aeronautics&r, designed for use on aircraft or cars."
		""
		"Although it is not very efficient, it is enough for your early game."
	]
	quest.5B26BC7019FB483C.title: "A1.6.2 Portable Engine"
	quest.5B63C5D6D8BF040D.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Arm can transport items in groups, and it has few placement restrictions, so it is rarely obstructed."
	]
	quest.5B63C5D6D8BF040D.title: "4.3 3D Transport"
	quest.5B74744EE5D552DC.quest_desc: [
		"Similar to the Crafting Upgrade, but there is not much need to carry it around."
	]
	quest.5B74744EE5D552DC.title: "O2.18 Useful, but Not Much"
	quest.5B7CAF6382995374.quest_desc: [
		"The Compacting Drawer from Functional Storage can automatically compress and store items, letting you take out blocks, ingots, or nuggets directly &7(no manual crafting needed)&r — very convenient."
	]
	quest.5B7CAF6382995374.title: "S2.10.2 A More Convenient Option"
	quest.5BA98A1B2E5358F3.quest_desc: [
		"After &eHaunting&r, stone becomes infested stone, and breaking infested stone spawns silverfish."
		""
		"Mass-killing silverfish to gain experience is a great idea."
	]
	quest.5BA98A1B2E5358F3.quest_subtitle: "Cobblestone gives birth to all things"
	quest.5BA98A1B2E5358F3.title: "ES1.2.2 Silverfish Experience Machine"
	quest.5BCB153F845192CB.quest_desc: [
		"An &eEncased Fan&r mob farm is very convenient — killing mobs with a &eDeployer&7 (Hand of God)&r also lets you enjoy the Looting enchantment."
		""
		"But if you don't want a mob farm, crushing &eBlaze Burners&r is also an option."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Moving monster spawners\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"417DDED017FF632B\"}}"
	]
	quest.5BCB153F845192CB.title: "H5.2.2 Infinite Power"
	quest.5C4E861F641219F0.quest_desc: [
		"A drawer locked with the Configuration Tool has the same traits as a Toolbox; paired with a controller, it can also wirelessly sort and transfer items."
	]
	quest.5C4E861F641219F0.title: "H1.11 Drawer Sorting"
	quest.5C64A338D885958B.quest_desc: [
		"Haunt sand in bulk to turn it into soul sand."
	]
	quest.5C64A338D885958B.title: "H3.3 Haunting"
	quest.5C981487B1D809D8.quest_desc: [
		"The best backpack in the overworld."
	]
	quest.5C981487B1D809D8.title: "O2.9 Reaching the Overworld's Highest Peak"
	quest.5CF3E224E58145A8.quest_desc: [
		"With a conveyor belt and a funnel, you can automatically feed Crushing Wheels placed horizontally or lying flat."
		""
		"&aTips&r: There are pictures on the next page."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Example diagram:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/s2_9_1.png width:256 height:142 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5CF3E224E58145A8.title: "S2.9.1 Horizontal Crushing"
	quest.5D1434F62FCEF197.quest_desc: [
		"You should have noticed there's a minimap in the upper-right corner of the screen. Press &eJ&r to view it fullscreen."
		""
		"Likewise, you can change it to &eM&r or any key you like."
		""
		"&7I plan to change the default key to M at the official release. If it isn't, then I forgot."
	]
	quest.5D1434F62FCEF197.title: "Travel Map"
	quest.5D769EF387D41C44.quest_desc: [
		"The Transcendence Resonator can be used as a pickaxe, axe, shovel, or hoe for rapid mining."
		""
		"Hold &eLeft Alt&r to switch modes; then you can also use each mode's right-click function — for example, stripping bark with the axe mode."
		""
		"Use the Four to One Smithing Template and a Resonator Core at the Ember Smithing Table to craft the Transcendence Resonator."
	]
	quest.5D769EF387D41C44.title: "S2.17.7 Multi-Purpose Tool"
	quest.5DEC221707659F22.quest_desc: [
		"The Storage Controller can create a drawer network and interact with the outside on behalf of all containers in the network. The network doesn't require drawers to touch the controller directly, so it can also transfer items wirelessly."
		"Two controllers cannot link to each other, and a drawer cannot be connected to two controllers."
	]
	quest.5DEC221707659F22.title: "O3.5 Drawer Network"
	quest.5DFC74E8F4776AFF.quest_desc: [
		"Hand-craft Wheat Flour with a water bucket to make Dough."
		""
		"You can also use the Encased Fan's &ebulk washing&r to make Dough at a much larger scale."
	]
	quest.5DFC74E8F4776AFF.title: "S1.7.11 Not Edible Yet"
	quest.5E2F67A9E4001AB1.quest_desc: [
		"These are the endgame sets for AnvilCraft!"
		""
		"But... there don't seem to be any monsters left to fight. How about adding some dungeon or BOSS Rush mods?"
		""
		"&8You can pick some mods you're interested in and add them yourself."
	]
	quest.5E2F67A9E4001AB1.quest_subtitle: "Reunion! Time to wrap dumplings!"
	quest.5E2F67A9E4001AB1.title: "AC1.26.2 Terrifyingly Strong"
	quest.5E6AC4D5CEFF7861.quest_desc: [
		"It's convenient to hook it up at the end of your ore processing line."
	]
	quest.5E6AC4D5CEFF7861.title: "O2.26 This Makes Compact Drawers Look Bad"
	quest.5EDEAC56DF308BBD.quest_desc: [
		"At this point, you already have a complete logistics system!"
		""
		"Try to connect all devices to this system."
	]
	quest.5EDEAC56DF308BBD.title: "3.12 Ultimate Mastery"
	quest.5EFE7FF5F215DEB3.title: "Create"
	quest.5F052C4E1F23717A.quest_desc: [
		"Besides portable engines, there are some more advanced stress sources."
		""
		"The &eStirling Engine&r produces 4096su of stress at &e256&r RPM."
		""
		"The two &eCompact Engines&r — Hydraulic and Wind — generate 8192su of stress without fuel, but only spin at 16 RPM."
		""
		"If your structure needs a huge amount of stress, don't forget the &eBoiler&7 (steam engine)&r — each Boiler level can output &e16384&r su of stress."
		""
		"&7Liquid Burners are not that great"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"And finally, the &eCreative Motor&r has a crafting recipe, so it will surely meet your stress needs."
	]
	quest.5F052C4E1F23717A.title: "More Portable Stress Sources"
	quest.5F14E48DD9F87225.quest_desc: [
		"A very useful anvil. When the upper magnet is deactivated, it will produce a falling phantom &7 (which can pass through leaves, but unfortunately cannot pass through Create funnels) &r for anvil processing."
		""
		"&aTips&r: See the tutorial book for details."
	]
	quest.5F14E48DD9F87225.title: "AC1.20.3 Phantom Anvil"
	quest.5F838CB565BAEE16.quest_desc: [
		"Decorative item that paints cables to look like blocks."
		""
		"This way you can bury the cables in walls, ceilings, or floors."
	]
	quest.5F838CB565BAEE16.title: "O4.14 Dyeing"
	quest.5F91CA3FD1CD4D40.quest_desc: [
		"The Encased Fan can blow entities around&7 (like that &8&mannoying&r&7 villager)&r, and can also do bulk washing, smelting, smoking, and haunting — super handy."
		""
		"&aTips:&f Multiple fans' wind fields stack, raising processing speed&7 (processing speed has nothing to do with fan RPM)&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"A simple 4x wind-stacking example:"
		"- Items dropped onto &especial-height blocks&7 (like Blaze Burners, Metal Girders, Mechanical Harvesters, etc.)&r get stuck right between two levels, so both wind fields process them at once."
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/encased_fan_eg.png width:128 height:71 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Also, the Encased Fan can blow item drops around."
		""
		"Watch how many blocks items get pushed during processing, then place a Funnel at the end for automatic collection."
		""
		"Again: processing speed has nothing to do with fan RPM!"
	]
	quest.5F91CA3FD1CD4D40.quest_subtitle: "799~Huhuhu~"
	quest.5F91CA3FD1CD4D40.title: "S1.7.6 Wind Rider"
	quest.6023C8292A09A3F4.quest_desc: [
		"Steam 'n' Rails lets a Deployer holding a wrench right-click a Train Station to automatically assemble and disassemble trains."
		""
		"This allows you to set up automatic train operations at stations, such as swapping cargo units."
		""
		"If you only need to add or remove cars, a coupler might be more practical."
	]
	quest.6023C8292A09A3F4.title: "T1.2.1 Auto Assembly"
	quest.603B57082D2B7448.quest_desc: [
		"Put the berries into a &ePressing Tub&r and slowly crush them with your feet &7(translation: jump in the pot)&r to get the key ingredient — berry juice."
		""
		"Pour the ingredients into the &ebarrel&7(it's a bit big, so find an open area)&r, put the lid on, and wait for fermentation."
		""
		"Finally, use a &eTap&r to pour the brewed wine into &eEmpty Bottles&r to get the finished product."
	]
	quest.603B57082D2B7448.title: "F3.3.2 Start Brewing"
	quest.605D85F70EF38B79.quest_desc: [
		"The Transcendence Anvil can exceed the enchantment level limit."
		""
		"At this point, you've basically beaten AnvilCraft — the dev team just hasn't developed any further for now www"
	]
	quest.605D85F70EF38B79.title: "AC1.27 Finale"
	quest.615941A4754A7287.quest_desc: [
		"Feed cobblestone and quartz into a &eMechanical Crafter&r to automatically make &ediorite&r."
		""
		"A single Mechanical Crafter is still too slow — try stacking several Mechanical Crafters together and feeding them in bulk."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Yes, it's complicated and really tests your thinking. Using Factory Gauges and Re-Packagers makes it a bit easier."
		""
		"Or you can reference other people's designs:"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Mechanical Crafter Stacking\",\"underlined\":true,\"color\":\"blue\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV129wAenEa8\"}}"
	]
	quest.615941A4754A7287.title: "H3.5 The Hardest Step"
	quest.62331BD6EDFF5E31.quest_desc: [
		"Whether building or mooring, there will always be times when you want to secure a physical structure."
		""
		"That's exactly what the &eDocking Connector&r does — it pins the physical structure firmly to the ground."
		""
		"Besides that, there are many ways to secure and connect physical structures, the Docking Connector included."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Ropes can be tied to mobs, letting you build carts."
	]
	quest.62331BD6EDFF5E31.title: "Securing"
	quest.628DB3001CC7723B.quest_desc: [
		"AnvilCraft needs a lot of iron at the start, but fortunately that's all it needs."
		""
		"To shorten the boring early-game grind, AnvilCraft provides a set of amethyst tools to speed up resource gathering."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aTips&r: &eZinc Ore&r requires an iron pickaxe to mine — unfortunately the amethyst pickaxe won't do... &7(but copper can)"
		""
		"Create doesn't need much starting resources either, so it's no big deal."
	]
	quest.628DB3001CC7723B.title: "AC1.2 An Amazing Early-Game Tool"
	quest.62A3BFD801BEDBBA.quest_desc: [
		"A pretend container used to join a linked storage network."
		""
		"&7But... why don't I just use Barrels instead?"
	]
	quest.62A3BFD801BEDBBA.title: "O4.11 Container with Capacity 0"
	quest.62BE831079501667.quest_desc: [
		"The Cart Assembler is great for building a spruce tree farm — efficient and simple."
		""
		"Before enabling the Cart Assembler, make sure you've set the &eRotation Lock&r!"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Keeping the cart near the center of the dynamic structure slightly reduces performance cost."
	]
	quest.62BE831079501667.title: "H2.4 Minecart Contraption"
	quest.62E879B3DC1F85DC.quest_desc: [
		"Crab Traps produce Crab Claws in all biomes, and will also yield different fish depending on the biome."
		""
		"&aTips&r: See the tutorial book for details."
	]
	quest.62E879B3DC1F85DC.quest_subtitle: "Crab Trap fishing is totally reasonable (for sure)"
	quest.62E879B3DC1F85DC.title: "AC1.3.1 Crab Trap"
	quest.63090FCD74572D61.quest_desc: [
		"With the Blaze Enchanter, you can pick the enchantment level for your enchantments."
	]
	quest.63090FCD74572D61.title: "E1.7 Living Enchantment Table"
	quest.631833863A2A5E1F.quest_desc: [
		"AnvilCraft, as the name suggests, is a mod that uses anvils to process items and blocks, so you'll need to prepare some anvils."
		""
		"AnvilCraft adds a recipe for damaged anvils, which are 16 iron cheaper than an intact anvil!"
	]
	quest.631833863A2A5E1F.title: "AC1.3 Save Where You Can, Splurge Where It Counts"
	quest.632D93F702658D14.quest_desc: [
		"After connecting to the &eStorage Controller&r with a &eLinking Tool&r, it can interact with the outside world on behalf of all drawers, just like the controller."
		""
		"The access point itself cannot bind drawers."
	]
	quest.632D93F702658D14.title: "O3.7 Extended Drawer Network"
	quest.63EDC91EAAEB20EF.quest_desc: [
		"You're probably already familiar with sequenced assembly, so I won't go into detail."
		""
		"One more thing: you can use the &eMechanical Grindstone&r instead of easily-broken sandpaper, which helps with mass production."
	]
	quest.63EDC91EAAEB20EF.quest_subtitle: "This is the co?re? technology~"
	quest.63EDC91EAAEB20EF.title: "HS5.4.3.1 Imitation Is Not Counterfeiting"
	quest.63F4051821289588.quest_desc: [
		"&cBefore we begin&r: please don't skip quest descriptions just to grab the rewards. If you do, I reserve the right to fill your backpack with assorted suspicious food."
		""
		"Create can look intimidating at first, but it starts to make sense once you actually build with it. Enough talking: jump in, try things, and let the machines teach you."
		""
		"&aTips&r: some quests have multiple pages. Click the arrow in the lower-right corner to keep reading."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Nice, you found the next page. &7# applause"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Yep, that's the idea."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Why hasn't the quest been completed yet?"
		""
		"Actually, you only need to click the &7gray check mark √&r in the &eTasks&r requirement. Once it turns &agreen&r, the quest can be completed."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The quest descriptions have been re-translated by hand to fix the old machine translations. If you still find anything wrong, feel free to help out:"
		""
		"I'd be glad if you can provide help:"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Check GitHub and send PR\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://github.com/MeadalFlute/Create-Plus-Aeronautics\" } }"
		""
		"Bug reports:"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Leave a comment under this video\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV165J56ZERr/\" } }"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Send GitHub Issue\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://github.com/MeadalFlute/Create-Plus-Aeronautics/issues\" } }"
	]
	quest.63F4051821289588.quest_subtitle: "&eDon't just grab the rewards and run off — please read the quest descriptions. I beg you, orz"
	quest.63F4051821289588.title: "Welcome!"
	quest.6415CF8000F08DF1.quest_desc: [
		"For the need to travel long distances, this pack includes Immersive Aircraft."
		""
		"I probably haven't modified this mod much yet, so everything on the wiki still applies."
	]
	quest.6415CF8000F08DF1.quest_subtitle: "I haven't finished writing it yet, but it won't have much impact."
	quest.6415CF8000F08DF1.title: "O5.1 Immersive Aircraft"
	quest.64200D4C8EAFC1F4.quest_desc: [
		"Bring the ingredients to a &eMechanical Press&r with a &eBasin&r — it will craft the Blaze Cake Base on its own, fast and good."
		""
		"Also, the &eMechanical Mixer&r can now cook for you — give it a try when you have time!"
	]
	quest.64200D4C8EAFC1F4.title: "H4.3 The Cake Sponge"
	quest.644E9D3E4DFC15BC.quest_desc: [
		"This interface is the quest system!"
		""
		"Besides opening it with the Quest Book, you can press E to open your inventory — in the &eupper-left corner of the screen&r there are several small tools, including a Quest Book shortcut icon. Click it to open this interface too."
		""
		"Move your mouse to the &efar left of the quest interface&r and you'll see many chapters — well-organized guide quests. Follow them when you don't know what to do."
	]
	quest.644E9D3E4DFC15BC.title: "How to Use the Quest System?"
	quest.6458C6BDA6F72ED6.quest_desc: [
		"Aeronautics' physical structures are still a long way from being drivable vehicles."
		""
		"After building the shell, you need to supply stress to the &edevices&7 (wheels, propellers...)&r to make them work."
		""
		"The &ePortable Engine&r is a stress source made for tight spaces — convenient and quick."
		""
		"Feel free to explore the other stress sources on your own; I won't go into detail."
		""
		"&aTips&r: If you really want, Water Wheels, Windmills, Boilers, and the like all work too."
	]
	quest.6458C6BDA6F72ED6.quest_subtitle: "Stress Sources"
	quest.6458C6BDA6F72ED6.title: "General Knowledge"
	quest.64595B1A54501FB3.quest_desc: [
		"In the &eupper-right corner of the quest interface&r there's a one-click claim button for quest rewards — no need to click each one manually."
		""
		"When using this feature, make sure there's a chest nearby to store all the assorted quest rewards."
	]
	quest.64595B1A54501FB3.title: "One-Click Claim"
	quest.646D0951BFFCE244.quest_desc: [
		"Excess seeds can be pressed into oil, and it has plenty of benefits:"
		""
		"First, both Seed Oil and Seed Oil Residue can be used as fuel, and Seed Oil burns for a very long time &7(I originally wanted Seed Oil to put Blaze Burners into superheated burning, but the code never worked)"
		""
		"Besides that, Seed Oil Residue can be made into &eOrganic Compost&r, which mixes with water to make &eLiquid Fertilizer&r"
		""
		"Finally, Seed Oil can be mixed with cream or butter to make &egrease&7 (for cooking)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"It exists for no other purpose than to use up excess vegetables, seeds, and the like."
		""
		"Kaleidoscope's item tag system is a complete mess, and it's driving me crazy."
	]
	quest.646D0951BFFCE244.title: "F1.3 Oil Extraction"
	quest.6498D4A8917CC48D.quest_desc: [
		"These special stones often generate in huge amounts underground; crushing them yields the corresponding ore."
		""
		"Use a Prospector Pickaxe to locate them quickly."
	]
	quest.6498D4A8917CC48D.title: "Massive Ore Veins"
	quest.64A10A249D1222A1.quest_desc: [
		"Ababa ababa..."
	]
	quest.64A10A249D1222A1.title: "O3.14 Upgrade 4"
	quest.64AEEAEE183968EE.quest_desc: [
		"Watching the workstation chug along so slowly gets frustrating — try raising the input rotation speed to 256rpm!"
	]
	quest.64AEEAEE183968EE.title: "256x"
	quest.64B66B16E701756E.quest_desc: [
		"Charge Neutronium Ingots to get Charged Neutronium Ingots... um..."
		""
		"&aTips&r: It requires a LOT of electricity, so make sure your base has enough power."
	]
	quest.64B66B16E701756E.quest_subtitle: "Makes sense!"
	quest.64B66B16E701756E.title: "AC1.23 Power Hog"
	quest.64D021939B024BB2.quest_desc: [
		"Of course these components can be used not only to mass-produce bread, but you can also produce other things."
		""
		"Search for &e@Farmer&r in the item filter to see if there's anything you like."
	]
	quest.64D021939B024BB2.title: "H1.18 Advanced"
	quest.658335D65A1F5A46.quest_desc: [
		"The dynamic structure here needs caches and interfaces to collect and remove wood."
	]
	quest.658335D65A1F5A46.title: "H2.2 The Old Favorites"
	quest.65BF8FC02AE8FD7D.quest_desc: [
		"Quartz is a useful resource too — mining it also gives a good chunk of XP, so grab it when you see it."
	]
	quest.65BF8FC02AE8FD7D.title: "S1.8.4 Since We're Here"
	quest.65EC18E9B0D560EC.quest_desc: [
		"This upgrade can be mass-produced, though it's a bit of a hassle."
	]
	quest.65EC18E9B0D560EC.title: "O2.13 No Need"
	quest.6673D40DCE9EEF4B.quest_desc: [
		"Create iron is cheaper than copper, so it's generally not used."
	]
	quest.6673D40DCE9EEF4B.title: "O2.11 Rarely Used"
	quest.6676FFE364D3886B.quest_desc: [
		"This magical little gadget is the material for crafting Waystones. It can also be used by holding right-click:"
		""
		"Select an already-activated Waystone &7(Sharestones won't work)&r to teleport."
		""
		"&cNote&f: Taking damage interrupts the teleport — use it somewhere safe."
	]
	quest.6676FFE364D3886B.title: "O1.3 Warp Stone"
	quest.66A07F9D10CBCB72.quest_desc: [
		"Want to transport packages and items over long distances, or even across dimensions?"
		""
		"No problem! Through Postboxes, packages can be transported over long distances, across dimensions, and fully automatically using the train system."
		""
		"&aTips&r: See the Ponder scenes for Postboxes and Train Stations for details."
	]
	quest.66A07F9D10CBCB72.quest_subtitle: "\"Mail You Later\" is the subtitle of Create 6.0"
	quest.66A07F9D10CBCB72.title: "4.11 \"Mailing You Later\""
	quest.66CD35919907E5AF.quest_desc: [
		"While the Void Energy Collector runs, it generates ores in the surrounding 5?5?5 area. These ores reduce its power output and are a hassle to process with AnvilCraft."
		""
		"But for Create, it's just a matter of setting up a few drills — you can even use it as an ore miner to get late-game resources early!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cBad news&r: Void Decay no longer produces Blocks of Cursed Gold."
	]
	quest.66CD35919907E5AF.title: "AC1.10.2 Void Miner (?)"
	quest.66DE1A267E937181.quest_desc: [
		"Kill Iron Golems to get Iron Ingots."
		""
		"Iron Golems spawn naturally in villages."
	]
	quest.66DE1A267E937181.quest_subtitle: "Not that you can't farm other mobs — it's just not recommended."
	quest.66DE1A267E937181.title: "Iron Farm"
	quest.66F7CB84CEA26D26.quest_desc: [
		"Let's try mass production. It doesn't require many resources and it's not very difficult."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Mass-Producing Bread\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"76B37CC4BA85F7C4\"}}"
	]
	quest.66F7CB84CEA26D26.title: "H1.7.1 Bread Not Selling, Please Help"
	quest.67B6BB4332CCECAE.quest_desc: [
		"Since people usually only think about crushing things when there's a large amount of raw material, a small temporary warehouse is essential."
		""
		"Its purpose is to absorb large short-term bursts of items so they don't spill onto the floor."
	]
	quest.67B6BB4332CCECAE.title: "Cache"
	quest.67F4721322D79770.quest_desc: [
		"Now, press \"&eT&r\" to open the chat box, and the input method will be switched automatically."
		"&7-It has some performance impact, but it solves the problem of new players getting stuck with their input method."
		"&7-Disable IMBlocker if you don't need it"
		""
		"In the &ecrafting interface&r, press \"&eTab&r\" to automatically repeat the last crafting recipe you used."
		""
		"In the &equest interface&r, press \"&eCtrl&r + &eF&r\" to search quests."
		""
		"By default, MC uses &eCtrl&r to sprint and &eShift&r to sneak."
		""
		"If a key doesn't respond, or you want to change the default settings, follow the steps on the &enext page&r to open the key configuration screen:"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"① Press &eEsc&r to open the menu and find \"&eOptions...&r\""
		""
		"② In \"&eOptions...&r\", find \"&eControls...&r\""
		""
		"③ In \"&eControls...&r\", find \"&eKey Binds...&r\""
		""
		"④ In the search box at the top of the \"&eKey Binds...&r\" page, search for the key you want to check. Here's how:"
		""
		"&ecategory:&r+&emod name&r — view all key bindings of a specific mod"
		""
		"&ekey:&r+&ekey name&r — view all bindings for a specific key"
		""
		"&ename:&r+&efunction name&r — check which key is bound to a function"
	]
	quest.67F4721322D79770.title: "Some Handy Tidbits"
	quest.68730811F19FBB0B.quest_desc: [
		"Who doesn't want a TBM you can drive out for a stroll &7(?)&r!"
		""
		"The Ponder scenes for the &ePhysics Assembler&r and the &eBorehead Bearing&r contain everything you need to know to build a TBM."
		""
		"It's troublesome to build, inefficient, and hard to control... but cool enough."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Using tracks is an economical choice, but turning and climbing hills gets very troublesome, so wheels are still recommended."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If you really want tracks, search \"&e@track&r\" in JEI&7(EMI)&r to see the content from &eCreate Tracks&r."
	]
	quest.68730811F19FBB0B.quest_subtitle: "Remember to view the Ponder scene!"
	quest.68730811F19FBB0B.title: "S1.11.6 Tunnel Boring Machine"
	quest.68EACC370598FD77.quest_desc: [
		"Sort out the wheat and grind it into wheat flour to get more out of your wheat."
	]
	quest.68EACC370598FD77.title: "H1.8 Milling"
	quest.697E93BB81B45AAE.quest_desc: [
		"The new wire control system noticeably reduces the pressure of redstone wiring."
		""
		"I've put the usage instructions in the item tooltip :)"
	]
	quest.697E93BB81B45AAE.title: "S1.11.5 Nifty Gadget 2.0"
	quest.6983C80D4250A5D0.quest_desc: [
		"When &elightning&r strikes a Block of Iron, it turns into a &eHollowed Block of Magnet&r."
		""
		"Putting an Iron Ingot into a Hollowed Block of Magnet slowly turns it into a &eBlock of Magnet&r."
	]
	quest.6994597220DA39DA.quest_desc: [
		"Drawers can take upgrades, and the effects of different upgrades are multiplicative."
		""
		"For example, stuffing in two Copper Upgrades gives 8?8=64x storage."
	]
	quest.6994597220DA39DA.title: "S2.12.2 Get an Upgrade"
	quest.69D8C4A7A0F6E3C6.quest_desc: [
		"Use a spatula to right-click an &eopen Grease Crock&r, scoop out some grease, and pour it straight into the wok for cooking."
		""
		"Cook's Stools are step blocks that make it easier to operate Woks and Stockpots."
		""
		"An Oil Can can hold Seed Oil and be used instead of grease for cooking."
	]
	quest.69D8C4A7A0F6E3C6.title: "F3.5 Practical Kitchenware (2)"
	quest.69DD7EFEEBE25791.quest_desc: [
		"Crushing Blaze Rods with the &eCrushing Wheel&r yields more Blaze Powder"
		""
		"But here's even better news:"
		""
		"Brewing potions in a Basin doesn't need Blaze Powder at all."
	]
	quest.69DD7EFEEBE25791.title: "S2.2.2 More Blaze Powder"
	quest.69FBB054877310A4.quest_desc: [
		"What to do after beating the Wither — grab a max-level beacon?"
		""
		"&7You can also craft Frost Metal Ingots!"
	]
	quest.69FBB054877310A4.title: "S1.10.2 Nether Star"
	quest.6A0BC46E8A670AF7.quest_desc: [
		"Uranium can generate electricity. That's it &7(not really)&r."
		""
		"You probably won't need it, but it's here for symmetry."
	]
	quest.6A0BC46E8A670AF7.title: "S2.2.14 Hazardous Metals"
	quest.6A1DFA5CB68B840B.quest_desc: [
		"Heliostats concentrate sunlight to heat Tungsten Blocks, which then generate electricity through a Heat Collector — a decent amount of power."
		""
		"The downsides are obvious though: it takes up a huge area and needs sunlight."
	]
	quest.6A1DFA5CB68B840B.title: "AC1.7.1 Solar Thermal Power Station"
	quest.6A395F0A533BBFA6.quest_desc: [
		"While looking up recipes in JEI&7 (EMI)&r, you've probably noticed that many Farmer's Delight dishes can be &eauto-cooked&r with Create machinery."
		""
		"Kaleidoscope food can't be made directly with Create machines, but the Deployer&7 (Mechanical Hand)&r is absolutely unstoppable&r —"
		""
		"Simulating hand-cooking with a Deployer is still doable, just more complicated."
		""
		"Maybe you'll open a huge tavern or restaurant later?"
	]
	quest.6A395F0A533BBFA6.title: "F3.6 Automated Cooking"
	quest.6A4AE77D81ABAFD9.quest_desc: [
		"Once your structure is finished, you may need to use heavier blocks like &eFlint Blocks&r&7 (recycling, you see)&r as &eballast&r to &eadjust the center of gravity&r."
		""
		"Use the &eStructure Diagram&r to check the forces acting on a physical structure and where its center of gravity is."
		""
		"Make sure your build's &ecenter of gravity&r isn't too far off, and that the overall &eresultant force&r doesn't stray too much from it — unless you know exactly what you're doing."
		""
		"&aTips&r: There's a gyroscope from the mod itself — feed it enough stress and it will forcibly keep the structure stable."
		""
		"It's a reliable catch-all solution; hopefully you won't rely on it too much."
	]
	quest.6A4AE77D81ABAFD9.title: "Balance Control"
	quest.6A667E59BF39167F.quest_desc: [
		"At its most basic, the Schematicannon can help you quickly expand your platform, deploy machines, and build mansions."
		""
		"It also has plenty of advanced features, such as clearing land for you:"
		""
		"Enable the air replacement function in the Schematicannon's lower-left settings, then print a blueprint that's all air."
		""
		"Covered blocks are not returned to you. Also, using multiple Schematicannons at once speeds things up."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"Rummaging around for materials is a pain — try throwing a Clipboard into the Schematicannon &7(it turns into a material list)&r, then bring it to the Stock Ticker &7(see the Stock Ticker's Ponder scene)&r to quickly gather materials."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Shift+right-click a backpack placed next to the Schematicannon and it will automatically pull items from it."
	]
	quest.6A667E59BF39167F.title: "Copy & Paste"
	quest.6A945F2BC97B33DE.quest_desc: [
		"When a Deployer kills mobs, it usually produces Nuggets of Experience."
		""
		"Paired with a mob farm, you'll have an endless stream of experience."
	]
	quest.6A945F2BC97B33DE.title: "ES1.2.1 Execution by the Deployer"
	quest.6B0E81A5DD26BBBC.quest_desc: [
		"Use it to bind an Inventory Cable Connector and remotely access your storage."
	]
	quest.6B0E81A5DD26BBBC.title: "O4.6 Ultimate Mastery"
	quest.6B151160907137A0.quest_desc: [
		"The enderman farm is a relatively troublesome machine. The blueprint system can greatly reduce the workload — go give it a try."
		""
		"&aTips:&f When holding a blueprint to place a build, Shift+right-click lets you input exact coordinates."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Put the &eClipboard&r into the Schematicannon to get a material list and prepare materials easily."
		""
		"You can hand the material list directly to the &eStock Ticker&7 (warehouse manager)&r, and it will intelligently sort out the materials from your storage."
	]
	quest.6B151160907137A0.title: "S2.17.2 Fire!"
	quest.6B58E7363BD4E0F4.quest_desc: [
		"What happens if something that can't be crushed gets caught in a Crushing Wheel?"
		""
		"It gets destroyed!"
		""
		"Quick, use an Attribute Filter with a raw ore as the reference, add the \"&ecan be crushed&r\" tag, and stuff it into the Crushing Wheel's entrance to save every block that's lost its footing."
	]
	quest.6B58E7363BD4E0F4.title: "S2.9.3 Goudi Review!"
	quest.6B622E9F4CE8D0A8.quest_desc: [
		"Use an axe to right-click a log to strip it. Then &ehold Andesite Alloy and right-click the stripped log&r to get an Andesite Casing."
	]
	quest.6B622E9F4CE8D0A8.title: "1.5 Casing Time!"
	quest.6B6979B9E5EB8248.quest_desc: [
		"A jetpack gives you a near-Creative flight experience, though it's a hassle to craft."
		""
		"That shouldn't be a problem for you, right?"
		""
		"&aTips&r: You can also search \"&equadcopter&r\" in JEI&7(EMI)&r — it's a cheaper alternative to the jetpack."
		""
		"Also, the &eJewel Crafting Table&r recipes are copying recipes, so it's best to make your first Feather Amulet with sequenced assembly."
	]
	quest.6B6979B9E5EB8248.title: "S2.8.2 Flying"
	quest.6B9FF06416BDA640.quest_desc: [
		"Throw the geode onto the &estamping platform&r and smash it with an anvil &8(or left-click the anvil hammer)&r to get three kinds of gems."
		""
		"&aTips&r: An anvil won't break from a 1-block fall."
	]
	quest.6B9FF06416BDA640.quest_subtitle: "Mechanical Press: ?"
	quest.6B9FF06416BDA640.title: "AC1.4 Clang!"
	quest.6BBE868EADD6AD33.quest_desc: [
		"Amethyst Clusters grow on Budding Amethyst; breaking the clusters drops Amethyst."
	]
	quest.6BCAC18D81E9476D.quest_desc: [
		"Most Create components include \"&ePonder&r\": a complete set of animated tutorials."
		""
		"All you need to do is open your backpack, move your mouse cursor to an item you don't know how to use, and hold down [&eW&r] to Ponder."
		""
		"If you still have questions or need inspiration, you can also check out the Create tutorials I did before :)"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Click here to view the tutorial\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1gCNkeGEJR/\"}}"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Dark blue text can be clicked"
	]
	quest.6BCAC18D81E9476D.title: "How to Play Create?"
	quest.6BE2FADB6BBB8E57.quest_desc: [
		"Item Vaults can store a huge number of items, making them great for storage."
		""
		"Although you can't open one directly, there's always a way around it."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"For example, attach a terminal to it\",\"underlined\":true,\"color\":\"blue\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"376B0226F9435FAD\"}}"
	]
	quest.6BE2FADB6BBB8E57.title: "S1.6.5 Large Warehouse"
	quest.6C3D3622E0DDCC95.quest_desc: [
		"With the Transcendent Upgrade Template, you can upgrade certain items to their Transcendent version — the creative version."
		""
		"Transcendent items need no power supply, have infinite durability, greater output, and more adjustable options."
		""
		"In short, they are the most powerful of their kind."
	]
	quest.6C3D3622E0DDCC95.title: "Transcendence"
	quest.6C3FDDA6C2D1E84D.quest_desc: [
		"After installation, it can collect dropped items from a chosen direction."
		""
		"It can also pump water."
	]
	quest.6C3FDDA6C2D1E84D.title: "O3.16 Collect Dropped Items"
	quest.6C446DC45D0EFE73.quest_desc: [
		"Smash enough mass into the Space Overcompressor and it will produce Neutronium Ingots &8(a minute of silence for the iron golems)&r"
		""
		"&aTips&r: Neutronium Ingots pass straight through most blocks, so it's best to place a layer of End Dust two blocks &ebelow&r the Space Overcompressor."
	]
	quest.6C446DC45D0EFE73.title: "AC1.22 Neutronium Ingot"
	quest.6C62197957BBF16F.quest_desc: [
		"It can be said that iron is the backbone of industry."
		""
		"I hope you weren't lazy when mass-producing iron."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Mass-Producing Iron\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"714DFF8B1435B67B\"}}"
	]
	quest.6C62197957BBF16F.title: "H5.2.1 Solid Foundation"
	quest.6C8815AFBC6DABAB.title: "Freight"
	quest.6C975F30267C6C34.quest_desc: [
		"Used with cables to connect remote containers to the storage network."
	]
	quest.6C975F30267C6C34.title: "O4.13 Installation Interface"
	quest.6CA92EBEC0822090.quest_desc: [
		"Honey is the secret to boosting ore production — it can multiply efficiency by hundreds of times."
		""
		"Bees can also boost crop yields, so you can keep them in your fields."
		""
		"A &eMechanical Pump&r can pump out honey automatically, but you'll still need to shear the honeycombs."
		""
		"You won't need that many honeycombs, so there's no need to use a Deployer."
	]
	quest.6CA92EBEC0822090.quest_subtitle: "Resource Bees is the name of a mod"
	quest.6CA92EBEC0822090.title: "F2.5 Resource Bees"
	quest.6DA5546C30AF595D.quest_desc: [
		"All the ingredients come straight from nature — pure, organic farm products &8(no doubt)."
	]
	quest.6DA5546C30AF595D.title: "S1.7.17 Purely Natural, No Additives, No Deception"
	quest.6DE014274FF80AB5.title: "H5.4.1 Preconditions"
	quest.6E069D46FB4B2F5E.quest_desc: [
		"Installing &edownward-facing sails&r on the body provides extra downforce at high speed, giving you better grip in theory."
		""
		"But if you really need to go fast, building a road is the better option."
		""
		"A friendly reminder: driving off-road too fast can easily make you dizzy or flip over."
		""
		"&7Or just take the train?"
	]
	quest.6E069D46FB4B2F5E.title: "Grip"
	quest.6E0DCE334B9D44B4.quest_desc: [
		"If you have a basic knowledge of redstone, you can explore the combination of dynamic structures and redstone by yourself :P"
	]
	quest.6E0DCE334B9D44B4.title: "S1.7.14 I Reckon It'll Work"
	quest.6E68235AA84E758D.quest_desc: [
		"Many times you'll want to control the speed of a &epower source&7 (tires, propellers, etc.)&r — that's exactly what the Analog Transmission was invented for."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Check its Ponder scene to learn how to use it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Directional control is covered in the tasks below:"
		"{\"text\":\"Aircraft / Ships\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"2311F440D9DD1D20\"}}"
		"{\"text\":\"Cars\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"3C2CEBF878AB2A20\"}}"
	]
	quest.6E68235AA84E758D.title: "Control System"
	quest.6E98B59A5D229C20.quest_desc: [
		"The Rope Pulley is great for driving a &eMechanical Drill&r — it can dig all the way down to bedrock."
		""
		"Once the Rope Pulley &estops moving&r, the rope can be used as a ladder to quickly climb back to the surface."
		""
		"&aTips&r:"
		""
		"When a &estorage block&r is part of the dynamic structure, produced items are automatically stored in it;"
		""
		"Also, Item Vaults can't be opened directly — that's not a bug. Check its Ponder scene."
	]
	quest.6E98B59A5D229C20.title: "S1.7.7 Journey to the Center of the Earth"
	quest.6F187E2EE4C10CAB.quest_desc: [
		"For an &eairship&7 (or a hot air balloon?)&r, the basis of lift is the balloon — the bigger, the better."
		""
		"As altitude rises, air pressure drops, and so does the lift produced by the balloon."
		""
		"For a &eship&r, buoyancy depends on displacement — although it doesn't actually displace water."
		""
		"As for an &eaircraft&r, it mainly generates lift through sails."
	]
	quest.6F187E2EE4C10CAB.title: "Lift/Buoyancy"
	quest.6FA194138A172530.quest_desc: [
		"Crush netherrack to get Cinder Flour, which is used to make Blaze Cake Base."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You can also get Nether Dust from the AnvilCraft Crushing Table; grinding Nether Dust yields even more Cinder Flour."
		""
		"Cinder Flour can also be crafted back into Nether Dust."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The following is discarded draft text — I like to keep abandoned ideas around, because I've been burned before oao"
		""
		"&mCrush netherrack to get Nether Dust; crush it again to get Cinder Flour, which is used to make Blaze Cake Base."
		""
		"&mIn vanilla Create, crushing netherrack gives Cinder Flour directly. I changed the recipe here on my own — because Nether Dust is useful."
		""
		"&mAs compensation, I increased the yield of Cinder Flour."
		""
		"&mObviously a tutorial pack shouldn't alter the original progression, but I couldn't think of a good recipe that works with AnvilCraft."
		""
		"If you have a good idea, feel free to suggest it."
	]
	quest.6FA194138A172530.title: "H4.2 Milling"
	quest.700C61FA7B245F9C.quest_desc: [
		"Zombies standing in the Corrupted Beacon's beam turn into Giants. If you stuff &eZombies&r with anvils first &7(right-click them with anvils — 20 at a time is recommended)&r, the resulting Giant may hold a Giant Anvil."
		""
		"&aTips&r: If a block sits above the Corrupted Beacon, no beam is produced. The beam passes through glass, bedrock, and &eHollowed Blocks of Magnet&r."
	]
	quest.700C61FA7B245F9C.title: "AC1.17 Biotechnology"
	quest.705A40C192CC3B85.quest_desc: [
		"Just like netherite, you need a smithing template to upgrade tools to Royal Steel."
		""
		"The Royal Steel smithing template can be found in blacksmith chests, or obtained by trading with a &eJeweler&7 (unemployed villagers near a Jewel Crafting Table become Jewelers)&r."
		""
		"&aTips&r: It's recommended to build a villager breeding center and a villager trading hall."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"By the way:"
		"Villagers don't start work until 8 o'clock, but Steve &7(you)&r gets up at 6."
		""
		"Related tutorials:"
		"{\"text\":\"Villager Breeding Center\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://zh.minecraft.wiki/w/%E6%9D%91%E6%B0%91?variant=zh-cn#%E5%B7%A5%E4%BD%9C%E7%AB%99%E7%82%B9%E4%B8%8E%E5%BA%8A\"}}"
		"{\"text\":\"Also check the Wiki\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://zh.minecraft.wiki/w/%E6%9D%91%E6%B0%91?variant=zh-cn\"}}"
	]
	quest.705A40C192CC3B85.title: "S1.11.2 Upgrade Template"
	quest.70A75AECE5AFE291.quest_desc: [
		"The best backpack in MC, it will accompany you till eternity."
	]
	quest.70A75AECE5AFE291.title: "O2.10 Ultimate Dedication"
	quest.70B69557EC69A476.quest_desc: [
		"The Millstone can grind wheat into wheat flour, improving your wheat yield."
		""
		"Grinding one wheat plant at a time is too slow, but there will be more efficient machines later."
	]
	quest.70B69557EC69A476.title: "S1.7.5 Small but Beautiful"
	quest.70FA30FEA136BF9E.quest_desc: [
		"The Boiler definitely can't burn all the charcoal, so send the excess back to storage!"
		""
		"A simple way:"
		""
		"Run a &econveyor belt&r straight to the storage. The wooden barrels that feed coal to the Boiler sit on both sides of the &7conveyor belt&e heading to storage&r — use &eAndesite/Brass Funnels&r to take items off."
		""
		"This way, when a barrel is full, its funnel stops pulling from the belt, and the charcoal naturally flows into storage."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You ask what the Threshold Switch here is for?"
		""
		"&7Actually not needed for now (or rather, hopefully you'll use it)."
		""
		"Or maybe use it to check when storage is full and shut down the tree farm?"
	]
	quest.70FA30FEA136BF9E.title: "H2.8 Flow Splitting"
	quest.712EF7E4583780CC.quest_desc: [
		"Besides batch smelting, crushed ores can also be batch-washed to get &eadditional by-products&r."
	]
	quest.712EF7E4583780CC.title: "2.10 Crushed Ore"
	quest.714DFF8B1435B67B.quest_desc: [
		"Iron is used in huge amounts, so you should build an &eiron production line&r, starting with a &ecobblestone generator&r!"
		""
		"You've probably noticed that washing &egravel&r&7(see the Encased Fan's Ponder scene)&r has a chance to yield &eIron Nuggets&r, and gravel can be obtained by crushing cobblestone."
		""
		"A simple cobblestone generator provides an endless supply of cobblestone, meaning Create can mass-produce iron."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"I figured mass-producing iron is a must, so I put it in the main questline ("
		""
		"The &etask screen&r given by the quest auto-submits tasks, though it's not required."
		""
		"&cBreaking News?"
		""
		"Cobblestone broken by a Mechanical Drill now goes straight into &eopen containers&r&7 below (chutes, funnels connected to containers, Depots, Basins, Millstones...)&r!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Cobblestone generator reference image:"
		"&7*There is water inside the copper grille"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/2_11.png width:256 height:142 align:center}"
	]
	quest.714DFF8B1435B67B.quest_subtitle: "&r&eCobblestone&r?[Crush]?>Gravel?[Wash]?>Iron Nuggets"
	quest.714DFF8B1435B67B.title: "2.11 Mass-Producing Iron"
	quest.7154DBA83C273F5C.quest_desc: [
		"All the prologue quest rewards are food — lots of different kinds."
		""
		"You can leave them unclaimed and just grab some when you're hungry."
	]
	quest.7154DBA83C273F5C.title: "Temporary Storage"
	quest.716AE9871B4943E8.quest_desc: [
		"Automatic farms can be built as early as the Andesite Age. If you plan to become a gourmet, build a farm to supply ingredients."
		""
		"Well... even a small auto farm can produce more than you'll ever use."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"?One farm grows multiple crops: vegetables, melons, berries, sugar cane, etc."
		""
		"?Separate out wheat and seeds, auto-grind the wheat into bread, and send the seeds to compost automatically."
		""
		"?Set up timers and full-chest detection &7(the farm stops automatically when a chest is full)&r for your farm to reduce performance cost."
		"&aTips:&r You'll need some simple redstone circuits; once you reach the Brass Age, Pulse Timers and Threshold Switches can simplify them."
	]
	quest.716AE9871B4943E8.title: "Automated Farm"
	quest.71B1E3A88A7C9635.quest_desc: [
		"Propellers are the primary source of thrust and are used to control structure movement."
		""
		"Smart propellers attempt to maintain structural stability when placed vertically."
		""
		"&7You can also use tires."
	]
	quest.71B1E3A88A7C9635.title: "Propeller Power"
	quest.720A1FD029A7EB35.quest_desc: [
		"Hit a villager with an anvil and it forgets its previous trades &7(meaning you can refresh the trades if you're unhappy with them)&r"
		""
		"Villagers hit by an anvil also have a chance to turn into a green-robed Nitwit &7(Nitwits can't trade)&r, which is totally reasonable."
	]
	quest.720A1FD029A7EB35.title: "AC1.11.1 Great Amnesia!"
	quest.72A0E7758CE7A42A.quest_desc: [
		"A set of combat gear can help you survive better in the perilous &7(debatable)&r MC world."
		""
		"Of course, it's not required."
	]
	quest.72A0E7758CE7A42A.title: "S1.3.2 Be Kind to Yourself"
	quest.73C23D5D71D93963.quest_desc: [
		"Fishing has plenty of perks — it yields ingredients and treasure, and it's a relaxing pastime."
	]
	quest.73C23D5D71D93963.title: "F4.4 Eat Seafood"
	quest.73C360170A8E199F.quest_desc: [
		"You can't play Create without Goggles and a Wrench, and you'll often need to carry them with you."
		""
		"As for Diving Boots: they keep you from being moved by Mechanical Belts, which is handy during maintenance."
	]
	quest.73C360170A8E199F.title: "Essential for Engineers"
	quest.7410E19C486BDA5F.quest_desc: [
		"Industrial mods always have one step leading to another."
		""
		"Take it slow — there's nothing scary about it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aTips&r: &7&mIf you want to skip ahead... unassembled partial products can be used directly in the next crafting step."
		""
		"I thought about it and changed it anyway."
		""
		"This little trick looks quite useful — you could use it to skip grind in other modpacks."
		""
		"But in reality, most modpack authors can't be bothered to add an intermediate product for you &7(like me)."
	]
	quest.7410E19C486BDA5F.quest_subtitle: "Matryoshka doll recipe"
	quest.7410E19C486BDA5F.title: "H5.2 Semi-Finished Products"
	quest.7459E4A4967D5550.quest_desc: [
		"Tom's Simple Storage greatly simplifies your storage — no more rummaging through boxes and cabinets!"
		""
		"&o&7For details, see the Life Hacks section&o"
	]
	quest.7459E4A4967D5550.title: "E1.7.2 How Can Something So Convenient Exist?"
	quest.74B22B35A46C23AB.quest_desc: [
		"It will stay with you for a while."
	]
	quest.74B22B35A46C23AB.title: "O2.7 Basic Backpack"
	quest.74B83B6A3D5C8C4D.quest_desc: [
		"Yes, it only accepts raw ore, so you need Silk Touch... right?"
		""
		"Just drop two gold ingots on netherrack and smash it with an anvil to get gold ore."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Netherrack can be mass-produced too."
	]
	quest.74B83B6A3D5C8C4D.quest_subtitle: "The child doesn’t understand, but the child is strong"
	quest.74B83B6A3D5C8C4D.title: "HS5.4.3.2 Does It Have to Be Raw Ore?"
	quest.7503562CA4582ABC.quest_desc: [
		"With a Factory Gauge, ores from your storage network can be automatically sent to be crushed."
	]
	quest.750CB599AAC54B5C.quest_desc: [
		"Although netherrack is everywhere, it's not renewable, so you'd have to gather it all over the place."
		""
		"Using a Factory Gauge to control production might ease the workload."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Actually, netherrack IS renewable now — check out those extra recipes."
		""
		"The steps are a bit long, but not hard."
		""
		"&8Honestly, it's better to just take a TBM to the Nether."
	]
	quest.750CB599AAC54B5C.title: "HS4.1.1 Control Output"
	quest.754C3BCFF567AFE2.quest_desc: [
		"Make a one-layer base of Cursed Gold Blocks, place a Beacon on top, then &eactivate the Beacon with Cursed Gold&r. There's a 5% chance it turns into a Corrupted Beacon."
		""
		"A three-layer Cursed Gold base gives 20%, and a four-layer base gives 100%."
		""
		"Two layers? &eStill 5%.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aDid you know&r: My first Corrupted Beacon took 37 activations — that beats 0% of players. Give it a shot!"
		""
		"&cDamn!"
	]
	quest.754C3BCFF567AFE2.title: "AC1.16 Test Your Luck!"
	quest.7552BB5C0D181427.quest_desc: [
		"Attach the &ePoster&r to the &ePackager&r to set the destination address for packages."
		""
		"You can also set the destination address with the &eStock Ticker&7 (the warehouse manager)&r and the &eRedstone Requester&r."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Inside the Stock Ticker, you can use a &eFilter&r to sort items in your warehouse."
	]
	quest.7552BB5C0D181427.title: "3.10 Assigning Addresses"
	quest.762F86F638041EC6.quest_desc: [
		"Usage is similar to Create's Attribute Filter."
		""
		"&8But crafting it doesn't require brass!"
	]
	quest.762F86F638041EC6.title: "O4.19 Attribute Filter"
	quest.765C6121F37BBFB3.quest_desc: [
		"Presumably, when you build a physical structure, you don't want it to just drive off on its own, nor do you want to climb around inside it to operate every device by hand, right?"
		""
		"Then you'll want some directly-controllable terminals to remotely operate your devices."
		""
		"We recommend the &eLinked Typewriter&r or the &eLinked Controller&r."
		""
		"&aTips&r: The Linked Controller can be placed on a &eLectern&r."
	]
	quest.765C6121F37BBFB3.title: "Human-Computer Interaction"
	quest.76B37CC4BA85F7C4.quest_desc: [
		"To mass-produce bread, you first need to mass-produce wheat. Mechanical Harvesters can automatically harvest mature crops and replant them — they need to be deployed on a dynamic structure."
	]
	quest.76B37CC4BA85F7C4.title: "H1.1 Automated Wheat Field"
	quest.77285283F3DEA858.quest_desc: [
		"All four sides of a Cross Gearbox can connect to Shafts, letting you change the direction of stress transmission and rotation."
		""
		"The two kinds of Cross Gearboxes can be crafted into each other, or converted directly with a &eWrench&r."
		""
		"Along a straight line, the two ends of a Cross Gearbox rotate in opposite directions — equivalent to a &eGearshift&r."
	]
	quest.77285283F3DEA858.quest_subtitle: "Okay, I admit that this part was added later, I don’t know how to label it appropriately."
	quest.7730913B25648467.quest_desc: [
		"And with that, your mass bread production line is complete!"
	]
	quest.7730913B25648467.title: "H1.17 Into Production!"
	quest.7763C28C3F9AF9AC.quest_desc: [
		"Mechanical Harvesters can harvest all kinds of crops, even kelp, berries, and cocoa beans."
		""
		"They must be mounted on a &edynamic structure&r!"
		""
		"&8Even though you can't eat all those crops, they may be useless, but we can't live without them (for real)"
	]
	quest.7763C28C3F9AF9AC.quest_subtitle: "Farming can also be automated!"
	quest.7763C28C3F9AF9AC.title: "S1.7.4 Can Farming Also Be Automated?"
	quest.77F7BC95F15429A6.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Grindstone can remove enchantments from items, turn Nuggets of Experience into Liquid Experience, and handle all sanding recipes."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Ponder a Nugget of Experience to see what Enchantment Industry adds."
	]
	quest.77F7BC95F15429A6.quest_subtitle: "A pair of small Crushing Wheels"
	quest.77F7BC95F15429A6.title: "E1.2 Disenchanting Basin"
	quest.7822A4F7E1300F47.quest_desc: [
		"Craft the Transcendent Alloy and you're &ea stone's throw&r from the ultimate artifact."
		""
		"The later steps get basic guidance in the side quests, but the finer details are left for you to figure out."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"e.g. Frost Metal Ingot\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"203380ED9BC38B15\" } }"
	]
	quest.7822A4F7E1300F47.quest_subtitle: "A hundred-mile journey is half completed at ninety miles"
	quest.7822A4F7E1300F47.title: "H5.6 Done Already?"
	quest.78555F9C28D8F5DD.quest_desc: [
		"You made the iron production line look easy — as expected of you."
		""
		"As for flint, you can deal with it yourself; I'll just wish it happiness here."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Still, flint can be used to make Andesite, and Andesite is quite useful &7(probably)&r."
	]
	quest.78555F9C28D8F5DD.quest_subtitle: "Cobblestone?[Crush]?>Gravel?[Wash]?>&eIron Nuggets"
	quest.78555F9C28D8F5DD.title: "2.14 Unlimited Iron!"
	quest.78627F8BDF656AC6.quest_desc: [
		"The machines ahead tend to be large, so it's a good idea to clear some open space in advance."
		""
		"Deployers can place blocks, which makes them great for expanding your platform."
		""
		"Actually, Create has dedicated components for land preparation &7(Mechanical Roller)&r, but if your base is in the sky or out at sea, a Deployer may still suit you better."
		""
		"&7Maybe a Schematicannon is the better choice?"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If mobs still spawn in your base even after you've placed light sources, try a &eHaunted Bell&r."
	]
	quest.78627F8BDF656AC6.title: "S2.4 Expand Your Turf"
	quest.78AB0ED9CF3AB973.quest_desc: [
		"With a Trading Depot, you can trade with villagers fully automatically and without limits —"
		""
		"&7Provided the villagers are on duty."
	]
	quest.78AB0ED9CF3AB973.title: "Automated Trading"
	quest.78BA4EC1ACB85BB2.quest_desc: [
		"Cocoa beans and bees are a bit hard to find, so gather some when you come across them — they'll be useful later."
		""
		"&aTips&r: You can catch bees with a &eCage&r or a &eBlock of Resin&r; also, a tool with &eSilk Touch&r can mine the beehive along with the bees inside."
	]
	quest.78BA4EC1ACB85BB2.title: "Have Some Dessert"
	quest.78BB766460EF42BF.quest_desc: [
		"Don't forget you can also search online, ask an AI, or check MC?? — all very convenient options."
		""
		"There are also plenty of tutorials on Bilibili — go take a look and find some inspiration."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"This one's pretty good, for example\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1wNPUezEnA/\"}}"
	]
	quest.78BB766460EF42BF.title: "What Should I Do If I Still Can’t Use It After Reading the Task?"
	quest.7938030579EFD8D8.quest_desc: [
		"If an anvil hits a mob &7(such as a pig)&r and deals more than &e20% of its max health&r in one hit, the mob drops its corresponding loot &7(such as pork)&r."
		""
		"Then heal the mob back up with a &eHealing Potion&r, and you can squeeze drops out of it endlessly."
	]
	quest.7938030579EFD8D8.title: "F2.6 Anvil Snatch"
	quest.797DC5A4D7FF51C2.quest_desc: [
		"Can teleport you one-way to a Sharestone of the same color."
	]
	quest.797DC5A4D7FF51C2.title: "O1.6 Portstone"
	quest.79A52045816BD907.quest_desc: [
		"A utensil rack is perfect for your kitchen — grab your utensils whenever you need them."
		""
		"The recipe book can simplify cooking steps &7(see the item description for details)&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Fruit baskets and lunch baskets are both handy for storing lots of different foods. The difference:"
		""
		"The fruit basket must be placed on the ground. Right-click it while holding food to insert items; Shift+right-click to take items out."
		""
		"The lunch basket works from your backpack, like a storage bag — select an item with left-click, hover it over the basket, and right-click to put it in &7(or just right-click the item with the lunch basket)"
		""
		"When the lunch basket is closed, hold right-click with it in hand to switch the selected food; when open, hold right-click to eat the selected food. &7(Hold the lunch basket and left-click the air to toggle it open/closed)"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/ftbq_image/f3_5.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.79A52045816BD907.title: "F3.5 Practical Kitchenware (1)"
	quest.79BCF6FADBD1CE8E.quest_desc: [
		"Next up: Cogwheels. On top of the Shaft's basics, they add &ehorizontal power transfer&r."
		""
		"Just like real physics: a Large Cogwheel driving a small one doubles the speed, and vice versa halves it."
		""
		"Right-click with &eCasing&r to box in a Cogwheel and hide its Shaft. Use a &eWrench&r to expose the Shaft again, or remove the Casing."
		""
		"Some machines&7 (like the Millstone)&r contain Cogwheels inside and can act as gears too."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Speed Changes & Stress\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"112A60B1E4DAD6AD\" } }"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Large Cogwheels &ecan't&r connect to each other horizontally — you need a small Cogwheel between them."
		""
		"Since the &espeed cap is 256 RPM&r, any gear&7 (and Shaft)&r exceeding it gets destroyed on the spot. For diagonal stress transfer, use a Large Cogwheel as an &eidler&7 (the gear in the middle)&f, or just use the handier &eConveyor Belt&r."
	]
	quest.79BCF6FADBD1CE8E.quest_subtitle: "There's no number, and it's definitely not because I forgot"
	quest.79F73F15B08EC5D1.quest_desc: [
		"You'll often need to move physical structures while building. The most basic way is to &eattack&r the structure directly, or drag the &eIron Handle&r on it."
		""
		"But these methods can only move a limited amount of mass, so you may want some more advanced tools."
		""
		"&aTips&r: A &eDeployer&r processing Iron Blocks with &eTopaz&7 (consumed)&r / &eBlocks of Topaz&7 (not consumed)&r yields &eHollowed Blocks of Magnet&r."
	]
	quest.79F73F15B08EC5D1.title: "Debugging, Moving"
	quest.7A0C5244D1ABB4B9.quest_desc: [
		"Ever noticed you can place the backpack down? These two upgrades make the backpack much more convenient to use as a storage component."
	]
	quest.7A0C5244D1ABB4B9.title: "O2.25 Drop Your Backpack, Become a Warehouse"
	quest.7A2900B878E9889C.quest_desc: [
		"Can store 8.2k items."
		""
		"A random frequency is assigned when placed. You can use the &eLinking Tool&r to save and apply frequencies."
		""
		"Ender Drawers with the same frequency share their storage."
		""
		"&aTips&r: If a frequency is lost, the items are hard to recover, so it's not recommended to store valuables in them."
	]
	quest.7A2900B878E9889C.title: "3.9 Wireless Transmission"
	quest.7A5EDF15A6FFCA13.quest_desc: [
		"When struck by lightning, a Block of Experience turns into a Block of Super Experience, which is used to make the smithing template for Super Enchanting."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Right-clicking a Lightning Rod with &eTopaz&r can also call down lightning."
	]
	quest.7A5EDF15A6FFCA13.title: "E1.11 Super Enchanting Template"
	quest.7A7825991729C7EB.quest_desc: [
		"Whether you know redstone or not, collect plenty when you see it — you'll need it to make strawberry-flavored lollipops &7(Rose Quartz)"
	]
	quest.7A7825991729C7EB.title: "S1.3.3 Redstone, I Don’t Know How to Do It?"
	quest.7A7FAEAFA2CF05EE.quest_desc: [
		"Adjusting the cobblestone flow between quartz and diorite production is admittedly complicated and tedious."
		""
		"Why not use a &eFactory Gauge&r to handle the distribution automatically? Go try it!"
	]
	quest.7A7FAEAFA2CF05EE.title: "HS3.5.3 Automated Allocation"
	quest.7A83749D7279F353.quest_desc: [
		"Who doesn't want an airship, a plane, or a ship!"
		""
		"This section teaches you how to build an &eairship&r; for &eships&r, you'll need to apply what you learn."
		""
		"&eAircraft&r are a bit harder — they're mentioned here, but we recommend learning from the video below:"
		"{\"text\":\"Concise fixed-wing tutorial\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1xCo7BKEdg\"}}"
	]
	quest.7A83749D7279F353.title: "Aircraft/Ships"
	quest.7ADEAB99C8CE4802.quest_desc: [
		"&eCreate: Aeronautics&r is a new Create add-on that lets you build aircraft freely — so freely it's hard to know where to start."
		""
		"But no matter what you want to do, building a &ePhysical Assembler&r first is always right: it converts your creation into a &ephysical structure&r, which is how you go on to make planes, ships, cars..."
		""
		"After that, you can keep building directly on the physical structure."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Take good care of your cane — its recipe is expensive."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"This section is still just a categorized pile of info, because I'm a bit lost on how to write it more clearly."
		""
		"Maybe it'll become a hands-on quest, like building a ship together?"
		""
		"If you have suggestions, feel free to tell me."
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Comment under this video\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV165J56ZERr/\" } }"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Github Issue\",\"color\":\"blue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://github.com/MeadalFlute/Create-Plus-Aeronautics/issues\" } }"
	]
	quest.7ADEAB99C8CE4802.quest_subtitle: "Unfinished, unnumbered."
	quest.7ADEAB99C8CE4802.title: "Aeronautics"
	quest.7AF85362D35B6C8D.quest_desc: [
		"A Deployer using &eTopaz&7 (consumed)&r or a &eBlock of Topaz&7 (not consumed)&r can turn Blocks of Iron into Hollowed Blocks of Magnet."
	]
	quest.7B1C99709A83DCEA.quest_desc: [
		"Jade &7(Jade)&r helps you quickly identify mobs, blocks, and more &7(displayed at the top-center of the screen)&r — you can search further using the name and mod info it shows."
	]
	quest.7B1C99709A83DCEA.quest_subtitle: "What's that?"
	quest.7B1C99709A83DCEA.title: "What Is That Stuff?"
	quest.7B351A912F847C76.quest_desc: [
		"Used with connectors to connect remote containers to the storage network."
	]
	quest.7B351A912F847C76.title: "O4.12 Pull Network Cable"
	quest.7B3DC5DA1E2B6C12.quest_desc: [
		"AnvilCraft's Block Placer is cheap and easy to use — no electricity or stress needed — but it still can't replace the Deployer..."
		""
		"&aTips&r: See the tutorial book for details."
		""
		"&8...though Crab Claws really do blow the Deployer out of the water..."
	]
	quest.7B3DC5DA1E2B6C12.quest_subtitle: "Deployer: ?"
	quest.7B3DC5DA1E2B6C12.title: "AC1.3.2 Deployer Youth Edition"
	quest.7B4967505448D27D.quest_desc: [
		"When combining two Heavy Halberds, the result &einherits the enchantments of the ingredients&r, so you can use the weapon in your hand directly for crafting."
		""
		"The Heavy Halberd isn't just high-damage with a fast attack speed — it can also be used as a Trident and a heavy hammer."
		""
		"&8It can also chop vegetables."
	]
	quest.7B4967505448D27D.title: "AC1.21.11 Every Strike Burns, Every Strike Booms"
	quest.7B8601DCACCF5152.quest_desc: [
		"The gear block works like redstone dust, but it can be placed in mid-air, and you can even stick Redstone Torches directly onto it."
		""
		"With it, dealing with AnvilCraft will be a breeze (thumbs up)."
	]
	quest.7B8601DCACCF5152.title: "AC1.6.4 Floating Redstone Powder"
	quest.7BD8FD7FE0303EB9.title: "Gems"
	quest.7C164BA476E7CD5B.quest_desc: [
		"&eTime Warp&r meat and heads to obtain crude oil."
	]
	quest.7C164BA476E7CD5B.title: "AC1.18 Beware of Mold"
	quest.7C4308026EBF4714.quest_desc: [
		"Place a Chain Conveyor near the warehouse, slightly higher up, because Package Frogports can only interact with chains at or above their own height."
	]
	quest.7CB70812BFE011B6.quest_desc: [
		"Time Warp a Geode to get Budding Amethyst."
	]
	quest.7CB70812BFE011B6.title: "Time Warp"
	quest.7CBCEFD6188F3C75.quest_desc: [
		"This quest just lists them out — their item descriptions are already clear enough."
		""
		"One extra note on using the &eBlock Placer&r:"
		""
		"&eLeft-click&r to select a block, &eRight-click&r to place it, &eShift+Right-click&r to open the config panel."
	]
	quest.7CBCEFD6188F3C75.title: "S2.8.2 Messy Stuff"
	quest.7CDA849025C588AC.quest_desc: [
		"Put it on the &ePackager&r and build your logistics network!"
	]
	quest.7CDA849025C588AC.title: "3.9 Logistics Network"
	quest.7CF1AA66784FE146.quest_desc: [
		"If you're not into fighting, you can get Blaze Powder by smashing Blaze Burners..."
		""
		"&7But... it will curse you..."
		""
		"&7But is a curse necessarily a bad thing?"
	]
	quest.7CF1AA66784FE146.quest_subtitle: "Come to cheat, come to sneak attack"
	quest.7CF1AA66784FE146.title: "S2.2.3 Don’t Fight, Don’t Fight"
	quest.7D1FB9AC8C967828.quest_desc: [
		"Crush granite into red sand, then wash it to get Gold Nuggets."
	]
	quest.7D1FB9AC8C967828.title: "H3.7 One Step Away"
	quest.7D51D96006CB0199.quest_desc: [
		"Collect some materials for crafting Waystones."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Ender Pearls are now renewable!"
	]
	quest.7D51D96006CB0199.title: "O1.1 Raw Materials"
	quest.7D64DD2E8BCB540A.quest_desc: [
		"Time Warp a Netherite Crystal Nucleus to get Ancient Debris."
		""
		"Smelt it with a &eHeater&r — one Ancient Debris yields two Netherite Scraps."
	]
	quest.7D64DD2E8BCB540A.title: "Time Warp"
	quest.7DBF6F727C671718.quest_desc: [
		"Using a Redstone Contact with wireless redstone, you can set up automatic back-and-forth movement."
	]
	quest.7DBF6F727C671718.title: "H1.6 Automated Reverse"
	quest.7DE975B729E0C49E.quest_desc: [
		"Put your eloquence to work and convince the Blazes to work for you XD ("
	]
	quest.7DE975B729E0C49E.title: "1.10 Mom, Look, Blaze!"
	quest.7DF4BEFADBEB9ADF.quest_desc: [
		"It looks like you're heading to the Ancient City to pick a fight with the Warden."
		""
		"&aTips&r: AnvilCraft adds a renewable source of Echo Shards: mobs defeated by a Warden's &esonic boom&r&7 (a Snow Golem is recommended)&r will drop one extra Echo Shard."
	]
	quest.7DF4BEFADBEB9ADF.title: "AC1.21.8 Resonator Core"
	quest.7E272446BF72E20D.quest_desc: [
		"Although you could just park chickens on a Hopper to auto-collect eggs..."
		""
		"But surely you haven't sunk so low that you need to squeeze the in-game chickens either... right...?"
		""
		"Consider building a grand chicken farm &7(just to have something to do)&r to give your animal employees a nice workplace — later you can even let them drive trains."
		""
		"&7Besides chickens, how about considering the other animals too?"
	]
	quest.7E272446BF72E20D.title: "HS4.2.2 Treat Your Employees Humanely"
	quest.7E37D652F20B3E43.quest_desc: [
		"A Stack Upgrade that's easy to mass-produce — you'll use a lot of these."
	]
	quest.7E37D652F20B3E43.title: "O2.12 Used a Lot"
	quest.7E822A094AFA032E.quest_desc: [
		"At the Ember Smithing Table, use a Four to One Smithing Template and a Heavy Halberd Core to craft a Heavy Halberd."
		""
		"The Heavy Halberd isn't just high-damage with a fast attack speed — it can also be used as a Trident, a heavy hammer, and a &eknife&7 (kitchen knife)"
		""
		"&aTips&r: The &eEnd&r has many scattered trial chambers full of vaults."
		""
		"Tridents now have a crafting recipe, and vaults can be reopened again and again &7(place a lead block on the vault and smash it with a falling anvil to open it once more)&r."
	]
	quest.7E822A094AFA032E.quest_subtitle: "Thousand Mechanisms Umbrella!"
	quest.7E822A094AFA032E.title: "S2.17.7 Multi-Purpose Weapon"
	quest.7EC51B1111DC5998.quest_desc: [
		"The direction a crane structure moves depends on the rotation direction of the crane mast."
		""
		"A Gearshift reverses its rotation direction when it receives a redstone signal, letting the crane structure travel back and forth."
	]
	quest.7EC51B1111DC5998.title: "H1.5 Get Back Here!"
	quest.7ECC4D0574D29CF2.quest_desc: [
		"The Mechanical Bearing can split one physical structure into two."
		""
		"You can also prepare two physical structures in advance and use the &eDocking Connector&r or &eAdhesive&r to connect and detach them."
		""
		"Its most important trick, though, is pairing with the &eCopper Valve Wheel&r to &erotate a physical structure&r at any angle."
	]
	quest.7ECC4D0574D29CF2.title: "Split"
	quest.7F3FBAD2ADE01B06.quest_desc: [
		"Send the sorted wheat flour through batch washing to turn it into dough."
		""
		"&aTips&r: Waterlogged blocks work for batch washing too — waterlogged leaves are the handiest."
	]
	quest.7F3FBAD2ADE01B06.title: "H1.13 Bulk Washing"
	quest.7F45495C1C98D740.quest_desc: [
		"Using Tom's Simple Storage hoppers to feed stacked Crafters is also a good method."
		""
		"But I won't provide a tutorial for that here — if you want to do it, look it up on MC?? yourself."
	]
	quest.7F45495C1C98D740.title: "HS3.5.1 The Less Create-y Way"
